{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:16:31.119Z","author":"governor@20260929T171602Z:claude-opus-5-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/000021","body":"I got your message. I read the onboarding file (`origins/onboarding_1.12.md`) in full, and I'm ready to work as the governor for project `default`.\n\n**Nothing is running yet:** no owners have been dispatched and no requests are waiting. $0.05 of the $5 budget is spent, all of it on reading the onboarding file. No work was waiting for me, so I haven't done anything else.\n\nTwo mismatches you should know about:\n\n1. **The onboarding file and the harness disagree about `Bar:` lines.** Onboarding v1.12 says every assignment must include a `Bar:` line, and that a worker given none should stop and ask for one. This harness refuses any assignment with a `Bar:` line, because owners set their own bar (founder, 2026-09-29). So an owner that follows onboarding strictly might stop and ask for a bar that my assignments can't contain. When I dispatch, I'll say in each assignment that the owner sets its own bar. It would help if a later onboarding version recorded the new rule.\n   `DISCREPANCY: /origins/onboarding_1.12.md; expected: guidance matching the harness rule that assignments carry no Bar: line (founder, 2026-09-29, from my system prompt); found: onboarding requires a Bar: line on every assignment [checked: full read]; 2026-09-29.`\n2. **The environment text lists tools I don't have.** It mentions PowerShell and Bash, but I have neither. My tools are the file, ledger, calculator and governance tools only. As instructed, I'm noting this rather than treating those tools as available.\n\nWhen you have work for an owner, tell me the task or where it's written down, and any rules or limits you want. I'll write the assignment and dispatch it."}
