{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:19:23.810Z","author":"governor@20260929T171602Z:claude-opus-5-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/000153","body":"I've started both agents. They work in the background, and I'll pass on their results when their turns end.\n\n**The agents**\n\n| Agent | Model | Budget | Writes only to |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| owner.1 | claude-opus-5-5 | $1.50 | `work/doctrine-priorities/claude/` |\n| owner.2 | gpt-6-sol | $1.00 | `work/doctrine-priorities/gpt/` |\n\n- **Model choice:** I picked gpt-6-sol myself; I had no basis for choosing among the GPT models. Tell me if you want a different one.\n- **GPT budget:** a GPT agent's own model runs don't cost dollars. Its $1.00 only pays for any Claude subagents it starts.\n- **Total:** the two budgets add up to $2.50 of the $4.77 left.\n\n**Their instructions** (saved in the ledger as `gov/assignments/doctrine-priorities-claude` and `-gpt`)\n- **Task:** your request, word for word. Start at the mapping project's `MAP.md` or `CONTINUE.md`. Each agent decides what counts as doctrine, how to rank it and how deep to read, and explains its choices.\n- **No shared work:** each agent is told the other exists. The permissions I set stop each from reading the other's instructions, files or ledger entries, so you can compare the two answers afterwards (onboarding's \"blind parallel candidates\" method).\n- **What they deliver:** a written recommendation in their own folder. It should state its own standard of success at the top, mark which claims were checked and which are working estimates, say what it didn't look at, and record any mismatches it finds as `DISCREPANCY:` lines.\n- **Rules:**\n  - Read-only outside their own folder, and no git commands.\n  - They may not read `candidate_repos`.\n  - They can't run any code; my rules also tell them not to find ways around that.\n  - Before quoting any personal data, they must check with me.\n  - They can ask me for clarification, more access or more budget, and they may object if the task seems malformed.\n\n**Two things you should know**\n- **Folders:** I didn't create their folders in advance. I don't know whether writing a file creates its folder automatically. If it doesn't, an agent will probably tell me.\n- **What they can read:** each agent can read almost everything except `candidate_repos`, the harness records, and the other agent's folder, ledger entries and instructions. That includes anything I write in my own ledger area from now on. I'll keep anything about comparing the two out of my ledger area until both have finished."}
