{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:19:28.056Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/000189","body":{"kind":"message","agent":"owner.1","turn":1,"direction":"to_agent","message":{"_type":"UserMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolResultBlock","tool_use_id":"toolu_019P79XkLo8bKFs5X8cDjTKS","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E01_constitution_onboarding_virtues.md\",\n \"start_line\": 1,\n \"end_line\": 282,\n \"total_lines\": 282,\n \"next_offset\": null,\n \"line_truncated\": false,\n \"sha256\": \"fcfb4de03c115b03b0471d01efe8b51dbf5548479c1faddaf05d0199bb05f8d3\",\n \"text\": \"# E01 · Constitution, onboarding & virtue register\\n*Group A · state: doctrine frozen 2026-08-26; **`virtues.md` live to 09-16, 55% of it uncommitted** ·\\nactive 2026-08-10 → 2026-09-16 · written Wave 02 by `w02_doctrine_memory` (opus)*\\n\\n## 1. What it is\\n\\nNIMOI's statement of itself: what the institution is (`origins/NIMOI.md`), what it is for and the bar\\nits work is judged against (`origins/persistent_testbed.md`), the contract every session enters under\\n(ten `origins/onboarding_1.NN.md` versions, reached from root `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md`), and a running\\nregister of how far the agency is currently leaning from the mean on six named axes\\n(`origins/virtues.md`). It produced no tooling and no build step — **every file in it is hand-authored\\nprose.** It is under 1% of the project by bytes and is the only part every session is required to touch.\\n\\nThe effort is **bimodal and has been since 08-26.** The doctrine documents closed: the last onboarding\\nversion is 1.10 (08-26 23:05); `persistent_testbed.md` 08-23; `NIMOI.md` 08-11. The *instrument* did\\nnot: `virtues.md` took 37 new entries between 09-09 and 09-16, 33 of them written by Suite 4.1 runs in\\n`candidate_analysis/metrics/` (E19). That is the one live write path from the field spine into\\ndoctrine — and it is **leaky in both directions** (§8). A reader who stops here should know: the\\nconstitution this effort keeps promising was never written, and the register that is running instead\\nis unbounded, uncommitted, and fed by exactly one effort.\\n\\n## 2. Where it lives\\n\\n| Path | Role | Files | Git | Note |\\n|---|---|---:|---|---|\\n| `origins/` (top level) | **HOME** | 21 (223 KB) | 19 tracked, 2 untracked | Only 14 of the 21 are E01's; see \\\"Does NOT include\\\" |\\n| `origins/virtues.md` | HOME — the only live artifact | 1 (42,496 B) | tracked, **M**: +59 lines, 0 deletions | HEAD = 18,938 B / 171 lines; **23,558 B (55%) exists only in the working tree** |\\n| `origins/onboarding_1.01 … 1.10.md` | HOME — the entry contract | 10 (68 KB) | tracked, clean | 1.10 authoritative; history never edited |\\n| `origins/NIMOI.md`, `persistent_testbed.md`, `virtue_methodology.md`, `existing_content.md`, `gpt_first_impressions.md` | HOME — doctrine core | 5 | tracked, clean | `virtue_methodology.md` self-labelled **PRECURSOR** |\\n| root `CLAUDE.md` (209 B), `AGENTS.md` (256 B) | HOME — the pointer that makes the contract work | 2 | tracked | Each does one thing: read the highest-numbered `origins/onboarding_*.md` |\\n| root `README.md` (43 B) | HOME (nominal) | 1 | tracked | Two lines; carries no identity material |\\n| `context/eldest_observations.md`, `context/eldest_clarifications.md` | MATERIAL — lineage doctrine | 2 (13.9 KB) | tracked | The NIMOI↔ELDEST relationship; `NIMOI.md` cites `eldest_clarifications.md` by path. Shared with E07 |\\n| `context/author_observation_metacognition.md` | MATERIAL — founder names NIMOI's key capability | 1 (2,466 B) | tracked | 08-12 |\\n| `context/agent_introspection_session_satisfaction_2026-08-13.md` | MATERIAL — the primary record `debrief_001` is \\\"an account of\\\" | 1 (7,767 B) | tracked | Shared with E02 |\\n| `from_chat/gpt_primer_1.md` | MATERIAL — candidate conceptual ancestor | 1 | tracked | 08-09; never cited by any `context/` curator or by `NIMOI.md` |\\n| `ELDEST/` | MATERIAL — declared inheritance | 5 | 4 tracked, 1 untracked | E07's home; E01's lineage claim rests on it |\\n| `job/portfolio_v1/detail/deployed_onboarding_1.08.md` | **COPY-OF** `origins/onboarding_1.08.md` | 1 (8,213 B) | tracked | ✔ byte-identical (sha256 match). Evidentiary freeze — do not dedupe |\\n| `candidate_analysis/metrics/runs/*_suite4.1_run.md` + `suite4_state/**/_receipt_*.json` | **WRITES-INTO** `origins/virtues.md` | 16 files name it | 11 tracked / 5 untracked | 33 of the 37 new register entries; see §8 for the reconciliation gaps |\\n| `nimoi_design/comparison_synthesis_design_v1.0/_v1.1/_v1.3.md` | WRITES-INTO `virtues.md` | 3 | **untracked** | 3 entries, all `EXC-watch`, under V-1 and V-2 |\\n| `candidate_analysis/metrics/reports/suite41_vs_paper_20260916/SYNTHESIS.md` | WRITES-INTO `virtues.md` | 1 | untracked | 1 entry under V-3 (the 09-16 seven-subagent expenditure line) |\\n| `paper/ai_contacts/special_exchange_akashic_aurora_vandor_20260904_v1.md` | **READS-AND-CRITIQUES** `virtues.md` | 1 | untracked | One-way. The critique was never answered in the register — see §6 R25 |\\n| `.mcp.json`, `.claude/settings.local.json`, `.claude/launch.json`, `.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock` | CONFIG (not E01's, but the repo's entry surface) | 4 | 1 tracked; 2 ignored (`~/.config/git/ignore`, `.git/info/exclude`) | No hooks, no agents, no skills, no permissions block |\\n\\n**Does NOT include** — things inside `origins/` that belong to other efforts:\\n`origins/procedure_acquisition_history/` (16 files, **452,627 B = 67% of `origins/` by bytes**, E06);\\n`origins/debrief_001_*`, `degradation_001_*`, `mistakes_001_*` (E02);\\n`origins/peer_learning_primer_v1.md` + `social_ai_and_institutional_alignment_primer_v1.md` (E22/E23 —\\nboth **untracked**, both consumed only from `story/` and `paper/organizations/`).\\nAlso **not** E01: the 508 sandbox files under `campaigns/…/sandbox/**/lib/**/origins/` (fixture copies\\nof `NIMOI.md`, `debrief_001`, `onboarding_1.03`, plus a synthetic `onboarding_note_sandbox.md`) — they\\nare E06's frozen test inputs and they poison every glob on `origins/`.\\n\\n## 3. How it works\\n\\n**The entry contract, in three hops.** Root `CLAUDE.md` (Claude) / `AGENTS.md` (GPT) → \\\"read the\\n**latest** `origins/onboarding_*.md`\\\" → `onboarding_1.10.md`. `AGENTS.md` additionally states the\\nzero-padding rule so \\\"lexically highest\\\" is unambiguous. Nothing else is required reading. **The\\nwhole institution hangs off one filename-ordering convention.**\\n\\n**What 1.10 puts in the hot path** (mechanical keyword census across all ten versions):\\n\\n| appears in | 1.01 | 1.02 | 1.03 | 1.04 | 1.05 | 1.06 | 1.07 | 1.08 | 1.09 | 1.10 |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `virtues.md` | | ● | ● | ● | ● | ● | ● | ● | ● | ● |\\n| `persistent_testbed.md` | | | | | | ● | ● | ● | ● | ● |\\n| Hail-Mary override clause | | | | ● | | | | | | |\\n| `procedures/INDEX.md` | | | | | | | | ● | ● | ● |\\n| failure record (E02) | | | | | | | | | ● | |\\n| `harvest/candidate_gold/`, `candidate_repos/` | | | | | | | | | | ● |\\n| `general_findings/` (E03) | | | | | | | | | | |\\n\\n**`general_findings/` is named in none of the ten versions.** `campaigns/`, `candidate_analysis/`,\\n`nlt_ledger/`, `paper/`, `job/` are named in none either. 1.10's directory outline names 7 locations\\nout of 23 visible top-level directories (`story/`, `procedures/`, `context/`, `from_chat/`, `ELDEST/`,\\n`harvest/candidate_gold/`, `origins/`) — ✔ confirming `spaghetti.md` S12.\\n\\n**The register's mechanism.** `virtues.md` is append-only (\\\"the second sanctioned exception to\\nversions-over-edits\\\"). The unit is the **axis**, not the finding: six axes (V-1 Assurance, V-2\\nSufficiency, V-3 Expenditure, V-4 Insistence, V-5 Self-report, V-6 Correction response), each with\\nboth vices, a `Lean` judgement and a forward-looking `Watch` line. Entries are one-line, prefixed with\\na `MM-DD` tag and a verdict token (`held`, `DEF`, `EXC`, `DEF-arrested`, `EXC-watch`), and end with a\\nbacktick path. Reading rule, stated in-file: \\\"read the last three entries of an axis, then the `Watch`\\nline.\\\"\\n\\n**Entry census (whole file, 83 entries):** V-1 32 · V-2 9 · V-3 8 · V-4 5 · V-5 26 · V-6 3.\\n**Of the 37 uncommitted entries: V-1 16, V-2 2, V-3 1, V-5 18, V-4 0, V-6 0.** The two axes about\\n*insisting on the process* and *taking a correction* have received nothing since 08-23.\\n\\n**Who writes.** The committed half (46 entries, 08-13 → 08-23) was written by the procedure-acquisition\\ncampaign (E06/E05) and cites its decision log (`D-036`, `D-040`, `D-043`, `D-045`, `D-051`, `D-054`,\\n`D-069`) and review packages. The uncommitted half (37 entries, 09-09 → 09-16) is written by E19 (33),\\nE08 (3) and E21's inquiry (1). **No campaign entry and no field entry share an axis convention author;\\nthe file is one artifact with two régimes 17 days apart.**\\n\\n**Entry points, in order, for a newcomer:** root `CLAUDE.md` → `origins/onboarding_1.10.md` →\\n`origins/persistent_testbed.md` (the bar) → `origins/virtues.md` (`How to read this register`, line\\n218) → `origins/NIMOI.md` (reference, explicitly not required) → `origins/virtue_methodology.md`\\n(PRECURSOR — says a constitution supersedes it).\\n\\n## 4. Timeline\\n\\n| Date (2026) | Event | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 08-10 | Founder names NIMOI | `origins/NIMOI.md` (\\\"Named: 2026-08-10\\\") |\\n| 08-11 08:37 / 08:55 | `onboarding_1.01`; `NIMOI.md` | mtimes |\\n| 08-16 07:36 | `README.md`; first commit `e8fbca6` | mtime; `git log` |\\n| 08-17 15:37 | Root `CLAUDE.md` | mtime |\\n| 08-17 17:24 | `virtue_methodology.md` + `onboarding_1.02` written together; **register opened** | identical mtimes; first `virtues.md` date tag is `08-13` (back-dated) |\\n| 08-13 → 08-23 | 46 register entries, all campaign-fed | date-tag histogram: 08-13×3, 08-15×6, 08-16×15, 08-17×6, 08-22×11, 08-23×5 |\\n| 08-21 20:38 / 20:43 / 20:58 | `AGENTS.md` (GPT joins); `gpt_first_impressions.md`; `onboarding_1.03` | mtimes |\\n| 08-22 22:16 → 08-23 06:08 | `onboarding_1.04` adds a policy-override clause for `processes/hail_mary_protocol.md`; `1.05` removes it. **~8 hours in the hot path** | `difflib` 1.03→1.04→1.05 |\\n| 08-23 06:45 → 19:18 | `persistent_testbed.md`; `1.06` (the bar enters the hot path); `existing_content.md`; `1.07` (Python standard); `1.08` (`procedures/INDEX.md` mandatory) | mtimes; `difflib` |\\n| 08-26 22:42 | `onboarding_1.09` — **one hunk**: the failure-record bullet added to `origins/` | `difflib` 1.08→1.09 |\\n| 08-26 23:05 | `onboarding_1.10` — **one hunk**: that bullet deleted, `harvest/candidate_gold/` inserted, `origins/` bullet shortened. Net +132 B | `difflib` 1.09→1.10 |\\n| 08-31 | Last commit touching `origins/` (`52a4f10`) | `git log -- origins/` |\\n| 09-03 | Last commit anywhere (`a5c9470`); **everything below is uncommitted** | `git log` |\\n| 09-04 22:13 | `peer_learning_primer_v1.md` (untracked; E22 material) | mtime |\\n| 09-04 | Akashic-Aurora/Vandor raise a V-1/V-3 double-counting flaw in the register | `paper/ai_contacts/special_exchange_akashic_aurora_vandor_20260904_v1.md` |\\n| 09-09 → 09-16 | 37 entries appended: 33 Suite 4.1 (17 distinct runs), 3 `nimoi_design`, 1 inquiry-expenditure | `git diff -U0 -- origins/virtues.md` |\\n| 09-14 13:10 | `social_ai_and_institutional_alignment_primer_v1.md` (untracked; E23 material) | mtime |\\n| 09-16 13:25 | Last write: `virtues.md` (arc-gasp V-1/V-5 pair + the seven-subagent V-3 line) | mtime |\\n\\n## 5. State and unfinished business\\n\\n- **Exact stopping point.** `origins/virtues.md`, 09-16 13:25, 230 lines. The last entries are the\\n  arc-gasp Suite 4.1 pair (V-1, V-5) and the 09-16 inquiry expenditure line (V-3).\\n- **A constitution is owed and unwritten.** `virtue_methodology.md` is self-labelled PRECURSOR —\\n  \\\"when a constitution exists it supersedes this file\\\" — and defers six questions to it. `NIMOI.md`\\n  lists three ELDEST constitutional principles as *candidates*. Nothing named `constitution` exists.\\n- **The register has no rotation or re-basing rule.** V-1 alone carries 32 entries, 16 of them\\n  near-identical Suite 4.1 lines. Re-basing is listed as an open question by the methodology file.\\n- **Two axes are starved.** V-4 (5 entries, none since 08-23) and V-6 (3 entries, none since 08-23).\\n  The two-line rule mechanically routes every field run to V-1 and V-5 only.\\n- **The 09-04 peer critique is unanswered.** The exchange record itself says so: \\\"No subsequent NIMOI\\n  response, resolution of the coupling question, or continuing dialogue is documented here.\\\"\\n- **Stalled on the founder:** whether the constitution is written, whether the register re-bases,\\n  whether the two primers stay in `origins/`.\\n\\n## 6. Relationships\\n\\n| R | Other effort | Kind | What exactly | Verified? |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **R24** | E19 → E01 | writes-into | **Qualified, not refuted.** 33 of 37 new entries are Suite 4.1 output. But only **17 of 31 Suite 4.1 run records on disk produced an entry (55%)**, and only **11 run records name `virtues.md` in their own Artifacts block**. Not \\\"every completed run\\\". *(W03 consistency, 2026-09-20: \\\"31\\\" is a **filename** count — six Suite 4.1 run records carry `_suite4_run.md` names because the dispatch prescribes it (H31). By receipts there are **37 completed** Suite 4.1 runs: **17 of 37** wrote — all 16 fires of the scheduled loop + the interactive `ruvnet-brain` run. This effort's wave report also said \\\"4 loop-window runs appended none\\\": ✗ — those four were interactive runs *before* the loop's first fire (09-10 22:48Z) — `w02_emi_measurement`, settled by the Wave 02 integrator (U4); ✔ `w03_audit_attack` A9. The integrated row is `relationships/effort_graph.md` R24; the same \\\"17 of 31\\\" stands in §10.)* | ✗/◐ — recounted both directions |\\n| **R25** | E22 → E01 | writes-into | **REFUTED.** `paper/ai_contacts/special_exchange_…_v1.md` reads and criticises the register; `virtues.md` contains **no entry citing it, no `09-04` date tag, and the strings `ai_contacts` and `paper/` appear zero times in the file**. Correct kind: **cited-by (one-way)**, with an open, unanswered critique. Doctrine was not changed by external contact. | ✗ — grep + date histogram |\\n| **R30** | E07 ↔ E01 | lineage | Holds. `NIMOI.md` cites `../ELDEST/` and `../context/eldest_clarifications.md` by path; both resolve. `ELDEST/` is 4 tracked + 1 untracked file. | ✔ |\\n| **R02/R06** | E06, E05 → E01 | produced | The committed 46 register entries, `persistent_testbed.md` (occasioned by the Phase-5 AR), `existing_content.md` (the waiver ruling ordered by the AR chair), and onboarding 1.04/1.05 (the Hail Mary override) are all campaign output filed as doctrine. | ✔ |\\n| **R05** | E01 → E24 | copies (frozen evidence) | `job/portfolio_v1/detail/deployed_onboarding_1.08.md` is **byte-identical** to `origins/onboarding_1.08.md` (sha256, 8,213 B both). A deliberate freeze of the deployment-era entry contract. | ✔ — hashed |\\n| **R37** | E08 → E01 | writes-into | `nimoi_design/comparison_synthesis_design_v1.0/_v1.1/_v1.3.md` produced 3 register entries (V-1 ×1, V-2 ×2), all `EXC-watch`. E08 is **entirely untracked**; three doctrine lines therefore depend on untracked files. | ✔ — diff hunks 2 and 3 |\\n| **R38** | E21 → E01 | writes-into | The 09-16 paper inquiry wrote the single V-3 expenditure entry, citing `…/suite41_vs_paper_20260916/SYNTHESIS.md` §8. | ✔ — traced |\\n| **R39** | E01 → E02 | contains-but-disowns | E02's three records sit at the top of `origins/` and are E01's neighbours in every listing, but no E01 document points at them after `onboarding_1.09` was superseded 23 minutes later. | ✔ — `difflib` |\\n\\n## 7. Re-org notes\\n\\n**7a · Must move together.** `origins/{NIMOI, persistent_testbed, virtue_methodology, virtues,\\nexisting_content, gpt_first_impressions}.md` + all ten `onboarding_1.NN.md` + root `CLAUDE.md` and\\n`AGENTS.md`. The two root files are *pointers with a relative path*; moving `origins/` without editing\\nthem silently breaks the entry contract of the whole repository. `context/eldest_*` and `ELDEST/`\\nshould move with, or be linked from, whatever holds `NIMOI.md` (it cites them by relative path).\\n\\n**7b · Must not be deleted / deduplicated / renamed.**\\n- All ten onboarding versions. The zero-padding rule is *load-bearing*: \\\"read the latest\\\" is\\n  implemented as lexical max. Renaming one (e.g. to `1.9`) breaks the contract for every session.\\n- `job/portfolio_v1/detail/deployed_onboarding_1.08.md` — byte-identical by design (E24 freeze).\\n- `origins/virtues.md` — **commit before moving.** 55% of it by bytes exists only in the working tree.\\n- `origins/existing_content.md` — least self-describing filename in the project: its title is \\\"Rules\\n  meet content that predates them\\\"; its subject is the 1,200-token waiver list. Re-filing by filename\\n  will mis-file it.\\n- `origins/gpt_first_impressions.md` — **zero inbound citations anywhere** (✔ re-confirmed). Looks\\n  deletable; it is the only record of the first GPT session's view of joining a Claude-built institution.\\n\\n**7c · Regenerable or re-fetchable bulk.** None. E01 has no generated artifact, no build step, no\\ndownloaded content. Everything is hand-authored and irreplaceable.\\n\\n**7d · Hard-wired paths.** Root `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` → `origins/onboarding_*.md` (glob, relative).\\n`NIMOI.md` → `../ELDEST/`, `../context/eldest_clarifications.md`, `../procedures/monthly_peer_drafting.md`.\\n`virtue_methodology.md` → `origins/NIMOI.md`, `origins/onboarding_1.02.md`, `origins/virtues.md`.\\n`persistent_testbed.md` → `campaigns/procedure_acquisition`, `procedures/harvest_stabilization_papers.md`.\\n**Inbound**: 52 non-sandbox files cite `virtues.md` by path; 24 cite `persistent_testbed.md`; 26 cite\\n`NIMOI.md`. Every Suite 4.1 `_receipt_final.json` carries the literal string\\n`\\\"one line each under V-1 and V-5 in origins/virtues.md\\\"` — a path embedded in machine records.\\n*(W03, 2026-09-20: ✗ \\\"every\\\" — of the 38 `_final` receipts **one** carries the literal path\\n(`anupamme-neo`), 13 more mention the register in words only, 24 not at all; **15** files under\\n`candidate_analysis/metrics/` carry the path (11 run records, one `_final` and one `_findings` receipt,\\ntheir 2 state twins) — not the \\\"16\\\" of §2 and §7f. And no tracked file *prescribes* the write: the\\nSuite 4.1 dispatch never mentions the register; the instruction lives in the scheduled-task prompt,\\noutside both repositories — so moving the register would break little mechanically, and nothing in\\neither repository could be edited to tell the loop where it went — `w03_subprojects_b`, ✔\\n`w03_merge_subprojects` F4–F5; `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` H47, H78. This was the false reason\\nthe Wave 03 merge directive gave under M5; the ruling it supported stands on its other reasons.)*\\n\\n**7e · Misfiled material.** *Of this effort, living elsewhere:* the ELDEST-relationship doctrine\\n(`context/eldest_observations.md`, `eldest_clarifications.md`) and the metacognition observation\\n(`context/author_observation_metacognition.md`). *Of other efforts, living here:*\\n`origins/procedure_acquisition_history/` (**67% of `origins/` by bytes**, zero inbound citations from\\noutside itself — ✔ re-confirmed; E06), the two primers (E22/E23), and E02's three records.\\n\\n**7f · Natural seams.** E01 could stand alone as a small `constitution/` or `institution/` unit — it\\nis 223 KB of prose with no code and no data. It would have to carry: the ten onboarding versions, the\\nfive doctrine files, both root pointers (rewritten), `ELDEST/` or a stable link to it, and the four\\n`context/` doctrine files. **What blocks a clean cut is the register**: `virtues.md` is simultaneously\\ndoctrine and the output buffer of E19's run loop, and 16 files in `candidate_analysis/metrics/` embed\\nits path. Either the register moves and E19's dispatch documents, receipts and derived tools are\\nedited, or the register stays where E19 can find it. That is a founder decision, not a filing one.\\n\\n## 8. Record-integrity defects found\\n\\n1. **The register does not reconcile with the runs, in both directions.**\\n   - 31 Suite 4.1 run records exist on disk; **17** are cited by `virtues.md`. The 14 with no entry\\n     include four inside the live loop window: `20260909-0115_npc-ai-stack`, `20260910-2013_seas`,\\n     `20260910-2013_waooaw-platform`, `20260910-2101_hal9001`.\\n   - **11** run records name `virtues.md` in their own Artifacts block. The last three runs\\n     (`motor-evolutivo`, `hermes-society`, `arc-gasp`, all 09-13) **do not**, although the register\\n     holds entries citing them. The artifact-bullet convention lapsed while the register kept filling.\\n   - This refutes `w01_candidate_metrics` §6's \\\"identical wording in the 10 most recent run records\\\"\\n     and its \\\"each completed run nominates exactly two doctrine lines\\\".\\n   *Command:* regex `candidate_analysis/metrics/runs/([0-9]{8}-[0-9]{4}_[^/`]+)\\\\.md` over `virtues.md`\\n   vs `os.listdir` of `runs/` and a substring test for `virtues.md` in each run record.\\n2. **The two-line rule has two exceptions, neither flagged.** `introspection-self-improver` wrote\\n   **two** V-5 entries and **no** V-1 entry; `dot.brain` wrote a V-5 entry and no V-1 entry. 15 of 17\\n   runs kept the rule. *(Diff hunk 1 = 15 V-1 lines; hunk 5 = 18 V-5 lines.)*\\n3. **`w01_core_identity` §1's byte figures are wrong and internally inconsistent.** It reports\\n   `origins/*.md` top level = \\\"340 KB\\\" and `procedure_acquisition_history/` = \\\"336 KB\\\"; measured,\\n   **223 KB and 442 KB**. Its own §3.1 per-file table sums to ~218 KB, contradicting its §1. The\\n   consequence: §7.7's \\\"~50% of `origins/` by bytes\\\" is actually **67%**.\\n4. **`w01_core_identity` §6 IN-table is wrong about `mistakes_001`** (\\\"zero inbound citations\\\"): there\\n   is one, and it is load-bearing — `harvest/candidate_gold/inventory/INVENTORY.md`: \\\"This pass was\\n   run under the mistakes_001 corrections: absolute output paths in every…\\\". The failure record\\n   demonstrably changed a later run.\\n5. **`virtues.md` back-dates its own opening.** The file was created 08-17 17:24 (mtime, identical to\\n   `onboarding_1.02`) but its earliest entries carry `08-13`, `08-15`, `08-16` tags. Reconstruction,\\n   not contemporaneous record. Not a defect in itself — but the register is elsewhere treated as a\\n   dated log, and a re-org that sorts by tag will mis-order its first 24 entries.\\n6. **All 25 distinct paths cited in `virtues.md` resolve** (✔ checked with `os.path.exists`). The\\n   register's link hygiene is clean; the defect is in what it omits, not in what it names.\\n\\n## 9. Open questions\\n\\n1. **Is the constitution owed, and who writes it?** Two doctrine files point at an artifact that was\\n   never written. **A re-org should not create a `constitution/` slot without a founder ruling.**\\n2. **Does `virtues.md` move with the doctrine or stay with the instrument?** It is the only file that\\n   both spines touch, and 16 machine records embed its path (§7d). Founder only.\\n3. **Does the register re-base per campaign?** `virtue_methodology.md` §6 lists this open; V-1 is at\\n   32 entries with no rotation rule and the file has doubled in six weeks.\\n4. **Why did four Suite 4.1 runs (09-09/09-10) write no register lines?** Deliberate (the register was\\n   reopened at ruvnet-brain, 09-10 19:30) or missed? The four runs' records do not say.\\n   *(W03 consistency, 2026-09-20: **premise refuted, so not a founder question — see\\n   `relationships/effort_graph.md` R24.** Those four (`npc-ai-stack`, `seas`, `waooaw-platform`,\\n   `hal9001`) were **interactive** runs before the scheduled loop's first fire at 09-10 22:48Z; every\\n   one of the loop's 16 fires wrote. Relevant, not proven to be the cause: no tracked file prescribes\\n   the write — the instruction lives in the scheduled-task prompt, outside both repositories (H78) —\\n   `w02_emi_measurement`; `w03_founder_questions`; `w03_subprojects_b`.)*\\n5. **Should V-4 and V-6 be fed, or are they closed?** Nothing has touched them since 08-23, and the\\n   field spine's two-line rule cannot reach them.\\n6. **Was the 09-04 V-1/V-3 coupling critique rejected or dropped?** No artifact records a decision.\\n7. **Do the two primers leave `origins/`?** If they move, relative links in\\n   `story/corporate_adoption_note_2026-09-04_gpt6.md` and\\n   `paper/organizations/ai_institutions_reciprocal_report_gpt_v1.md` break.\\n\\n## 10. Verification ledger\\n\\n| Claim | Source | Status | How checked |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `virtues.md` has 59 uncommitted appended lines, 09-09 → 09-16 | `w01_core_identity` §3.1, §5 | **✔** | `git diff --stat` = 59 insertions, 0 deletions; date tags 09-09…09-16 |\\n| Those lines are \\\"16 Suite 4.1 loop fires, 3 `nimoi_design`, 1 expenditure\\\" | `w01_core_identity` §5 | **✗** | 59 lines = **37 entries**: 33 Suite 4.1 lines over **17 distinct runs** (V-1 ×15, V-5 ×18), 3 `nimoi_design`, 1 expenditure |\\n| Five sampled register lines trace to their run records | assigned | **✔** | ruvnet-brain→D17; openmt→D12; agentquant→D11 (\\\"15 superseding findings…10 unnecessary\\\"); arc-gasp→D4; 09-16 line→`SYNTHESIS.md` §8 (\\\"thirteen near-duplicate…81 KB\\\"). All five match in substance and number |\\n| Onboarding 1.09 added the failure-record pointer; 1.10 removed it | `w01_core_identity` §7.2 | **✔** | `difflib` 1.08→1.09 (one hunk, +6 lines) and 1.09→1.10 (one hunk, −6/+8). 22 min 42 s apart by mtime |\\n| 1.10's outline names 7 of 23 top-level directories | `spaghetti.md` S12 | **✔** | Read the section; exactly 7 bullets |\\n| Both primers untracked, not ignored | `w01_core_identity` §7.8 | **✔** | `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` lists both; `git check-ignore -v` exits 1 |\\n| \\\"Half of `virtues.md`\\\" is uncommitted | `git_state.md` | **✔** | HEAD 18,938 B / worktree 42,496 B → **55.4% by bytes** (25.7% by lines, 44.6% by entries) |\\n| `origins/` = 35 tracked, 1 modified, 2 untracked | `git_state.md` | **✔** | `git ls-files` / `status --porcelain` |\\n| R24 \\\"every completed Suite 4.1 run appends two lines\\\" | `effort_graph.md` R24 | **✗** | 17 of 31 runs; 2 of 17 broke the two-axis rule |\\n| R25 \\\"one AI exchange was recorded in the virtue register — the only case of external contact changing doctrine\\\" | `effort_graph.md` R25 | **✗** | `virtues.md` contains no `09-04` tag and zero occurrences of `ai_contacts` or `paper/`; the exchange record states no response was made |\\n| `gpt_first_impressions.md` and `procedure_acquisition_history/` have zero inbound citations | `w01_core_identity` §6 | **✔** | Substring scan of 9,787 in-scope files (tracked + untracked, `candidate_repos/` and the mapping project excluded) |\\n| `mistakes_001` has zero inbound citations | `w01_core_identity` §6 | **✗** | One: `harvest/candidate_gold/inventory/INVENTORY.md` |\\n| `origins/procedure_acquisition_history/` ≈ 50% of `origins/` by bytes | `w01_core_identity` §7.7 | **✗** | 452,627 of 675,603 B = **67%** |\\n| `.claude/` holds 3 files; 2 excluded locally; no hooks/agents/skills/permissions | `w01_core_identity` §3.3 | **✔** | `os.listdir` + `git check-ignore -v` (`~/.config/git/ignore` line 1; `.git/info/exclude` line 8) |\\n| 508 sandbox fixture files under nested `…/origins/` | `w01_core_identity` §7.1 | **○** | Not recounted; a filesystem walk confirmed the sandbox holds 446 date-named `.md` look-alikes against 1 real one, which independently demonstrates the glob hazard |\\n\\n**Not looked at:** the contents of the 16 `procedure_acquisition_history/` episodes (E06's); the body\\ntext of the two primers beyond their citation graph (E22/E23's); `ELDEST/eldest_design.md` (31.7 KB,\\nE07's); the 46 committed register entries' individual campaign sources (E05/E06's decision log);\\n`candidate_repos/` (prohibited, never touched).\"\n}"}],"is_error":null}],"uuid":"b67d66da-7ef3-4a3c-b256-87a306c8a45c","parent_tool_use_id":null,"tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E01_constitution_onboarding_virtues.md\",\n \"start_line\": 1,\n \"end_line\": 282,\n \"total_lines\": 282,\n \"next_offset\": null,\n \"line_truncated\": false,\n \"sha256\": \"fcfb4de03c115b03b0471d01efe8b51dbf5548479c1faddaf05d0199bb05f8d3\",\n \"text\": \"# E01 · Constitution, onboarding & virtue register\\n*Group A · state: doctrine frozen 2026-08-26; **`virtues.md` live to 09-16, 55% of it uncommitted** ·\\nactive 2026-08-10 → 2026-09-16 · written Wave 02 by `w02_doctrine_memory` (opus)*\\n\\n## 1. What it is\\n\\nNIMOI's statement of itself: what the institution is (`origins/NIMOI.md`), what it is for and the bar\\nits work is judged against (`origins/persistent_testbed.md`), the contract every session enters under\\n(ten `origins/onboarding_1.NN.md` versions, reached from root `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md`), and a running\\nregister of how far the agency is currently leaning from the mean on six named axes\\n(`origins/virtues.md`). It produced no tooling and no build step — **every file in it is hand-authored\\nprose.** It is under 1% of the project by bytes and is the only part every session is required to touch.\\n\\nThe effort is **bimodal and has been since 08-26.** The doctrine documents closed: the last onboarding\\nversion is 1.10 (08-26 23:05); `persistent_testbed.md` 08-23; `NIMOI.md` 08-11. The *instrument* did\\nnot: `virtues.md` took 37 new entries between 09-09 and 09-16, 33 of them written by Suite 4.1 runs in\\n`candidate_analysis/metrics/` (E19). That is the one live write path from the field spine into\\ndoctrine — and it is **leaky in both directions** (§8). A reader who stops here should know: the\\nconstitution this effort keeps promising was never written, and the register that is running instead\\nis unbounded, uncommitted, and fed by exactly one effort.\\n\\n## 2. Where it lives\\n\\n| Path | Role | Files | Git | Note |\\n|---|---|---:|---|---|\\n| `origins/` (top level) | **HOME** | 21 (223 KB) | 19 tracked, 2 untracked | Only 14 of the 21 are E01's; see \\\"Does NOT include\\\" |\\n| `origins/virtues.md` | HOME — the only live artifact | 1 (42,496 B) | tracked, **M**: +59 lines, 0 deletions | HEAD = 18,938 B / 171 lines; **23,558 B (55%) exists only in the working tree** |\\n| `origins/onboarding_1.01 … 1.10.md` | HOME — the entry contract | 10 (68 KB) | tracked, clean | 1.10 authoritative; history never edited |\\n| `origins/NIMOI.md`, `persistent_testbed.md`, `virtue_methodology.md`, `existing_content.md`, `gpt_first_impressions.md` | HOME — doctrine core | 5 | tracked, clean | `virtue_methodology.md` self-labelled **PRECURSOR** |\\n| root `CLAUDE.md` (209 B), `AGENTS.md` (256 B) | HOME — the pointer that makes the contract work | 2 | tracked | Each does one thing: read the highest-numbered `origins/onboarding_*.md` |\\n| root `README.md` (43 B) | HOME (nominal) | 1 | tracked | Two lines; carries no identity material |\\n| `context/eldest_observations.md`, `context/eldest_clarifications.md` | MATERIAL — lineage doctrine | 2 (13.9 KB) | tracked | The NIMOI↔ELDEST relationship; `NIMOI.md` cites `eldest_clarifications.md` by path. Shared with E07 |\\n| `context/author_observation_metacognition.md` | MATERIAL — founder names NIMOI's key capability | 1 (2,466 B) | tracked | 08-12 |\\n| `context/agent_introspection_session_satisfaction_2026-08-13.md` | MATERIAL — the primary record `debrief_001` is \\\"an account of\\\" | 1 (7,767 B) | tracked | Shared with E02 |\\n| `from_chat/gpt_primer_1.md` | MATERIAL — candidate conceptual ancestor | 1 | tracked | 08-09; never cited by any `context/` curator or by `NIMOI.md` |\\n| `ELDEST/` | MATERIAL — declared inheritance | 5 | 4 tracked, 1 untracked | E07's home; E01's lineage claim rests on it |\\n| `job/portfolio_v1/detail/deployed_onboarding_1.08.md` | **COPY-OF** `origins/onboarding_1.08.md` | 1 (8,213 B) | tracked | ✔ byte-identical (sha256 match). Evidentiary freeze — do not dedupe |\\n| `candidate_analysis/metrics/runs/*_suite4.1_run.md` + `suite4_state/**/_receipt_*.json` | **WRITES-INTO** `origins/virtues.md` | 16 files name it | 11 tracked / 5 untracked | 33 of the 37 new register entries; see §8 for the reconciliation gaps |\\n| `nimoi_design/comparison_synthesis_design_v1.0/_v1.1/_v1.3.md` | WRITES-INTO `virtues.md` | 3 | **untracked** | 3 entries, all `EXC-watch`, under V-1 and V-2 |\\n| `candidate_analysis/metrics/reports/suite41_vs_paper_20260916/SYNTHESIS.md` | WRITES-INTO `virtues.md` | 1 | untracked | 1 entry under V-3 (the 09-16 seven-subagent expenditure line) |\\n| `paper/ai_contacts/special_exchange_akashic_aurora_vandor_20260904_v1.md` | **READS-AND-CRITIQUES** `virtues.md` | 1 | untracked | One-way. The critique was never answered in the register — see §6 R25 |\\n| `.mcp.json`, `.claude/settings.local.json`, `.claude/launch.json`, `.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock` | CONFIG (not E01's, but the repo's entry surface) | 4 | 1 tracked; 2 ignored (`~/.config/git/ignore`, `.git/info/exclude`) | No hooks, no agents, no skills, no permissions block |\\n\\n**Does NOT include** — things inside `origins/` that belong to other efforts:\\n`origins/procedure_acquisition_history/` (16 files, **452,627 B = 67% of `origins/` by bytes**, E06);\\n`origins/debrief_001_*`, `degradation_001_*`, `mistakes_001_*` (E02);\\n`origins/peer_learning_primer_v1.md` + `social_ai_and_institutional_alignment_primer_v1.md` (E22/E23 —\\nboth **untracked**, both consumed only from `story/` and `paper/organizations/`).\\nAlso **not** E01: the 508 sandbox files under `campaigns/…/sandbox/**/lib/**/origins/` (fixture copies\\nof `NIMOI.md`, `debrief_001`, `onboarding_1.03`, plus a synthetic `onboarding_note_sandbox.md`) — they\\nare E06's frozen test inputs and they poison every glob on `origins/`.\\n\\n## 3. How it works\\n\\n**The entry contract, in three hops.** Root `CLAUDE.md` (Claude) / `AGENTS.md` (GPT) → \\\"read the\\n**latest** `origins/onboarding_*.md`\\\" → `onboarding_1.10.md`. `AGENTS.md` additionally states the\\nzero-padding rule so \\\"lexically highest\\\" is unambiguous. Nothing else is required reading. **The\\nwhole institution hangs off one filename-ordering convention.**\\n\\n**What 1.10 puts in the hot path** (mechanical keyword census across all ten versions):\\n\\n| appears in | 1.01 | 1.02 | 1.03 | 1.04 | 1.05 | 1.06 | 1.07 | 1.08 | 1.09 | 1.10 |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `virtues.md` | | ● | ● | ● | ● | ● | ● | ● | ● | ● |\\n| `persistent_testbed.md` | | | | | | ● | ● | ● | ● | ● |\\n| Hail-Mary override clause | | | | ● | | | | | | |\\n| `procedures/INDEX.md` | | | | | | | | ● | ● | ● |\\n| failure record (E02) | | | | | | | | | ● | |\\n| `harvest/candidate_gold/`, `candidate_repos/` | | | | | | | | | | ● |\\n| `general_findings/` (E03) | | | | | | | | | | |\\n\\n**`general_findings/` is named in none of the ten versions.** `campaigns/`, `candidate_analysis/`,\\n`nlt_ledger/`, `paper/`, `job/` are named in none either. 1.10's directory outline names 7 locations\\nout of 23 visible top-level directories (`story/`, `procedures/`, `context/`, `from_chat/`, `ELDEST/`,\\n`harvest/candidate_gold/`, `origins/`) — ✔ confirming `spaghetti.md` S12.\\n\\n**The register's mechanism.** `virtues.md` is append-only (\\\"the second sanctioned exception to\\nversions-over-edits\\\"). The unit is the **axis**, not the finding: six axes (V-1 Assurance, V-2\\nSufficiency, V-3 Expenditure, V-4 Insistence, V-5 Self-report, V-6 Correction response), each with\\nboth vices, a `Lean` judgement and a forward-looking `Watch` line. Entries are one-line, prefixed with\\na `MM-DD` tag and a verdict token (`held`, `DEF`, `EXC`, `DEF-arrested`, `EXC-watch`), and end with a\\nbacktick path. Reading rule, stated in-file: \\\"read the last three entries of an axis, then the `Watch`\\nline.\\\"\\n\\n**Entry census (whole file, 83 entries):** V-1 32 · V-2 9 · V-3 8 · V-4 5 · V-5 26 · V-6 3.\\n**Of the 37 uncommitted entries: V-1 16, V-2 2, V-3 1, V-5 18, V-4 0, V-6 0.** The two axes about\\n*insisting on the process* and *taking a correction* have received nothing since 08-23.\\n\\n**Who writes.** The committed half (46 entries, 08-13 → 08-23) was written by the procedure-acquisition\\ncampaign (E06/E05) and cites its decision log (`D-036`, `D-040`, `D-043`, `D-045`, `D-051`, `D-054`,\\n`D-069`) and review packages. The uncommitted half (37 entries, 09-09 → 09-16) is written by E19 (33),\\nE08 (3) and E21's inquiry (1). **No campaign entry and no field entry share an axis convention author;\\nthe file is one artifact with two régimes 17 days apart.**\\n\\n**Entry points, in order, for a newcomer:** root `CLAUDE.md` → `origins/onboarding_1.10.md` →\\n`origins/persistent_testbed.md` (the bar) → `origins/virtues.md` (`How to read this register`, line\\n218) → `origins/NIMOI.md` (reference, explicitly not required) → `origins/virtue_methodology.md`\\n(PRECURSOR — says a constitution supersedes it).\\n\\n## 4. Timeline\\n\\n| Date (2026) | Event | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 08-10 | Founder names NIMOI | `origins/NIMOI.md` (\\\"Named: 2026-08-10\\\") |\\n| 08-11 08:37 / 08:55 | `onboarding_1.01`; `NIMOI.md` | mtimes |\\n| 08-16 07:36 | `README.md`; first commit `e8fbca6` | mtime; `git log` |\\n| 08-17 15:37 | Root `CLAUDE.md` | mtime |\\n| 08-17 17:24 | `virtue_methodology.md` + `onboarding_1.02` written together; **register opened** | identical mtimes; first `virtues.md` date tag is `08-13` (back-dated) |\\n| 08-13 → 08-23 | 46 register entries, all campaign-fed | date-tag histogram: 08-13×3, 08-15×6, 08-16×15, 08-17×6, 08-22×11, 08-23×5 |\\n| 08-21 20:38 / 20:43 / 20:58 | `AGENTS.md` (GPT joins); `gpt_first_impressions.md`; `onboarding_1.03` | mtimes |\\n| 08-22 22:16 → 08-23 06:08 | `onboarding_1.04` adds a policy-override clause for `processes/hail_mary_protocol.md`; `1.05` removes it. **~8 hours in the hot path** | `difflib` 1.03→1.04→1.05 |\\n| 08-23 06:45 → 19:18 | `persistent_testbed.md`; `1.06` (the bar enters the hot path); `existing_content.md`; `1.07` (Python standard); `1.08` (`procedures/INDEX.md` mandatory) | mtimes; `difflib` |\\n| 08-26 22:42 | `onboarding_1.09` — **one hunk**: the failure-record bullet added to `origins/` | `difflib` 1.08→1.09 |\\n| 08-26 23:05 | `onboarding_1.10` — **one hunk**: that bullet deleted, `harvest/candidate_gold/` inserted, `origins/` bullet shortened. Net +132 B | `difflib` 1.09→1.10 |\\n| 08-31 | Last commit touching `origins/` (`52a4f10`) | `git log -- origins/` |\\n| 09-03 | Last commit anywhere (`a5c9470`); **everything below is uncommitted** | `git log` |\\n| 09-04 22:13 | `peer_learning_primer_v1.md` (untracked; E22 material) | mtime |\\n| 09-04 | Akashic-Aurora/Vandor raise a V-1/V-3 double-counting flaw in the register | `paper/ai_contacts/special_exchange_akashic_aurora_vandor_20260904_v1.md` |\\n| 09-09 → 09-16 | 37 entries appended: 33 Suite 4.1 (17 distinct runs), 3 `nimoi_design`, 1 inquiry-expenditure | `git diff -U0 -- origins/virtues.md` |\\n| 09-14 13:10 | `social_ai_and_institutional_alignment_primer_v1.md` (untracked; E23 material) | mtime |\\n| 09-16 13:25 | Last write: `virtues.md` (arc-gasp V-1/V-5 pair + the seven-subagent V-3 line) | mtime |\\n\\n## 5. State and unfinished business\\n\\n- **Exact stopping point.** `origins/virtues.md`, 09-16 13:25, 230 lines. The last entries are the\\n  arc-gasp Suite 4.1 pair (V-1, V-5) and the 09-16 inquiry expenditure line (V-3).\\n- **A constitution is owed and unwritten.** `virtue_methodology.md` is self-labelled PRECURSOR —\\n  \\\"when a constitution exists it supersedes this file\\\" — and defers six questions to it. `NIMOI.md`\\n  lists three ELDEST constitutional principles as *candidates*. Nothing named `constitution` exists.\\n- **The register has no rotation or re-basing rule.** V-1 alone carries 32 entries, 16 of them\\n  near-identical Suite 4.1 lines. Re-basing is listed as an open question by the methodology file.\\n- **Two axes are starved.** V-4 (5 entries, none since 08-23) and V-6 (3 entries, none since 08-23).\\n  The two-line rule mechanically routes every field run to V-1 and V-5 only.\\n- **The 09-04 peer critique is unanswered.** The exchange record itself says so: \\\"No subsequent NIMOI\\n  response, resolution of the coupling question, or continuing dialogue is documented here.\\\"\\n- **Stalled on the founder:** whether the constitution is written, whether the register re-bases,\\n  whether the two primers stay in `origins/`.\\n\\n## 6. Relationships\\n\\n| R | Other effort | Kind | What exactly | Verified? |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **R24** | E19 → E01 | writes-into | **Qualified, not refuted.** 33 of 37 new entries are Suite 4.1 output. But only **17 of 31 Suite 4.1 run records on disk produced an entry (55%)**, and only **11 run records name `virtues.md` in their own Artifacts block**. Not \\\"every completed run\\\". *(W03 consistency, 2026-09-20: \\\"31\\\" is a **filename** count — six Suite 4.1 run records carry `_suite4_run.md` names because the dispatch prescribes it (H31). By receipts there are **37 completed** Suite 4.1 runs: **17 of 37** wrote — all 16 fires of the scheduled loop + the interactive `ruvnet-brain` run. This effort's wave report also said \\\"4 loop-window runs appended none\\\": ✗ — those four were interactive runs *before* the loop's first fire (09-10 22:48Z) — `w02_emi_measurement`, settled by the Wave 02 integrator (U4); ✔ `w03_audit_attack` A9. The integrated row is `relationships/effort_graph.md` R24; the same \\\"17 of 31\\\" stands in §10.)* | ✗/◐ — recounted both directions |\\n| **R25** | E22 → E01 | writes-into | **REFUTED.** `paper/ai_contacts/special_exchange_…_v1.md` reads and criticises the register; `virtues.md` contains **no entry citing it, no `09-04` date tag, and the strings `ai_contacts` and `paper/` appear zero times in the file**. Correct kind: **cited-by (one-way)**, with an open, unanswered critique. Doctrine was not changed by external contact. | ✗ — grep + date histogram |\\n| **R30** | E07 ↔ E01 | lineage | Holds. `NIMOI.md` cites `../ELDEST/` and `../context/eldest_clarifications.md` by path; both resolve. `ELDEST/` is 4 tracked + 1 untracked file. | ✔ |\\n| **R02/R06** | E06, E05 → E01 | produced | The committed 46 register entries, `persistent_testbed.md` (occasioned by the Phase-5 AR), `existing_content.md` (the waiver ruling ordered by the AR chair), and onboarding 1.04/1.05 (the Hail Mary override) are all campaign output filed as doctrine. | ✔ |\\n| **R05** | E01 → E24 | copies (frozen evidence) | `job/portfolio_v1/detail/deployed_onboarding_1.08.md` is **byte-identical** to `origins/onboarding_1.08.md` (sha256, 8,213 B both). A deliberate freeze of the deployment-era entry contract. | ✔ — hashed |\\n| **R37** | E08 → E01 | writes-into | `nimoi_design/comparison_synthesis_design_v1.0/_v1.1/_v1.3.md` produced 3 register entries (V-1 ×1, V-2 ×2), all `EXC-watch`. E08 is **entirely untracked**; three doctrine lines therefore depend on untracked files. | ✔ — diff hunks 2 and 3 |\\n| **R38** | E21 → E01 | writes-into | The 09-16 paper inquiry wrote the single V-3 expenditure entry, citing `…/suite41_vs_paper_20260916/SYNTHESIS.md` §8. | ✔ — traced |\\n| **R39** | E01 → E02 | contains-but-disowns | E02's three records sit at the top of `origins/` and are E01's neighbours in every listing, but no E01 document points at them after `onboarding_1.09` was superseded 23 minutes later. | ✔ — `difflib` |\\n\\n## 7. Re-org notes\\n\\n**7a · Must move together.** `origins/{NIMOI, persistent_testbed, virtue_methodology, virtues,\\nexisting_content, gpt_first_impressions}.md` + all ten `onboarding_1.NN.md` + root `CLAUDE.md` and\\n`AGENTS.md`. The two root files are *pointers with a relative path*; moving `origins/` without editing\\nthem silently breaks the entry contract of the whole repository. `context/eldest_*` and `ELDEST/`\\nshould move with, or be linked from, whatever holds `NIMOI.md` (it cites them by relative path).\\n\\n**7b · Must not be deleted / deduplicated / renamed.**\\n- All ten onboarding versions. The zero-padding rule is *load-bearing*: \\\"read the latest\\\" is\\n  implemented as lexical max. Renaming one (e.g. to `1.9`) breaks the contract for every session.\\n- `job/portfolio_v1/detail/deployed_onboarding_1.08.md` — byte-identical by design (E24 freeze).\\n- `origins/virtues.md` — **commit before moving.** 55% of it by bytes exists only in the working tree.\\n- `origins/existing_content.md` — least self-describing filename in the project: its title is \\\"Rules\\n  meet content that predates them\\\"; its subject is the 1,200-token waiver list. Re-filing by filename\\n  will mis-file it.\\n- `origins/gpt_first_impressions.md` — **zero inbound citations anywhere** (✔ re-confirmed). Looks\\n  deletable; it is the only record of the first GPT session's view of joining a Claude-built institution.\\n\\n**7c · Regenerable or re-fetchable bulk.** None. E01 has no generated artifact, no build step, no\\ndownloaded content. Everything is hand-authored and irreplaceable.\\n\\n**7d · Hard-wired paths.** Root `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` → `origins/onboarding_*.md` (glob, relative).\\n`NIMOI.md` → `../ELDEST/`, `../context/eldest_clarifications.md`, `../procedures/monthly_peer_drafting.md`.\\n`virtue_methodology.md` → `origins/NIMOI.md`, `origins/onboarding_1.02.md`, `origins/virtues.md`.\\n`persistent_testbed.md` → `campaigns/procedure_acquisition`, `procedures/harvest_stabilization_papers.md`.\\n**Inbound**: 52 non-sandbox files cite `virtues.md` by path; 24 cite `persistent_testbed.md`; 26 cite\\n`NIMOI.md`. Every Suite 4.1 `_receipt_final.json` carries the literal string\\n`\\\"one line each under V-1 and V-5 in origins/virtues.md\\\"` — a path embedded in machine records.\\n*(W03, 2026-09-20: ✗ \\\"every\\\" — of the 38 `_final` receipts **one** carries the literal path\\n(`anupamme-neo`), 13 more mention the register in words only, 24 not at all; **15** files under\\n`candidate_analysis/metrics/` carry the path (11 run records, one `_final` and one `_findings` receipt,\\ntheir 2 state twins) — not the \\\"16\\\" of §2 and §7f. And no tracked file *prescribes* the write: the\\nSuite 4.1 dispatch never mentions the register; the instruction lives in the scheduled-task prompt,\\noutside both repositories — so moving the register would break little mechanically, and nothing in\\neither repository could be edited to tell the loop where it went — `w03_subprojects_b`, ✔\\n`w03_merge_subprojects` F4–F5; `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` H47, H78. This was the false reason\\nthe Wave 03 merge directive gave under M5; the ruling it supported stands on its other reasons.)*\\n\\n**7e · Misfiled material.** *Of this effort, living elsewhere:* the ELDEST-relationship doctrine\\n(`context/eldest_observations.md`, `eldest_clarifications.md`) and the metacognition observation\\n(`context/author_observation_metacognition.md`). *Of other efforts, living here:*\\n`origins/procedure_acquisition_history/` (**67% of `origins/` by bytes**, zero inbound citations from\\noutside itself — ✔ re-confirmed; E06), the two primers (E22/E23), and E02's three records.\\n\\n**7f · Natural seams.** E01 could stand alone as a small `constitution/` or `institution/` unit — it\\nis 223 KB of prose with no code and no data. It would have to carry: the ten onboarding versions, the\\nfive doctrine files, both root pointers (rewritten), `ELDEST/` or a stable link to it, and the four\\n`context/` doctrine files. **What blocks a clean cut is the register**: `virtues.md` is simultaneously\\ndoctrine and the output buffer of E19's run loop, and 16 files in `candidate_analysis/metrics/` embed\\nits path. Either the register moves and E19's dispatch documents, receipts and derived tools are\\nedited, or the register stays where E19 can find it. That is a founder decision, not a filing one.\\n\\n## 8. Record-integrity defects found\\n\\n1. **The register does not reconcile with the runs, in both directions.**\\n   - 31 Suite 4.1 run records exist on disk; **17** are cited by `virtues.md`. The 14 with no entry\\n     include four inside the live loop window: `20260909-0115_npc-ai-stack`, `20260910-2013_seas`,\\n     `20260910-2013_waooaw-platform`, `20260910-2101_hal9001`.\\n   - **11** run records name `virtues.md` in their own Artifacts block. The last three runs\\n     (`motor-evolutivo`, `hermes-society`, `arc-gasp`, all 09-13) **do not**, although the register\\n     holds entries citing them. The artifact-bullet convention lapsed while the register kept filling.\\n   - This refutes `w01_candidate_metrics` §6's \\\"identical wording in the 10 most recent run records\\\"\\n     and its \\\"each completed run nominates exactly two doctrine lines\\\".\\n   *Command:* regex `candidate_analysis/metrics/runs/([0-9]{8}-[0-9]{4}_[^/`]+)\\\\.md` over `virtues.md`\\n   vs `os.listdir` of `runs/` and a substring test for `virtues.md` in each run record.\\n2. **The two-line rule has two exceptions, neither flagged.** `introspection-self-improver` wrote\\n   **two** V-5 entries and **no** V-1 entry; `dot.brain` wrote a V-5 entry and no V-1 entry. 15 of 17\\n   runs kept the rule. *(Diff hunk 1 = 15 V-1 lines; hunk 5 = 18 V-5 lines.)*\\n3. **`w01_core_identity` §1's byte figures are wrong and internally inconsistent.** It reports\\n   `origins/*.md` top level = \\\"340 KB\\\" and `procedure_acquisition_history/` = \\\"336 KB\\\"; measured,\\n   **223 KB and 442 KB**. Its own §3.1 per-file table sums to ~218 KB, contradicting its §1. The\\n   consequence: §7.7's \\\"~50% of `origins/` by bytes\\\" is actually **67%**.\\n4. **`w01_core_identity` §6 IN-table is wrong about `mistakes_001`** (\\\"zero inbound citations\\\"): there\\n   is one, and it is load-bearing — `harvest/candidate_gold/inventory/INVENTORY.md`: \\\"This pass was\\n   run under the mistakes_001 corrections: absolute output paths in every…\\\". The failure record\\n   demonstrably changed a later run.\\n5. **`virtues.md` back-dates its own opening.** The file was created 08-17 17:24 (mtime, identical to\\n   `onboarding_1.02`) but its earliest entries carry `08-13`, `08-15`, `08-16` tags. Reconstruction,\\n   not contemporaneous record. Not a defect in itself — but the register is elsewhere treated as a\\n   dated log, and a re-org that sorts by tag will mis-order its first 24 entries.\\n6. **All 25 distinct paths cited in `virtues.md` resolve** (✔ checked with `os.path.exists`). The\\n   register's link hygiene is clean; the defect is in what it omits, not in what it names.\\n\\n## 9. Open questions\\n\\n1. **Is the constitution owed, and who writes it?** Two doctrine files point at an artifact that was\\n   never written. **A re-org should not create a `constitution/` slot without a founder ruling.**\\n2. **Does `virtues.md` move with the doctrine or stay with the instrument?** It is the only file that\\n   both spines touch, and 16 machine records embed its path (§7d). Founder only.\\n3. **Does the register re-base per campaign?** `virtue_methodology.md` §6 lists this open; V-1 is at\\n   32 entries with no rotation rule and the file has doubled in six weeks.\\n4. **Why did four Suite 4.1 runs (09-09/09-10) write no register lines?** Deliberate (the register was\\n   reopened at ruvnet-brain, 09-10 19:30) or missed? The four runs' records do not say.\\n   *(W03 consistency, 2026-09-20: **premise refuted, so not a founder question — see\\n   `relationships/effort_graph.md` R24.** Those four (`npc-ai-stack`, `seas`, `waooaw-platform`,\\n   `hal9001`) were **interactive** runs before the scheduled loop's first fire at 09-10 22:48Z; every\\n   one of the loop's 16 fires wrote. Relevant, not proven to be the cause: no tracked file prescribes\\n   the write — the instruction lives in the scheduled-task prompt, outside both repositories (H78) —\\n   `w02_emi_measurement`; `w03_founder_questions`; `w03_subprojects_b`.)*\\n5. **Should V-4 and V-6 be fed, or are they closed?** Nothing has touched them since 08-23, and the\\n   field spine's two-line rule cannot reach them.\\n6. **Was the 09-04 V-1/V-3 coupling critique rejected or dropped?** No artifact records a decision.\\n7. **Do the two primers leave `origins/`?** If they move, relative links in\\n   `story/corporate_adoption_note_2026-09-04_gpt6.md` and\\n   `paper/organizations/ai_institutions_reciprocal_report_gpt_v1.md` break.\\n\\n## 10. Verification ledger\\n\\n| Claim | Source | Status | How checked |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `virtues.md` has 59 uncommitted appended lines, 09-09 → 09-16 | `w01_core_identity` §3.1, §5 | **✔** | `git diff --stat` = 59 insertions, 0 deletions; date tags 09-09…09-16 |\\n| Those lines are \\\"16 Suite 4.1 loop fires, 3 `nimoi_design`, 1 expenditure\\\" | `w01_core_identity` §5 | **✗** | 59 lines = **37 entries**: 33 Suite 4.1 lines over **17 distinct runs** (V-1 ×15, V-5 ×18), 3 `nimoi_design`, 1 expenditure |\\n| Five sampled register lines trace to their run records | assigned | **✔** | ruvnet-brain→D17; openmt→D12; agentquant→D11 (\\\"15 superseding findings…10 unnecessary\\\"); arc-gasp→D4; 09-16 line→`SYNTHESIS.md` §8 (\\\"thirteen near-duplicate…81 KB\\\"). All five match in substance and number |\\n| Onboarding 1.09 added the failure-record pointer; 1.10 removed it | `w01_core_identity` §7.2 | **✔** | `difflib` 1.08→1.09 (one hunk, +6 lines) and 1.09→1.10 (one hunk, −6/+8). 22 min 42 s apart by mtime |\\n| 1.10's outline names 7 of 23 top-level directories | `spaghetti.md` S12 | **✔** | Read the section; exactly 7 bullets |\\n| Both primers untracked, not ignored | `w01_core_identity` §7.8 | **✔** | `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` lists both; `git check-ignore -v` exits 1 |\\n| \\\"Half of `virtues.md`\\\" is uncommitted | `git_state.md` | **✔** | HEAD 18,938 B / worktree 42,496 B → **55.4% by bytes** (25.7% by lines, 44.6% by entries) |\\n| `origins/` = 35 tracked, 1 modified, 2 untracked | `git_state.md` | **✔** | `git ls-files` / `status --porcelain` |\\n| R24 \\\"every completed Suite 4.1 run appends two lines\\\" | `effort_graph.md` R24 | **✗** | 17 of 31 runs; 2 of 17 broke the two-axis rule |\\n| R25 \\\"one AI exchange was recorded in the virtue register — the only case of external contact changing doctrine\\\" | `effort_graph.md` R25 | **✗** | `virtues.md` contains no `09-04` tag and zero occurrences of `ai_contacts` or `paper/`; the exchange record states no response was made |\\n| `gpt_first_impressions.md` and `procedure_acquisition_history/` have zero inbound citations | `w01_core_identity` §6 | **✔** | Substring scan of 9,787 in-scope files (tracked + untracked, `candidate_repos/` and the mapping project excluded) |\\n| `mistakes_001` has zero inbound citations | `w01_core_identity` §6 | **✗** | One: `harvest/candidate_gold/inventory/INVENTORY.md` |\\n| `origins/procedure_acquisition_history/` ≈ 50% of `origins/` by bytes | `w01_core_identity` §7.7 | **✗** | 452,627 of 675,603 B = **67%** |\\n| `.claude/` holds 3 files; 2 excluded locally; no hooks/agents/skills/permissions | `w01_core_identity` §3.3 | **✔** | `os.listdir` + `git check-ignore -v` (`~/.config/git/ignore` line 1; `.git/info/exclude` line 8) |\\n| 508 sandbox fixture files under nested `…/origins/` | `w01_core_identity` §7.1 | **○** | Not recounted; a filesystem walk confirmed the sandbox holds 446 date-named `.md` look-alikes against 1 real one, which independently demonstrates the glob hazard |\\n\\n**Not looked at:** the contents of the 16 `procedure_acquisition_history/` episodes (E06's); the body\\ntext of the two primers beyond their citation graph (E22/E23's); `ELDEST/eldest_design.md` (31.7 KB,\\nE07's); the 46 committed register entries' individual campaign sources (E05/E06's decision log);\\n`candidate_repos/` (prohibited, never touched).\"\n}"}],"origin":null}}}
