{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:19:28.513Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/000194","body":{"kind":"message","agent":"owner.1","turn":1,"direction":"to_agent","message":{"_type":"UserMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolResultBlock","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xtm4gDk8mbaVDYfUcvkn1N","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E02_failure_records.md\",\n \"start_line\": 1,\n \"end_line\": 250,\n \"total_lines\": 250,\n \"next_offset\": null,\n \"line_truncated\": false,\n \"sha256\": \"0b39628c8669fb00dad5576228990d4d63bd1756acd15c460fab587507d2d56a\",\n \"text\": \"# E02 · Failure records\\n*Group A · state: **dormant in both of its two conventions**; the live practice has migrated to four\\nother registers, one of them outside the repository · active 2026-08-12 → 2026-09-10 · written\\nWave 02 by `w02_doctrine_memory` (opus)*\\n\\n## 1. What it is\\n\\nNIMOI declares that failures are its product — \\\"an unrecorded failure is a failure bought and thrown\\naway\\\" (`procedures/failure_record.md`) — and E02 is the mechanism that was supposed to make that\\nliteral: a durable, attributable, cost-carrying record of each failure the institution wants back\\nlater, ranked so that **failures which corrupt the record outrank failures that merely break\\nsomething.**\\n\\nWhat actually exists is **two incompatible schemes and four records.** Scheme A is a naming\\nconvention at the top of `origins/` (`<series>_NNN_YYYY-MM-DD.md`) with three files, one per series,\\nnone since 08-26. Scheme B is `procedures/failure_record.md` (effective 08-26), which mandates\\n`<area>/reports/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md` and an eight-section schema; **exactly one file in either\\nrepository has ever been written under it.** Meanwhile the institution has recorded on the order of\\n**760 numbered defects** since 08-13 — in run-record `## Deviations` blocks, a campaign deviations\\nregister, a campaign decision log, and a harness-private memory store that is not in git at all. E02\\nis not dormant because the institution stopped failing or stopped recording; it is dormant because\\nthe recording moved and nobody re-pointed the hot path (§3, §5).\\n\\n## 2. Where it lives\\n\\n| Path | Role | Files | Git | Note |\\n|---|---|---:|---|---|\\n| `origins/degradation_001_2026-08-12.md` | **HOME** — scheme A, series 1 | 1 (6,936 B) | tracked | 87% of a weekly Fable-5 limit by Wednesday. **Cited by 23 non-sandbox files**, incl. 5 `processes/` files as the *trigger authority* for `external_technical_assimilation_campaign_v0.1`–`v0.4` |\\n| `origins/debrief_001_2026-08-13.md` | HOME — scheme A, series 2 | 1 (15,548 B) | tracked | Session-nature debrief (S-002). Cited by 14 non-sandbox files (campaigns 9). Says in-file \\\"the agency should not build on this document\\\" |\\n| `origins/mistakes_001_2026-08-26.md` | HOME — scheme A, series 3 | 1 (26,925 B) | tracked | Nine mistakes M-1…M-9 of the gold-harvest session. **1 inbound citation** (`harvest/candidate_gold/inventory/INVENTORY.md`, and it is load-bearing). Holds 2 self-declared unresolved exposures (M-6, M-7) |\\n| `procedures/failure_record.md` | **GOVERNANCE** — scheme B | 1 (3,475 B) | tracked | v1, Effective-Date 08-26, State `directed`. Written 08-26 14:30, committed 08-31 (`52a4f10`). Listed in `procedures/INDEX.md` |\\n| `candidate_analysis/metrics/reports/2026-09-10-gate3-receipts-written-before-read.md` | **OUTPUT-ELSEWHERE** — the only scheme-B record | 1 | tracked | ✔ The **only** file in either repository matching `*/reports/YYYY-MM-DD-*.md` outside the sandbox |\\n| `context/agent_introspection_session_satisfaction_2026-08-13.md` | MATERIAL — the primary record `debrief_001` is \\\"an account of\\\" | 1 (7,767 B) | tracked | Shared with E01 |\\n| `job/portfolio_v1/08_process_failure_history_excerpt.md` | COPY-OF / derived | 1 | tracked | E24's frozen excerpt of the campaign's failure history |\\n\\n### Where failures are actually recorded (the R29 thread, followed)\\n\\n| Register | Where | Volume | Convention | Git | In the hot path? |\\n|---|---|---:|---|---|---|\\n| **Run-record deviations** (E19) | `candidate_analysis/metrics/runs/*.md` → `## Deviations` | **643 entries across 60 run records** (485 carry an extractable bolded `D<n>` id) | `D<n> (stage, class)` — numbering **resets every run**; 297 tag-instances across a 40-term taxonomy | 44 tracked, 16 untracked | No |\\n| **Campaign deviations register** (E06) | `campaigns/procedure_acquisition/sandbox/DEVIATIONS.md` | **42 entries, 184,423 B, 2,855 lines** | `## D-NN · <title>`, append-only, each naming what changed and why | ~~**gitignored** (`sandbox/`)~~ **tracked** *(W03: ✗ \\\"gitignored\\\" — the file is tracked, clean and on the remote: one of the 224 tracked files inside the otherwise ignored `sandbox/` (`git ls-files -s` → blob `cde9f11d`; `check-ignore` exit 1; sha256 of disk = `HEAD` = `origin/v1`). Status was inferred from the directory's ignore rule instead of read per file; this row is where the error began, and the map repeated it in six places — `w03_audit_attack` D10 / W3; ✔ `w03_merge_subprojects`; ✔ integrator)* | No |\\n| **Campaign decision log** (E06) | `campaigns/procedure_acquisition/ledger.md` (323,635 B) + `archive/ledger_phase*.md` | **76 distinct `D-001`…`D-076`** | Decisions, many of them failures; the source of `virtues.md`'s `D-036/040/043/045/051/054/069` | tracked | No |\\n| **Harness session memory** (all efforts) | `C:\\\\Users\\\\pjhud\\\\.claude\\\\projects\\\\C--Users-pjhud-local-26-nimoi\\\\memory\\\\` | **8 files + index, 08-22 → 09-16** | YAML frontmatter (`name`, `description`, `metadata.originSessionId`), body with recurrence counts and run-record `D<n>` citations | **outside the repository entirely** | It *is* the hot path, for Claude sessions only |\\n| **Autosurvey** (E13) | `nimoi-autosurvey/` | **zero** | No `Deviations` heading, no `D-NN` id, no `Lessons` heading anywhere in 19,317 tracked+untracked files. Failures ride in `dev/` procedure version bumps and 6 of 72 commit subjects | — | No |\\n| **Hail Mary 2** (E11/E17) | `hail_mary_2/` (253 files) | **one section** (`work/runs/scan-cycle-1/report.md` → \\\"Caps / failures\\\") | none | tracked | No |\\n\\n**Does NOT include:** the **446** files under `campaigns/procedure_acquisition/sandbox/` whose names\\nmatch `YYYY-MM-DD[-_]*.md` (fixtures and mutants: `2026-08-20_reconcile_failure.md`,\\n`2026-08-21_close_note_failure.md`, …). Against **one** real scheme-B record in the whole tree, they\\nare a 446:1 decoy ratio. Also not E02: `general_findings/` (E03 — `failure_record.md` explicitly\\nroutes \\\"a finding true outside the work that produced it\\\" there).\\n\\n## 3. How it works\\n\\n**Scheme A — `origins/<series>_NNN_YYYY-MM-DD.md`.** Three parallel series, one instance each.\\n`mistakes_001` documents opening the third series and why (\\\"the word is the founder's own\\\"). The\\nschema is the one `mistakes_001` argues for: *what I believed · why it was reasonable · what happened ·\\nevidence · cost · the reusable lesson*, with the second field named as the load-bearing one.\\nNo procedure governs scheme A; it is convention only.\\n\\n**Scheme B — `procedures/failure_record.md` v1 (08-26).** Path `<area>/reports/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md`,\\ndated the day the failure was *established*. Eight sections in fixed order: TL;DR · Symptom\\n(*\\\"including no symptom… Silence is the finding\\\"*) · Reproduction (every claim carries its command and\\nthat command's actual output; a claim without one is marked **unverified** and stays visible) · Root\\ncause (the mechanism, with a **control** quoted where one exists) · What was lost (counted) ·\\nResolution (recovery before fix) · Verification (prefer a check that fails on the old code) ·\\nFollow-up (including **negative results**). Its provenance is declared: the format is adapted from\\n`maci0/clanker`'s `docs/reports/bugs/`, read in\\n`context/candidate_repos_areev_clanker_read_2026-08-26.md`, rewritten rather than copied.\\n\\n**The two schemes do not know about each other.** ✔ `failure_record.md` never mentions `origins/`,\\n`degradation`, `debrief` or `mistakes`; `mistakes_001` contains zero occurrences of `failure_record`.\\nThe three `origins/` files match neither scheme B's path nor its schema.\\n\\n**The 08-26 collision, to the minute** — one day, four acts, no coherence:\\n\\n| Time | Act | Consequence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 14:30 | `procedures/failure_record.md` written (scheme B) | A new scheme exists |\\n| 22:42 | `onboarding_1.09` adds a hot-path bullet naming **scheme A** (`degradation_NNN_*`, `mistakes_NNN_*`) with a firing condition | Scheme A enters the hot path; scheme B never does |\\n| 23:05 | `onboarding_1.10` **deletes that bullet** and uses the position for `harvest/candidate_gold/` | Scheme A leaves the hot path after 23 minutes |\\n| 23:47 | `mistakes_001` finalised — written under scheme A, citing neither scheme B nor 1.09/1.10 | The newest record is orphaned at birth |\\n\\n`mistakes_001`'s own Provenance says: *\\\"This file is not referenced from the hot path. Per\\n`general_findings/warm-reference-not-cold-archive`, that makes it cold archive rather than warm\\nreference. No pointer was added to `origins/onboarding_1.08.md`…\\\"* — **wrong twice**: the current\\nversion was 1.10, not 1.08, and a pointer *had* been added (1.09) and removed (1.10) in the preceding\\n65 minutes.\\n\\n**Entry points, in order:** `procedures/INDEX.md` (hot path since onboarding 1.08) → \\\"**Failure\\nRecord** — writes the durable record of a failure…\\\" → `procedures/failure_record.md` → the single\\nrecord at `candidate_analysis/metrics/reports/2026-09-10-gate3-receipts-written-before-read.md`.\\nScheme A has **no** entry point: no onboarding version names it, and `origins/` has no index.\\n\\n## 4. Timeline\\n\\n| Date (2026) | Event | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 08-12 | `degradation_001` — first impactful degradation declared; *\\\"for a GA, failures are assets\\\"* | file |\\n| 08-13 18:44 | `debrief_001` (S-002 of `procedure_acquisition`) | mtime |\\n| 08-13 → 08-21 | 42 deviations accumulate in the campaign's `sandbox/DEVIATIONS.md` (D-01 → D-42) | file |\\n| 08-22 17:08 | **First harness-memory file written** (`nlt-ledger-parallel-candidates.md`) — the fork begins | mtime |\\n| 08-26 14:30 | `procedures/failure_record.md` v1 | mtime; in-file Effective-Date |\\n| 08-26 22:42 → 23:47 | The collision (§3 table) | `difflib`, mtimes |\\n| 08-31 | Suite 1/2 opens `## Deviations` blocks in run records; **643-entry accumulation begins** | `runs/20260831-*` |\\n| 08-31 | `52a4f10` commits `failure_record.md` (added) and `general_findings.md` (modified) | `git log --name-status` |\\n| 09-03 | Last commit anywhere | `git log` |\\n| 09-10 16:33 → 18:49 | **Five harness-memory files written in one afternoon** (`candidate-repos-clone-longpaths`, `suite4-orchestration-harness-limits`, `gate-receipts-compute-then-write`, `bash-cwd-and-heredoc-hazards`, `harness-injects-candidate-claude-md`) | mtimes |\\n| 09-10 22:25–22:29 UTC | The gate-3 receipt failure occurs | the record |\\n| 09-10 | **The only scheme-B record ever written**, \\\"Format per `procedures/failure_record.md`\\\" | `candidate_analysis/metrics/reports/2026-09-10-…md` |\\n| 09-11 16:55 | `derived-tool-path-bell-character.md` (harness memory) | mtime |\\n| 09-13 19:53 | Last Suite 4.1 run; deviation accumulation stops at 643 | `runs/20260913-1953_arc-gasp_…` |\\n| 09-16 13:20 | `large-tool-output-slicing.md` + `MEMORY.md` — last failure-shaped record written anywhere in the project's orbit, **and it is outside the repository** | mtimes |\\n\\n## 5. State and unfinished business\\n\\n- **Exact stopping point.** Scheme A: `mistakes_001`, 08-26 23:47. Scheme B: one record, 09-10.\\n  Both dormant. The *practice* continued to 09-16 in registers E02 does not own.\\n- **What it says it still owes.** `mistakes_001` §5 names four items: a decision about `candidate_repos/`\\n  (M-6, \\\"the only entry here with an unresolved live exposure\\\" — nine untrusted `CLAUDE.md` files still\\n  in the tree, gitignored); a verification pass over a sample of the gold harvest's grades (M-7, the\\n  debt named in `harvest/candidate_gold/SYNTHESIS.md` Part V); a check of M-8's heredoc failure against\\n  the existing general finding; and an escalation for M-9 (\\\"third instance of `silent-tool-failure` in\\n  one session… past the point where recording it again is the right response\\\"). **None was done.**\\n- **The gate-3 record has an unbuilt follow-up** (per `w01_candidate_metrics` §4 E2).\\n- **Stalled on:** a ruling on which scheme wins. This is the cheapest live decision in Group A and it\\n  currently costs the institution its declared primary product.\\n\\n## 6. Relationships\\n\\n| R | Other effort | Kind | What exactly | Verified? |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **R29** | E19, E11, E13 ⇸ E02, E03 | **missing link** | **Confirmed and enlarged by an order of magnitude.** W01 said \\\"dozens\\\"; measured: **643** deviations in 60 run records, **42** in `sandbox/DEVIATIONS.md`, **76** campaign decision-log entries, **8** harness-memory files — against **1** scheme-B record and **3** scheme-A records. E13 records nothing at all. | **✔ (magnitude ✗)** |\\n| **R39** | E01 ↔ E02 | contains-but-disowns | E02's three files sit in E01's directory; no E01 document points at them after 1.09 was superseded 23 minutes later. E02's doctrine (\\\"failures are the product\\\") lives in `origins/persistent_testbed.md` §3 — E01's file. | ✔ |\\n| **R40** | E19 → E02 | produced (once) | E19 wrote the only scheme-B record. `candidate_analysis/metrics`' *single* citation of `procedures/` in 3,299 files is that record's \\\"Format per `procedures/failure_record.md`\\\". | ✔ |\\n| **R41** | E15 → E02 | produced (the format) | Scheme B's eight-section schema is adapted from `maci0/clanker`'s bug reports, read during E15's first-contact reads. **Declared in-file**; the provenance statement exists because `processes/procedure_deployment_entry.md` §2 makes undeclared external text the first thing an audit looks for. | ✔ |\\n| **R42** | E02 → E16 | corrected | `harvest/candidate_gold/inventory/INVENTORY.md`: \\\"This pass was run under the mistakes_001 corrections: absolute output paths in every…\\\". The one demonstrated case of a failure record changing later work. | ✔ |\\n| **R43** | E02 ∥ harness memory | **parallel — a fifth register, outside git** | 8 files at `~/.claude/projects/C--Users-pjhud-local-26-nimoi/memory/`, 08-22 → 09-16, in exactly E03's shape (frontmatter + cross-cutting body + recurrence counts) and citing run-record deviation ids. **Invisible to git, to a re-org, and to every GPT session** (it is a Claude-Code-side store; `AGENTS.md` cannot reach it). | ✔ |\\n| **R44** | E05, E06 → E02 | depends-on | `processes/external_technical_assimilation_campaign_v0.1`–`v0.4` cite `degradation_001` as **trigger authority**. Deleting or re-homing that file without a forwarding pointer invalidates four process versions' trigger condition. | ✔ |\\n\\n## 7. Re-org notes\\n\\n**7a · Must move together.** The three `origins/` records + `procedures/failure_record.md` + the one\\nscheme-B record + `context/agent_introspection_session_satisfaction_2026-08-13.md` (the evidence\\n`debrief_001` is an account of). If the *practice* is to be consolidated, the four other registers\\n(§2 table) must move or be linked in the same operation, or consolidation will move four files and\\nleave 760 records behind.\\n\\n**7b · Must not be deleted / deduplicated / renamed.**\\n- `origins/degradation_001_2026-08-12.md` — **cited as trigger authority by five `processes/` versions**\\n  (R44). The most load-bearing file in E02 despite being the oldest. *(W03 consistency, 2026-09-20:\\n  \\\"five `processes/` versions\\\" here and in §9 Q5, against \\\"v0.1–v0.4\\\" in §6 — both count the same\\n  grep: **four process versions** (v0.1–v0.4, two citations each) **plus one mention in\\n  `processes/reference/…_history.md`** = five `processes/` *files*, four *versions* — Wave 02\\n  integrator check c3; R44.)*\\n- `campaigns/…/sandbox/DEVIATIONS.md` — 184 KB, **gitignored**, the only record of 42 spec deviations\\n  in E06's Phase 5. A backup-by-`git ls-files` loses it entirely (hazard H01's class). *(W03: ✗ — it is\\n  **tracked**; a backup by `git ls-files` **keeps** it. It stays on this must-not-delete list for what\\n  it records, not for a git exposure it does not have — `w03_audit_attack` A11; see §2.)*\\n- The harness memory store — not in the repository, not in any backup of it, and it holds the only\\n  written account of at least four environment hazards (R43).\\n- The 446 sandbox date-named look-alikes — E06 mutation-test corpus (H20).\\n\\n**7c · Regenerable or re-fetchable bulk.** None. Every E02 artifact is a one-off account of an event\\nthat cannot be re-run.\\n\\n**7d · Hard-wired paths.** `procedures/failure_record.md` mandates a **relative, area-scoped** path\\nshape (`<area>/reports/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md`), so re-homing any area silently changes where its\\nfuture failure records belong and orphans the existing one from its area. `failure_record.md` cites\\n`context/candidate_repos_areev_clanker_read_2026-08-26.md` and\\n`processes/procedure_deployment_entry.md` by path. `degradation_001` is cited by path from\\n`processes/` ×5, `campaigns/` ×13, `job/` ×2, `origins/` ×2, `context/` ×1.\\n\\n**7e · Misfiled material.** *Of this effort, elsewhere:* the entire live practice (§2, second table).\\n*Of other efforts, here:* nothing — E02's three files are small and genuinely E02's; their problem is\\nthat they sit inside E01's directory with no pointer of their own.\\n\\n**7f · Natural seams.** E02 **cannot** stand alone as filed: four files is not a register. The real\\nseam is the opposite one — a re-org could make E02 the *index* of the institution's failure memory\\nrather than its container: one `failure/` location holding the procedure, the four records, and a\\nstated map to the four external registers with their conventions and volumes. That requires deciding\\nscheme A vs scheme B first, and deciding whether the harness-memory store is inside or outside the\\ninstitution. Both are founder calls. **What must not happen is a re-org that files \\\"failure records\\\"\\nas a 4-file folder and thereby certifies that the institution recorded four failures in six weeks.**\\n\\n## 8. Record-integrity defects found\\n\\n1. **`mistakes_001`'s Provenance is wrong at the moment of writing** — names `onboarding_1.08.md` when\\n   1.10 was current, and says no pointer was added when one had been added (1.09, 22:42) and removed\\n   (1.10, 23:05) in the preceding 65 minutes. *Command:* `difflib` over 1.08/1.09/1.10 + mtimes.\\n2. **Scheme B has never been exercised outside one area.** *Command:* regex\\n   `(^|/)reports?/20\\\\d\\\\d-\\\\d\\\\d-\\\\d\\\\d[-_].*\\\\.md$` over `git ls-files` + `git ls-files --others\\n   --exclude-standard` for **both** repositories (9,787 + 19,317 paths) → **1 hit**; and an\\n   `os.walk` of the whole `nimoi/` filesystem (49,852 files, `candidate_repos/` excluded) for\\n   `^20\\\\d\\\\d-\\\\d\\\\d-\\\\d\\\\d[-_].*\\\\.md$` → 447 hits, **446 of them in `campaigns/…/sandbox/`**.\\n3. **Deviation numbering is per-run and therefore non-addressable.** Every run record restarts at\\n   `D1`. `virtues.md` cites \\\"run deviation D17\\\" and the `D-036`-style campaign ids in the same file\\n   with no namespace distinguishing them. Two of the four live registers use the token `D<n>` for\\n   incompatible things.\\n4. **Recurrence is counted but never promoted.** Run records self-count: *\\\"Fourteenth consecutive run\\n   with an orchestrator briefing error caught by agents\\\"* (necrozma, 09-12); *\\\"Twelfth consecutive\\n   run…\\\"* (mini-ork); *\\\"Third consecutive run this rule has failed\\\"* (mobius). **17 deviations are\\n   explicitly tagged `carried`** — recurring and unrepaired. The `record_audit_v4.1` \\\"domain routing\\n   while withholding the rubric\\\" defect is recorded as carried across **twelve** runs. None became a\\n   failure record or a general finding.\\n5. **`procedures/failure_record.md` is `State: directed` and listed in `procedures/INDEX.md`, yet\\n   `candidate_analysis/metrics` — the one area that used it — cites `procedures/` exactly once in\\n   3,299 files, and `processes/` zero times.** The procedure is deployed and effectively unused.\\n\\n## 9. Open questions\\n\\n1. **Which scheme wins?** Founder only. Scheme A is warm-referenced (23 + 14 inbound citations) but\\n   has no entry point; scheme B has an entry point and one record.\\n2. **Are run-record deviations failure records?** They satisfy most of scheme B's schema (symptom,\\n   root cause, resolution, verification) at a finer grain and higher volume. If yes, E02's home is\\n   `candidate_analysis/metrics/runs/` and the institution should say so. If no, 643 defects are\\n   outside the memory system by design and the institution should say *that*.\\n3. **Is the harness memory store part of NIMOI?** It is where the institution's environment knowledge\\n   actually went after 08-22. It is per-machine, per-harness, per-model-vendor, and unversioned.\\n   *(W03 consistency, 2026-09-20: the same question as **E03 §9 Q2**, asked from the other side; it is\\n   put to the founder once, as **FQ-38** — `w03_founder_questions`. Two facts since: the store holds\\n   **9** files now — the ninth written by the mapping effort's own session on 09-19 (H39) — and\\n   `nimoi-autosurvey` has a store of its own, 7 entries (H72).)*\\n4. **What happened to M-6?** `mistakes_001` records nine untrusted `CLAUDE.md` files inside the working\\n   tree as a **live unresolved exposure**. The 09-10 `seas` run then recorded (D8) the harness\\n   injecting a candidate repository's `CLAUDE.md` into a producer's context as if it were project\\n   instructions — i.e. **the exposure fired**, was recorded as a run deviation and in harness memory,\\n   and was never written back to M-6.\\n5. **Does `degradation_001` move?** Five `processes/` versions depend on it as a trigger authority.\\n\\n## 10. Verification ledger\\n\\n| Claim | Source (W01 §) | Status | How checked |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Two incompatible failure-record conventions exist | `w01_core_identity` §7.3 | **✔** | Read both in full; scheme B's path/schema vs the three `origins/` filenames |\\n| \\\"Neither document mentions the other\\\" | `w01_core_identity` §7.3 | **✔** | `failure_record.md` contains no `origins`/`debrief`/`degradation`/`mistakes`; `mistakes_001` contains `failure_record` ×0 |\\n| No record exists under scheme B other than the gate-3 one | assigned | **✔** | Two independent enumerations (git in both repos; `os.walk` of the filesystem) → 1 hit, 446 sandbox decoys |\\n| `failure_record.md` is v1, effective 08-26, state `directed` | `w01_core_identity` §4 E2 | **✔** | In-file header; mtime 08-26 14:30; added to git in `52a4f10` (08-31) |\\n| E02 is \\\"dormant and structurally orphaned\\\" | `w01_core_identity` §4 E2 | **◐ partly ✗** | Dormant ✔. \\\"Orphaned\\\" holds for `mistakes_001` (1 citer) but **not** for `degradation_001` (23 citers, incl. 5 processes as trigger authority) or `debrief_001` (14 citers) |\\n| \\\"Dozens\\\" of defects recorded as run deviations since 08-31 | `w01_core_identity` §8.3 / R29 | **✗ (understated)** | **643** across 60 run records (`## Deviations` section parse); 297 tagged instances; 17 tagged `carried` |\\n| Failures are also recorded in `sandbox/DEVIATIONS.md` | assigned | **✔** | 42 entries `D-01`…`D-42`, 184,423 B, 2,855 lines; gitignored *(W03: the ✔ certifies the counts — 70 `## D-` entries, highest D-42, 184,423 B all reproduce; ✗ the adjective: the file is **tracked** — `w03_audit_attack` D10)* |\\n| …in `hail_mary_2` | assigned | **✗** | No failure-record convention: one \\\"Caps / failures\\\" heading in 253 files (`work/runs/scan-cycle-1/report.md`) |\\n| …in autosurvey's `dev/` history | assigned | **✗** | Zero `Deviations`/`D-NN`/`Lessons` occurrences in 19,317 files. `dev/` is a *version* history (92 files: 43 procedure versions, 49 standards versions); failures ride in version bumps and 6 of 72 commit subjects |\\n| …in the session memory files | assigned | **✔ and material** | 8 files + `MEMORY.md`, 08-22 → 09-16, at `~/.claude/projects/C--Users-pjhud-local-26-nimoi/memory/`; frontmatter + recurrence counts + run-record `D<n>` citations |\\n| The campaign decision log is a fourth register | followed | **✔** | 76 distinct `D-001`…`D-076` across `campaigns/` non-sandbox `.md` files; `ledger.md` alone is 323,635 B |\\n| Fraction of run deviations meeting `general_findings/`'s admission test | assigned | **≈ 40–50%** | Systematic sample: every 20th of 485 extractable deviations (n = 25), hand-classified against \\\"would this still be true and useful in a piece of work that has nothing to do with where it was learned?\\\" → 11 clear yes, 2 borderline. See E03 §5 for the worked list |\\n\\n**Not looked at:** the body text of the 643 deviations beyond the 25-item sample and the 17 `carried`\\nentries; `campaigns/procedure_acquisition/ledger.md` in full (323 KB, E06's); the gate-3 record's\\nown eight sections in detail (E19's); `candidate_repos/` (prohibited, never touched).\"\n}"}],"is_error":null}],"uuid":"c53bc98c-c0ef-4c81-97bb-95c58c6d7a34","parent_tool_use_id":null,"tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E02_failure_records.md\",\n \"start_line\": 1,\n \"end_line\": 250,\n \"total_lines\": 250,\n \"next_offset\": null,\n \"line_truncated\": false,\n \"sha256\": \"0b39628c8669fb00dad5576228990d4d63bd1756acd15c460fab587507d2d56a\",\n \"text\": \"# E02 · Failure records\\n*Group A · state: **dormant in both of its two conventions**; the live practice has migrated to four\\nother registers, one of them outside the repository · active 2026-08-12 → 2026-09-10 · written\\nWave 02 by `w02_doctrine_memory` (opus)*\\n\\n## 1. What it is\\n\\nNIMOI declares that failures are its product — \\\"an unrecorded failure is a failure bought and thrown\\naway\\\" (`procedures/failure_record.md`) — and E02 is the mechanism that was supposed to make that\\nliteral: a durable, attributable, cost-carrying record of each failure the institution wants back\\nlater, ranked so that **failures which corrupt the record outrank failures that merely break\\nsomething.**\\n\\nWhat actually exists is **two incompatible schemes and four records.** Scheme A is a naming\\nconvention at the top of `origins/` (`<series>_NNN_YYYY-MM-DD.md`) with three files, one per series,\\nnone since 08-26. Scheme B is `procedures/failure_record.md` (effective 08-26), which mandates\\n`<area>/reports/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md` and an eight-section schema; **exactly one file in either\\nrepository has ever been written under it.** Meanwhile the institution has recorded on the order of\\n**760 numbered defects** since 08-13 — in run-record `## Deviations` blocks, a campaign deviations\\nregister, a campaign decision log, and a harness-private memory store that is not in git at all. E02\\nis not dormant because the institution stopped failing or stopped recording; it is dormant because\\nthe recording moved and nobody re-pointed the hot path (§3, §5).\\n\\n## 2. Where it lives\\n\\n| Path | Role | Files | Git | Note |\\n|---|---|---:|---|---|\\n| `origins/degradation_001_2026-08-12.md` | **HOME** — scheme A, series 1 | 1 (6,936 B) | tracked | 87% of a weekly Fable-5 limit by Wednesday. **Cited by 23 non-sandbox files**, incl. 5 `processes/` files as the *trigger authority* for `external_technical_assimilation_campaign_v0.1`–`v0.4` |\\n| `origins/debrief_001_2026-08-13.md` | HOME — scheme A, series 2 | 1 (15,548 B) | tracked | Session-nature debrief (S-002). Cited by 14 non-sandbox files (campaigns 9). Says in-file \\\"the agency should not build on this document\\\" |\\n| `origins/mistakes_001_2026-08-26.md` | HOME — scheme A, series 3 | 1 (26,925 B) | tracked | Nine mistakes M-1…M-9 of the gold-harvest session. **1 inbound citation** (`harvest/candidate_gold/inventory/INVENTORY.md`, and it is load-bearing). Holds 2 self-declared unresolved exposures (M-6, M-7) |\\n| `procedures/failure_record.md` | **GOVERNANCE** — scheme B | 1 (3,475 B) | tracked | v1, Effective-Date 08-26, State `directed`. Written 08-26 14:30, committed 08-31 (`52a4f10`). Listed in `procedures/INDEX.md` |\\n| `candidate_analysis/metrics/reports/2026-09-10-gate3-receipts-written-before-read.md` | **OUTPUT-ELSEWHERE** — the only scheme-B record | 1 | tracked | ✔ The **only** file in either repository matching `*/reports/YYYY-MM-DD-*.md` outside the sandbox |\\n| `context/agent_introspection_session_satisfaction_2026-08-13.md` | MATERIAL — the primary record `debrief_001` is \\\"an account of\\\" | 1 (7,767 B) | tracked | Shared with E01 |\\n| `job/portfolio_v1/08_process_failure_history_excerpt.md` | COPY-OF / derived | 1 | tracked | E24's frozen excerpt of the campaign's failure history |\\n\\n### Where failures are actually recorded (the R29 thread, followed)\\n\\n| Register | Where | Volume | Convention | Git | In the hot path? |\\n|---|---|---:|---|---|---|\\n| **Run-record deviations** (E19) | `candidate_analysis/metrics/runs/*.md` → `## Deviations` | **643 entries across 60 run records** (485 carry an extractable bolded `D<n>` id) | `D<n> (stage, class)` — numbering **resets every run**; 297 tag-instances across a 40-term taxonomy | 44 tracked, 16 untracked | No |\\n| **Campaign deviations register** (E06) | `campaigns/procedure_acquisition/sandbox/DEVIATIONS.md` | **42 entries, 184,423 B, 2,855 lines** | `## D-NN · <title>`, append-only, each naming what changed and why | ~~**gitignored** (`sandbox/`)~~ **tracked** *(W03: ✗ \\\"gitignored\\\" — the file is tracked, clean and on the remote: one of the 224 tracked files inside the otherwise ignored `sandbox/` (`git ls-files -s` → blob `cde9f11d`; `check-ignore` exit 1; sha256 of disk = `HEAD` = `origin/v1`). Status was inferred from the directory's ignore rule instead of read per file; this row is where the error began, and the map repeated it in six places — `w03_audit_attack` D10 / W3; ✔ `w03_merge_subprojects`; ✔ integrator)* | No |\\n| **Campaign decision log** (E06) | `campaigns/procedure_acquisition/ledger.md` (323,635 B) + `archive/ledger_phase*.md` | **76 distinct `D-001`…`D-076`** | Decisions, many of them failures; the source of `virtues.md`'s `D-036/040/043/045/051/054/069` | tracked | No |\\n| **Harness session memory** (all efforts) | `C:\\\\Users\\\\pjhud\\\\.claude\\\\projects\\\\C--Users-pjhud-local-26-nimoi\\\\memory\\\\` | **8 files + index, 08-22 → 09-16** | YAML frontmatter (`name`, `description`, `metadata.originSessionId`), body with recurrence counts and run-record `D<n>` citations | **outside the repository entirely** | It *is* the hot path, for Claude sessions only |\\n| **Autosurvey** (E13) | `nimoi-autosurvey/` | **zero** | No `Deviations` heading, no `D-NN` id, no `Lessons` heading anywhere in 19,317 tracked+untracked files. Failures ride in `dev/` procedure version bumps and 6 of 72 commit subjects | — | No |\\n| **Hail Mary 2** (E11/E17) | `hail_mary_2/` (253 files) | **one section** (`work/runs/scan-cycle-1/report.md` → \\\"Caps / failures\\\") | none | tracked | No |\\n\\n**Does NOT include:** the **446** files under `campaigns/procedure_acquisition/sandbox/` whose names\\nmatch `YYYY-MM-DD[-_]*.md` (fixtures and mutants: `2026-08-20_reconcile_failure.md`,\\n`2026-08-21_close_note_failure.md`, …). Against **one** real scheme-B record in the whole tree, they\\nare a 446:1 decoy ratio. Also not E02: `general_findings/` (E03 — `failure_record.md` explicitly\\nroutes \\\"a finding true outside the work that produced it\\\" there).\\n\\n## 3. How it works\\n\\n**Scheme A — `origins/<series>_NNN_YYYY-MM-DD.md`.** Three parallel series, one instance each.\\n`mistakes_001` documents opening the third series and why (\\\"the word is the founder's own\\\"). The\\nschema is the one `mistakes_001` argues for: *what I believed · why it was reasonable · what happened ·\\nevidence · cost · the reusable lesson*, with the second field named as the load-bearing one.\\nNo procedure governs scheme A; it is convention only.\\n\\n**Scheme B — `procedures/failure_record.md` v1 (08-26).** Path `<area>/reports/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md`,\\ndated the day the failure was *established*. Eight sections in fixed order: TL;DR · Symptom\\n(*\\\"including no symptom… Silence is the finding\\\"*) · Reproduction (every claim carries its command and\\nthat command's actual output; a claim without one is marked **unverified** and stays visible) · Root\\ncause (the mechanism, with a **control** quoted where one exists) · What was lost (counted) ·\\nResolution (recovery before fix) · Verification (prefer a check that fails on the old code) ·\\nFollow-up (including **negative results**). Its provenance is declared: the format is adapted from\\n`maci0/clanker`'s `docs/reports/bugs/`, read in\\n`context/candidate_repos_areev_clanker_read_2026-08-26.md`, rewritten rather than copied.\\n\\n**The two schemes do not know about each other.** ✔ `failure_record.md` never mentions `origins/`,\\n`degradation`, `debrief` or `mistakes`; `mistakes_001` contains zero occurrences of `failure_record`.\\nThe three `origins/` files match neither scheme B's path nor its schema.\\n\\n**The 08-26 collision, to the minute** — one day, four acts, no coherence:\\n\\n| Time | Act | Consequence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 14:30 | `procedures/failure_record.md` written (scheme B) | A new scheme exists |\\n| 22:42 | `onboarding_1.09` adds a hot-path bullet naming **scheme A** (`degradation_NNN_*`, `mistakes_NNN_*`) with a firing condition | Scheme A enters the hot path; scheme B never does |\\n| 23:05 | `onboarding_1.10` **deletes that bullet** and uses the position for `harvest/candidate_gold/` | Scheme A leaves the hot path after 23 minutes |\\n| 23:47 | `mistakes_001` finalised — written under scheme A, citing neither scheme B nor 1.09/1.10 | The newest record is orphaned at birth |\\n\\n`mistakes_001`'s own Provenance says: *\\\"This file is not referenced from the hot path. Per\\n`general_findings/warm-reference-not-cold-archive`, that makes it cold archive rather than warm\\nreference. No pointer was added to `origins/onboarding_1.08.md`…\\\"* — **wrong twice**: the current\\nversion was 1.10, not 1.08, and a pointer *had* been added (1.09) and removed (1.10) in the preceding\\n65 minutes.\\n\\n**Entry points, in order:** `procedures/INDEX.md` (hot path since onboarding 1.08) → \\\"**Failure\\nRecord** — writes the durable record of a failure…\\\" → `procedures/failure_record.md` → the single\\nrecord at `candidate_analysis/metrics/reports/2026-09-10-gate3-receipts-written-before-read.md`.\\nScheme A has **no** entry point: no onboarding version names it, and `origins/` has no index.\\n\\n## 4. Timeline\\n\\n| Date (2026) | Event | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 08-12 | `degradation_001` — first impactful degradation declared; *\\\"for a GA, failures are assets\\\"* | file |\\n| 08-13 18:44 | `debrief_001` (S-002 of `procedure_acquisition`) | mtime |\\n| 08-13 → 08-21 | 42 deviations accumulate in the campaign's `sandbox/DEVIATIONS.md` (D-01 → D-42) | file |\\n| 08-22 17:08 | **First harness-memory file written** (`nlt-ledger-parallel-candidates.md`) — the fork begins | mtime |\\n| 08-26 14:30 | `procedures/failure_record.md` v1 | mtime; in-file Effective-Date |\\n| 08-26 22:42 → 23:47 | The collision (§3 table) | `difflib`, mtimes |\\n| 08-31 | Suite 1/2 opens `## Deviations` blocks in run records; **643-entry accumulation begins** | `runs/20260831-*` |\\n| 08-31 | `52a4f10` commits `failure_record.md` (added) and `general_findings.md` (modified) | `git log --name-status` |\\n| 09-03 | Last commit anywhere | `git log` |\\n| 09-10 16:33 → 18:49 | **Five harness-memory files written in one afternoon** (`candidate-repos-clone-longpaths`, `suite4-orchestration-harness-limits`, `gate-receipts-compute-then-write`, `bash-cwd-and-heredoc-hazards`, `harness-injects-candidate-claude-md`) | mtimes |\\n| 09-10 22:25–22:29 UTC | The gate-3 receipt failure occurs | the record |\\n| 09-10 | **The only scheme-B record ever written**, \\\"Format per `procedures/failure_record.md`\\\" | `candidate_analysis/metrics/reports/2026-09-10-…md` |\\n| 09-11 16:55 | `derived-tool-path-bell-character.md` (harness memory) | mtime |\\n| 09-13 19:53 | Last Suite 4.1 run; deviation accumulation stops at 643 | `runs/20260913-1953_arc-gasp_…` |\\n| 09-16 13:20 | `large-tool-output-slicing.md` + `MEMORY.md` — last failure-shaped record written anywhere in the project's orbit, **and it is outside the repository** | mtimes |\\n\\n## 5. State and unfinished business\\n\\n- **Exact stopping point.** Scheme A: `mistakes_001`, 08-26 23:47. Scheme B: one record, 09-10.\\n  Both dormant. The *practice* continued to 09-16 in registers E02 does not own.\\n- **What it says it still owes.** `mistakes_001` §5 names four items: a decision about `candidate_repos/`\\n  (M-6, \\\"the only entry here with an unresolved live exposure\\\" — nine untrusted `CLAUDE.md` files still\\n  in the tree, gitignored); a verification pass over a sample of the gold harvest's grades (M-7, the\\n  debt named in `harvest/candidate_gold/SYNTHESIS.md` Part V); a check of M-8's heredoc failure against\\n  the existing general finding; and an escalation for M-9 (\\\"third instance of `silent-tool-failure` in\\n  one session… past the point where recording it again is the right response\\\"). **None was done.**\\n- **The gate-3 record has an unbuilt follow-up** (per `w01_candidate_metrics` §4 E2).\\n- **Stalled on:** a ruling on which scheme wins. This is the cheapest live decision in Group A and it\\n  currently costs the institution its declared primary product.\\n\\n## 6. Relationships\\n\\n| R | Other effort | Kind | What exactly | Verified? |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **R29** | E19, E11, E13 ⇸ E02, E03 | **missing link** | **Confirmed and enlarged by an order of magnitude.** W01 said \\\"dozens\\\"; measured: **643** deviations in 60 run records, **42** in `sandbox/DEVIATIONS.md`, **76** campaign decision-log entries, **8** harness-memory files — against **1** scheme-B record and **3** scheme-A records. E13 records nothing at all. | **✔ (magnitude ✗)** |\\n| **R39** | E01 ↔ E02 | contains-but-disowns | E02's three files sit in E01's directory; no E01 document points at them after 1.09 was superseded 23 minutes later. E02's doctrine (\\\"failures are the product\\\") lives in `origins/persistent_testbed.md` §3 — E01's file. | ✔ |\\n| **R40** | E19 → E02 | produced (once) | E19 wrote the only scheme-B record. `candidate_analysis/metrics`' *single* citation of `procedures/` in 3,299 files is that record's \\\"Format per `procedures/failure_record.md`\\\". | ✔ |\\n| **R41** | E15 → E02 | produced (the format) | Scheme B's eight-section schema is adapted from `maci0/clanker`'s bug reports, read during E15's first-contact reads. **Declared in-file**; the provenance statement exists because `processes/procedure_deployment_entry.md` §2 makes undeclared external text the first thing an audit looks for. | ✔ |\\n| **R42** | E02 → E16 | corrected | `harvest/candidate_gold/inventory/INVENTORY.md`: \\\"This pass was run under the mistakes_001 corrections: absolute output paths in every…\\\". The one demonstrated case of a failure record changing later work. | ✔ |\\n| **R43** | E02 ∥ harness memory | **parallel — a fifth register, outside git** | 8 files at `~/.claude/projects/C--Users-pjhud-local-26-nimoi/memory/`, 08-22 → 09-16, in exactly E03's shape (frontmatter + cross-cutting body + recurrence counts) and citing run-record deviation ids. **Invisible to git, to a re-org, and to every GPT session** (it is a Claude-Code-side store; `AGENTS.md` cannot reach it). | ✔ |\\n| **R44** | E05, E06 → E02 | depends-on | `processes/external_technical_assimilation_campaign_v0.1`–`v0.4` cite `degradation_001` as **trigger authority**. Deleting or re-homing that file without a forwarding pointer invalidates four process versions' trigger condition. | ✔ |\\n\\n## 7. Re-org notes\\n\\n**7a · Must move together.** The three `origins/` records + `procedures/failure_record.md` + the one\\nscheme-B record + `context/agent_introspection_session_satisfaction_2026-08-13.md` (the evidence\\n`debrief_001` is an account of). If the *practice* is to be consolidated, the four other registers\\n(§2 table) must move or be linked in the same operation, or consolidation will move four files and\\nleave 760 records behind.\\n\\n**7b · Must not be deleted / deduplicated / renamed.**\\n- `origins/degradation_001_2026-08-12.md` — **cited as trigger authority by five `processes/` versions**\\n  (R44). The most load-bearing file in E02 despite being the oldest. *(W03 consistency, 2026-09-20:\\n  \\\"five `processes/` versions\\\" here and in §9 Q5, against \\\"v0.1–v0.4\\\" in §6 — both count the same\\n  grep: **four process versions** (v0.1–v0.4, two citations each) **plus one mention in\\n  `processes/reference/…_history.md`** = five `processes/` *files*, four *versions* — Wave 02\\n  integrator check c3; R44.)*\\n- `campaigns/…/sandbox/DEVIATIONS.md` — 184 KB, **gitignored**, the only record of 42 spec deviations\\n  in E06's Phase 5. A backup-by-`git ls-files` loses it entirely (hazard H01's class). *(W03: ✗ — it is\\n  **tracked**; a backup by `git ls-files` **keeps** it. It stays on this must-not-delete list for what\\n  it records, not for a git exposure it does not have — `w03_audit_attack` A11; see §2.)*\\n- The harness memory store — not in the repository, not in any backup of it, and it holds the only\\n  written account of at least four environment hazards (R43).\\n- The 446 sandbox date-named look-alikes — E06 mutation-test corpus (H20).\\n\\n**7c · Regenerable or re-fetchable bulk.** None. Every E02 artifact is a one-off account of an event\\nthat cannot be re-run.\\n\\n**7d · Hard-wired paths.** `procedures/failure_record.md` mandates a **relative, area-scoped** path\\nshape (`<area>/reports/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>.md`), so re-homing any area silently changes where its\\nfuture failure records belong and orphans the existing one from its area. `failure_record.md` cites\\n`context/candidate_repos_areev_clanker_read_2026-08-26.md` and\\n`processes/procedure_deployment_entry.md` by path. `degradation_001` is cited by path from\\n`processes/` ×5, `campaigns/` ×13, `job/` ×2, `origins/` ×2, `context/` ×1.\\n\\n**7e · Misfiled material.** *Of this effort, elsewhere:* the entire live practice (§2, second table).\\n*Of other efforts, here:* nothing — E02's three files are small and genuinely E02's; their problem is\\nthat they sit inside E01's directory with no pointer of their own.\\n\\n**7f · Natural seams.** E02 **cannot** stand alone as filed: four files is not a register. The real\\nseam is the opposite one — a re-org could make E02 the *index* of the institution's failure memory\\nrather than its container: one `failure/` location holding the procedure, the four records, and a\\nstated map to the four external registers with their conventions and volumes. That requires deciding\\nscheme A vs scheme B first, and deciding whether the harness-memory store is inside or outside the\\ninstitution. Both are founder calls. **What must not happen is a re-org that files \\\"failure records\\\"\\nas a 4-file folder and thereby certifies that the institution recorded four failures in six weeks.**\\n\\n## 8. Record-integrity defects found\\n\\n1. **`mistakes_001`'s Provenance is wrong at the moment of writing** — names `onboarding_1.08.md` when\\n   1.10 was current, and says no pointer was added when one had been added (1.09, 22:42) and removed\\n   (1.10, 23:05) in the preceding 65 minutes. *Command:* `difflib` over 1.08/1.09/1.10 + mtimes.\\n2. **Scheme B has never been exercised outside one area.** *Command:* regex\\n   `(^|/)reports?/20\\\\d\\\\d-\\\\d\\\\d-\\\\d\\\\d[-_].*\\\\.md$` over `git ls-files` + `git ls-files --others\\n   --exclude-standard` for **both** repositories (9,787 + 19,317 paths) → **1 hit**; and an\\n   `os.walk` of the whole `nimoi/` filesystem (49,852 files, `candidate_repos/` excluded) for\\n   `^20\\\\d\\\\d-\\\\d\\\\d-\\\\d\\\\d[-_].*\\\\.md$` → 447 hits, **446 of them in `campaigns/…/sandbox/`**.\\n3. **Deviation numbering is per-run and therefore non-addressable.** Every run record restarts at\\n   `D1`. `virtues.md` cites \\\"run deviation D17\\\" and the `D-036`-style campaign ids in the same file\\n   with no namespace distinguishing them. Two of the four live registers use the token `D<n>` for\\n   incompatible things.\\n4. **Recurrence is counted but never promoted.** Run records self-count: *\\\"Fourteenth consecutive run\\n   with an orchestrator briefing error caught by agents\\\"* (necrozma, 09-12); *\\\"Twelfth consecutive\\n   run…\\\"* (mini-ork); *\\\"Third consecutive run this rule has failed\\\"* (mobius). **17 deviations are\\n   explicitly tagged `carried`** — recurring and unrepaired. The `record_audit_v4.1` \\\"domain routing\\n   while withholding the rubric\\\" defect is recorded as carried across **twelve** runs. None became a\\n   failure record or a general finding.\\n5. **`procedures/failure_record.md` is `State: directed` and listed in `procedures/INDEX.md`, yet\\n   `candidate_analysis/metrics` — the one area that used it — cites `procedures/` exactly once in\\n   3,299 files, and `processes/` zero times.** The procedure is deployed and effectively unused.\\n\\n## 9. Open questions\\n\\n1. **Which scheme wins?** Founder only. Scheme A is warm-referenced (23 + 14 inbound citations) but\\n   has no entry point; scheme B has an entry point and one record.\\n2. **Are run-record deviations failure records?** They satisfy most of scheme B's schema (symptom,\\n   root cause, resolution, verification) at a finer grain and higher volume. If yes, E02's home is\\n   `candidate_analysis/metrics/runs/` and the institution should say so. If no, 643 defects are\\n   outside the memory system by design and the institution should say *that*.\\n3. **Is the harness memory store part of NIMOI?** It is where the institution's environment knowledge\\n   actually went after 08-22. It is per-machine, per-harness, per-model-vendor, and unversioned.\\n   *(W03 consistency, 2026-09-20: the same question as **E03 §9 Q2**, asked from the other side; it is\\n   put to the founder once, as **FQ-38** — `w03_founder_questions`. Two facts since: the store holds\\n   **9** files now — the ninth written by the mapping effort's own session on 09-19 (H39) — and\\n   `nimoi-autosurvey` has a store of its own, 7 entries (H72).)*\\n4. **What happened to M-6?** `mistakes_001` records nine untrusted `CLAUDE.md` files inside the working\\n   tree as a **live unresolved exposure**. The 09-10 `seas` run then recorded (D8) the harness\\n   injecting a candidate repository's `CLAUDE.md` into a producer's context as if it were project\\n   instructions — i.e. **the exposure fired**, was recorded as a run deviation and in harness memory,\\n   and was never written back to M-6.\\n5. **Does `degradation_001` move?** Five `processes/` versions depend on it as a trigger authority.\\n\\n## 10. Verification ledger\\n\\n| Claim | Source (W01 §) | Status | How checked |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Two incompatible failure-record conventions exist | `w01_core_identity` §7.3 | **✔** | Read both in full; scheme B's path/schema vs the three `origins/` filenames |\\n| \\\"Neither document mentions the other\\\" | `w01_core_identity` §7.3 | **✔** | `failure_record.md` contains no `origins`/`debrief`/`degradation`/`mistakes`; `mistakes_001` contains `failure_record` ×0 |\\n| No record exists under scheme B other than the gate-3 one | assigned | **✔** | Two independent enumerations (git in both repos; `os.walk` of the filesystem) → 1 hit, 446 sandbox decoys |\\n| `failure_record.md` is v1, effective 08-26, state `directed` | `w01_core_identity` §4 E2 | **✔** | In-file header; mtime 08-26 14:30; added to git in `52a4f10` (08-31) |\\n| E02 is \\\"dormant and structurally orphaned\\\" | `w01_core_identity` §4 E2 | **◐ partly ✗** | Dormant ✔. \\\"Orphaned\\\" holds for `mistakes_001` (1 citer) but **not** for `degradation_001` (23 citers, incl. 5 processes as trigger authority) or `debrief_001` (14 citers) |\\n| \\\"Dozens\\\" of defects recorded as run deviations since 08-31 | `w01_core_identity` §8.3 / R29 | **✗ (understated)** | **643** across 60 run records (`## Deviations` section parse); 297 tagged instances; 17 tagged `carried` |\\n| Failures are also recorded in `sandbox/DEVIATIONS.md` | assigned | **✔** | 42 entries `D-01`…`D-42`, 184,423 B, 2,855 lines; gitignored *(W03: the ✔ certifies the counts — 70 `## D-` entries, highest D-42, 184,423 B all reproduce; ✗ the adjective: the file is **tracked** — `w03_audit_attack` D10)* |\\n| …in `hail_mary_2` | assigned | **✗** | No failure-record convention: one \\\"Caps / failures\\\" heading in 253 files (`work/runs/scan-cycle-1/report.md`) |\\n| …in autosurvey's `dev/` history | assigned | **✗** | Zero `Deviations`/`D-NN`/`Lessons` occurrences in 19,317 files. `dev/` is a *version* history (92 files: 43 procedure versions, 49 standards versions); failures ride in version bumps and 6 of 72 commit subjects |\\n| …in the session memory files | assigned | **✔ and material** | 8 files + `MEMORY.md`, 08-22 → 09-16, at `~/.claude/projects/C--Users-pjhud-local-26-nimoi/memory/`; frontmatter + recurrence counts + run-record `D<n>` citations |\\n| The campaign decision log is a fourth register | followed | **✔** | 76 distinct `D-001`…`D-076` across `campaigns/` non-sandbox `.md` files; `ledger.md` alone is 323,635 B |\\n| Fraction of run deviations meeting `general_findings/`'s admission test | assigned | **≈ 40–50%** | Systematic sample: every 20th of 485 extractable deviations (n = 25), hand-classified against \\\"would this still be true and useful in a piece of work that has nothing to do with where it was learned?\\\" → 11 clear yes, 2 borderline. See E03 §5 for the worked list |\\n\\n**Not looked at:** the body text of the 643 deviations beyond the 25-item sample and the 17 `carried`\\nentries; `campaigns/procedure_acquisition/ledger.md` in full (323 KB, E06's); the gate-3 record's\\nown eight sections in detail (E19's); `candidate_repos/` (prohibited, never touched).\"\n}"}],"origin":null}}}
