{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:19:32.583Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/000234","tag":"agent.owner.1"}
{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:19:32.589Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/000235","body":{"kind":"message","agent":"owner.1","turn":1,"direction":"to_agent","message":{"_type":"UserMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolResultBlock","tool_use_id":"toolu_01D2MLSKvBSYWXjFh9snmamU","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n \"start_line\": 1,\n \"end_line\": 272,\n \"total_lines\": 272,\n \"next_offset\": null,\n \"line_truncated\": false,\n \"sha256\": \"72ddabea99b2e1de1fb4c7c95e46399e827ae0eaca4ea06debd49108d501e2d1\",\n \"text\": \"# FOUNDER_QUESTIONS — 52 decisions only you can make\\n\\n*This is every question the map cannot answer for itself, merged from ~110 raised across the 26 effort files and three mapping waves. Written 2026-09-19 (Wave 03).*\\n**How to answer:** a word or a line each — \\\"paused\\\", \\\"abandoned\\\", \\\"yes\\\", \\\"later\\\", \\\"your call\\\" are all complete answers. Write them anywhere; nothing here asks you to do work at the keyboard.\\n**If you skip one, the stated default stands** and the map will be written that way. No default deletes anything, publishes anything, or runs anything, so skipping is always safe.\\n**If you answer only six,** make them **FQ-46 (are the `nimoi` and autosurvey GitHub remotes private? — it gates the rest)**, FQ-17 (push autosurvey), FQ-19 (what to commit), FQ-27 / FQ-47 (what is already public), FQ-01 (is the measurement loop over), FQ-25 (who owns the shared libraries). *(FQ-46–FQ-52 were added by the orchestrator on 2026-09-20, after the subproject scheme was merged; FQ-24, FQ-26 and FQ-30 were corrected the same day — each says how.)*\\nGroups: **A** what is finished vs paused · **B** protect before moving · **C** subprojects and what may be public · **D** repairs to the record · **E** small things · **F** seven added after the subproject scheme. The last two sections need nothing from you.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## A · State calls — finished, paused, or abandoned?\\n\\n*Every one of these decides whether a pile of files is a live working set (must stay reachable and keep its tools) or a closed record (can be frozen, moved and forgotten).*\\n\\n**FQ-01 · Is the five-hourly scanning loop over — and if it resumes, does it take the 23 unscanned clones or the 99 shortlisted repositories it cannot see?**\\nIt stopped 09-13 with no stop note, four days before its own expiry; it decides whether the 3,300-file measurement directory is a growing working set or a closed record.\\n*Default:* **closed as of 09-13; queue not resumed** (nothing deleted). · *Touches:* EMI index and suites (E19), clone corpus (E15), detection ranking (E14). · *Read:* `efforts/E19_emi_index_measurement_suites.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-02 · Is the instrument finished — is Suite 4.2 wanted, and is a v6 of the EMI index definition owed?**\\nNine Suite 4.2 proposals sit unowned; v5's canon is seven clauses you wrote, so only you can open a v6 — and the rubric is already public, so a v6 changes a published document.\\n*Default:* **no Suite 4.2, no v6; v5 and Suite 4.1 are the final instrument.** · *Touches:* EMI suites (E19), paradigm theory (E18). · *Read:* `efforts/E18_paradigm_theory.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-03 · Which survey draft is current, v5 or v6 — and do the 09-16 review's 11 recommended edits get applied, or are the drafts frozen at 09-08?**\\nTwo unreconciled drafts; a re-org that takes \\\"v6\\\" as latest by filename would quietly discard a live alternative. (Note: what is *published* is neither — it is the v2/v3 line, frozen 09-04.)\\n*Default:* **both frozen at 09-08, v6 marked \\\"latest file, not adjudicated\\\"; edits not applied.** · *Touches:* survey paper (E21), chart toolchain (E26). · *Read:* `efforts/E21_emi_paper_charts.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-04 · Did the outreach posts go out — to whom and when — and is peer contact still a live line of work?**\\nThree replies prove contact happened but nothing records sending; until it is settled the map must label this effort's state as unknown, and it is the effort most entangled with personal data.\\n*Default:* **contact happened via the public repository's Discussions only; the line is closed as of 09-06.** · *Touches:* outreach (E22), survey paper (E21). · *Read:* `efforts/E22_outreach_peer_contact.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-05 · Is the NLT ledger server parked or abandoned?**\\nIt was switched off in a deliberate, separately dated act on 08-29; it works, it is wired, its credential is still provisioned, and a public extraction of it exists — it is the cleanest single-subproject candidate in the estate.\\n*Default:* **parked, not abandoned** — kept whole, off, with its credential revoked (FQ-20). · *Touches:* NLT ledger (E07). · *Read:* `efforts/E07_nlt_ledger.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-06 · Is the procedure library's stage 2 to be deployed, rolled back, or declared a finished testbed experiment?**\\nThe library is stalled mid-deployment and its generator would now fail if run; everything about where `procedures/` goes hangs on this.\\n*Default:* **finished testbed experiment** — stage 1 frozen as the record, stage 2 not pursued. · *Touches:* procedure library (E04), the campaign that built it (E06). · *Read:* `efforts/E04_procedure_library_governance.md` §5\\n\\n**FQ-07 · Is the procedure-acquisition campaign to be closed formally now (and under process v0.14 or v1.0), or left open to its 2026-11-21 deadline — and who holds its 16 open liens?**\\n27,000 files, mostly unversioned, cannot be filed as \\\"record\\\" or \\\"working set\\\" until the campaign is open or shut.\\n*Default:* **left open on paper, treated as dormant**; liens unassigned; closes under v0.14 if closed. · *Touches:* campaign (E06), ETA process (E05), procedure library (E04). · *Read:* `efforts/E06_procedure_acquisition_campaign.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-08 · Is ETA still the institution's process for acquiring capability, given that three major builds bypassed it?**\\nIf yes, it is doctrine and belongs with the institution core; if no, it is a completed artifact and can be filed as history.\\n*Default:* **still the declared process, never re-used** — filed as doctrine, marked unexercised. · *Touches:* ETA process (E05), campaign (E06). · *Read:* `efforts/E05_eta_process.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-09 · Is the institution/ARPI scanning line retired for good, and should its open survey tickets be finished or retired?**\\nIts analysis method was superseded, but the mission is resumable by design and leaving partial reports unflagged in the record is the kind of defect NIMOI ranks above a failure.\\n*Default:* **retired; open tickets retired with a note, not finished.** · *Touches:* institution/ARPI scan (E11), step surveys (E17), paradigm theory (E18). · *Read:* `efforts/E11_institution_arpi_scan_hm2_harness.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-10 · Is the papers-harvest line finished — no third window — and is the ~4.7 GB of arXiv material across the two repositories archival?**\\nIt is the largest reclaimable disk in the estate, and \\\"archival\\\" vs \\\"parked\\\" decides whether the download tooling and its state files must keep working.\\n*Default:* **finished; both corpora archival, kept, not re-fetched, tooling frozen.** · *Touches:* papers harvest (E10), nimoi-autosurvey (E13). · *Read:* `efforts/E10_papers_harvest.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-11 · Is the next-generation design line live, superseded, or simply never read?**\\nIts two branches were written the same day and never reconciled; one of them is the only per-domain mechanism catalogue NIMOI has, and filing it as \\\"superseded\\\" would be a guess.\\n*Default:* **dormant, both branches kept as live alternatives; neither superseded.** · *Touches:* next-generation design (E08), comparison study (E20). · *Read:* `efforts/E08_nextgen_design.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-12 · Did `nimoi-autosurvey` owe a final synthesis stage, or was that synthesis executed inside `nimoi` under a different regime?**\\nThis decides whether the survey line is one effort spanning two repositories — i.e. whether they must become one subproject or can be split cleanly.\\n*Default:* **the synthesis happened in `nimoi`; autosurvey's last stage is not owed.** · *Touches:* nimoi-autosurvey (E13), paradigm theory (E18), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `efforts/E13_nimoi_autosurvey.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-13 · Is the ai-2026 story finished, paused, or abandoned?**\\nIt is a self-contained candidate for its own private subproject; the answer also settles which of two conflicting \\\"first run\\\" claims in its record is right.\\n*Default:* **paused, kept whole, nothing pruned.** · *Touches:* the story (E09), procedure library (E04, which indexes four of its procedures). · *Read:* `efforts/E09_story_ai2026.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-14 · Is the general-findings corpus abandoned, or has promoting findings into it simply never been anyone's job?**\\nNine findings against roughly 770 deviation entries elsewhere: if the corpus is the memory, the memory is nearly empty, and a re-org that files it as \\\"the memory\\\" files the smaller part.\\n*Default:* **not abandoned, unstaffed** — kept open, no promotion backlog assumed. · *Touches:* general findings (E03), failure records (E02), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `efforts/E03_general_findings.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-15 · Is the job-search line live or closed?**\\nIt did not stop on 08-23 as the map said: `applications/` runs to 08-24 with a second employer and résumés to v2.5 — and it is the least-protected work in the estate (FQ-18).\\n*Default:* **closed as of 08-24; kept private and backed up, not developed.** · *Touches:* job search and portfolio (E24). · *Read:* `directories/siblings.md` §`applications/`\\n\\n**FQ-16 · Three small state calls, a word each: does the portable \\\"survey craft\\\" package still have a job? Is a second edition of the 49-feature comparison wanted over the now-34 scored systems? And the one measured repository with a ledger but no card (`jarvis`) — finish it, stop-card it, or document it as incomplete?**\\nEach is a single stuck deliverable that otherwise gets filed as \\\"complete\\\" by default and quietly disappears.\\n*Default:* **no job / no second edition / documented as incomplete.** · *Touches:* legacy package (E12), comparison study (E20), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `efforts/E12_legacy_survey_package.md` §9\\n\\n---\\n\\n## B · Protect first — before anything moves\\n\\n*A gitignored subproject gets no protection from the parent's git. These are the things that exist on one disk today.*\\n\\n**FQ-17 · May `nimoi-autosurvey`'s 54 unpushed commits be pushed now?**\\nThe entire 15,072-repository survey record exists on one disk; any split or move risks it, and it is a one-command fix. Verified still 54 ahead today.\\n*Default:* **push blocked; the map will say loudly that this is unresolved.** · *Touches:* nimoi-autosurvey (E13) and everything downstream of the survey. · *Read:* `relationships/git_state.md`\\n\\n**FQ-18 · May `applications/` (290 MB, 2,236 files, no git, no remote, no backup) be backed up before anything else happens?**\\nIt is the only record of a second job target and a PDF toolchain that exists nowhere else; it is the single least-protected thing found anywhere in the estate.\\n*Default:* **back it up** (copy only; no repository created, nothing published). · *Touches:* job search (E24). · *Read:* `directories/siblings.md` §`applications/`\\n\\n**FQ-19 · Which untracked work gets committed before the re-org — all of it, or a named subset?**\\nUntracked today: the whole next-generation design, the comparison study, outreach, the AI-organizations study, most of the paper and chart toolchain, 47% of the EMI record including all 63 per-run tools, and the only record of nine clone deletions. Moving untracked files loses their history silently.\\n*Default:* **commit all of it, in one labelled commit per effort, before any move.** · *Touches:* E08, E19, E20, E21, E22, E23, E26, E15. · *Read:* `relationships/git_state.md`\\n\\n**FQ-20 · Is the `harness-prod` credential (and its two token files) to be revoked, or carried?**\\nThe same secrets now exist in two places on disk — including inside a repository you push — and they authorise six write prefixes for a harness that was never built. Only `.gitignore` keeps them off GitHub.\\n*Default:* **carried, unrevoked, and both copies flagged as a blocker on any public move.** · *Touches:* NLT ledger (E07). · *Read:* `directories/siblings.md` §Re-org cautions\\n\\n**FQ-21 · Should the campaign's sandbox, its runs and results, and `build/` come under version control?**\\nAbout 1,830 irreplaceable files are excluded by an ignore rule written before most of them existed; a subproject boundary would make that permanent.\\n*Default:* **left ignored, and listed as at-risk in the map.** · *Touches:* campaign (E06), procedure library (E04). · *Read:* `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` §H-A\\n\\n**FQ-22 · Should a `folder → origin → revision` manifest of the cloned-repository corpus be written before anything moves?**\\nThe corpus is the cleanest thing to excise from the tree, but without a manifest it cannot be re-created and the measurement records' pins cannot be checked; clone folder names also steer the scanner's pick order, so they are not free to rename.\\n*Default:* **write the manifest first** (a read-only listing; nothing is cloned, fetched or executed). · *Touches:* clone corpus (E15), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `directories/candidate_repos.md`\\n\\n**FQ-23 · The fetched-README stores — four in `harvest/` and autosurvey's 15,072 samples — freeze them, drop them, or accept that they drift?**\\nThey are the evidence base under thousands of verdicts, they are a 2026-08/09 snapshot, and the largest set is gitignored and drifting; re-fetching would invalidate every score.\\n*Default:* **frozen where they are, never re-fetched; the autosurvey set flagged as unprotected.** · *Touches:* institution scan (E11), nimoi-autosurvey (E13), gold harvest (E16). · *Read:* `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` §H-E\\n\\n**FQ-24 · Confirm the mechanics: each subproject is made from the working tree — in place, or by *moving* it, never by re-cloning — with git's text conversion switched *off* wherever checksum-bound records live, and gets its own remote?**\\nAbout 3,800 tracked files are CRLF on disk but LF inside git (machine-wide `core.autocrlf=true`, no `.gitattributes`), and NIMOI's checksums bind the bytes *on disk* — the 75 frozen review files, the EMI cards, 11 of the comparison study's 69 pinned sources. A fresh clone rewrites those bytes and breaks every such checksum. And a gitignored subproject with no remote has no backup at all.\\n*Default:* **yes to all three**; the map assumes every subproject needs a remote you will have to create. · *Touches:* all. · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` §8, `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` §H-A\\n*(Corrected 09-20 by the orchestrator: this question first said to copy the public ledger repository's `.gitattributes`. That file normalises text to LF — right for a repository with no byte-bound hashes, wrong here. Found by `w03_merge_subprojects`, re-checked.)*\\n\\n---\\n\\n## C · Subprojects and what may be public\\n\\n*The re-org's own design questions. The map can lay out options for every one of these; it cannot choose.*\\n\\n**FQ-25 · Where do the shared libraries go — the procedure library, `context/`, `from_chat/`, `references/` and the root tools — when each subproject gets its own git?**\\nThey belong to no one effort (the procedure library alone is shared by six, one root tool by twelve areas), so every boundary in the scheme depends on this one answer. Options: a parent-level shared library; duplicate frozen copies; or one owning subproject that the others point at.\\n*Default:* **they stay in the parent as a shared library, and subprojects reference them by pointer, not by path.** · *Touches:* E01, E04, E05, E06, E09, E10, E24 and every tool user. · *Read:* `relationships/root_tools.md`\\n\\n**FQ-26 · Does doctrine — `origins/`, onboarding, and the virtue register — live in the parent, or in an \\\"institution\\\" subproject of its own; and does the virtue register travel with doctrine or with the measurement suites that write to it?**\\nThe register is the only file both halves of NIMOI touch, 15 machine records embed its path, and 55% of it is uncommitted. *(Corrected 09-20: \\\"16\\\" → 15; and the map has since found that **no tracked file tells the scanning loop to write there** — the instruction lives in the scheduled-task prompt, outside both repositories — so moving the register breaks little mechanically, but no file can be edited to tell the loop where it went.)*\\n*Default:* **doctrine stays in the parent; the register stays with doctrine and the suites write to it across the boundary.** · *Touches:* doctrine (E01), failure records (E02), findings (E03), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `efforts/E01_constitution_onboarding_virtues.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-27 · The public `nimoi_samples` repository was published verbatim with no licence — sanitise it, licence it, or withdraw it?**\\nIt is world-readable today and carries your full name, NIMOI's name (212 times), the elder agency's name inside a copy of onboarding, an absolute local path, and a review protocol addressed to an AI reviewer — and with no licence file, no reuse is granted either. It is also the counter-example that the sanitisation standard has to be written against.\\n*Default:* **left exactly as it is**, and recorded in the map as an unresolved live exposure. · *Touches:* job search (E24), ETA process (E05), doctrine (E01). · *Read:* `directories/siblings.md` §`nimoi_samples/`\\n\\n**FQ-28 · Does the seven-project modular seed in your own design work govern this re-organisation, or is the re-org independent of it?**\\nIt is the only existing internal proposal for how NIMOI should be divided; if it governs, the sub-grouping must be checked against it rather than drawn fresh.\\n*Default:* **independent** — the seed is read as input and precedent, not as the specification. · *Touches:* next-generation design (E08). · *Read:* `efforts/E08_nextgen_design.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-29 · For each of the three public repositories, which side is authoritative — the public copy or the private original?**\\nAll three have diverged both ways: the public ledger holds four documents that exist nowhere privately; the public portfolio is a *later* edition than the private one; and the public survey's 0.3→0.4 editorial pass was never brought back, while the private drafts moved on to v4–v6. Two known blemishes ride on the same answer: the published figure plots 16 of 37 cards, and one published ledger file leaks an internal clone path.\\n*Default:* **private is authoritative everywhere; public-only material is pulled back into the map as \\\"public-only, unmerged\\\"; nothing republished, nothing corrected.** · *Touches:* NLT ledger (E07), EMI suites (E19), paper (E21), charts (E26), job search (E24). · *Read:* `directories/siblings.md`\\n\\n**FQ-30 · Do the untrusted cloned repositories stay inside the working tree?**\\nYou opened this yourself in the 08-26 mistakes record and nothing has closed it; the exposure has since fired once, and the re-org is the natural moment to move them out. It is also the cheapest large excision available.\\n*Default:* **they stay where they are for now — a gitignored quarantine at the parent level, with a manifest (FQ-22) and a marker file — and moving them out is a later, separate step.** The scanner's target picker and the ARPI pipeline both find the clones from the parent root, and the picker's memory of what has been scanned depends on it; moving the clones means re-pointing both first. · *Touches:* clone corpus (E15), failure records (E02), EMI suites (E19), gold harvest (E16). · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` (the quarantine rows), `directories/candidate_repos.md`\\n*(Corrected 09-20 by the orchestrator: the first default here was \\\"they move out of the tree\\\", which contradicted both subproject proposals and the merged scheme. The question is unchanged and still yours — \\\"move them out now\\\" remains a complete answer.)*\\n\\n**FQ-31 · One procedure regime for the whole family, or a federation in which each subproject keeps its own?**\\nThree regimes already operate side by side and only one is registered anywhere; the measurement suites have effectively seceded, and the size ceilings the library imposes are not applied to them or to autosurvey's products. This is the deepest design question in the map.\\n*Default:* **federation, stated openly** — each subproject declares its own regime; the library governs only the parent. · *Touches:* procedure library (E04), EMI suites (E19), gold harvest (E16), nimoi-autosurvey (E13). · *Read:* `relationships/themes.md` §T10\\n\\n**FQ-32 · Does the re-org honour `nimoi-autosurvey`'s own rebaseline clause, waive it in writing, or exempt that repository from the re-org?**\\nBy the repository's written standard, moving an operational product requires an exact sentence from you first; ignoring it would be the one rule-break the estate documents in advance.\\n*Default:* **the repository is exempt from the re-org for now** — pulled in as a subproject unchanged, no rebaseline triggered. · *Touches:* nimoi-autosurvey (E13), three-loop harness (E25). · *Read:* `efforts/E13_nimoi_autosurvey.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-33 · Is the third-party contacts folder to be retained at all?**\\nIt is tracked and committed and holds outside people's names, employers and professional assessments gathered from public profiles, plus one drafted message; retention is a decision only you can take, and it decides whether the whole outreach line can ever be public.\\n*Default:* **retained, private, and marked as a hard publication blocker.** · *Touches:* outreach (E22), detection ranking (E14). · *Read:* `efforts/E22_outreach_peer_contact.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-34 · Was committing fetched third-party content intended — and may any of it be redistributed in a public subproject?**\\n2,630 fetched documents are tracked, plus a 10.9 MB page committed against its own README's caveat, another collective's 56-file handbook, and extracted paper texts. 41 of them contain text addressed to a model reader. Republishing them is a licence question, not a tidiness question.\\n*Default:* **kept, never republished**; any subproject containing them is private until each source's terms are checked. · *Touches:* papers harvest (E10), institution scan (E11), detection (E14), AI-organizations study (E23), nimoi-autosurvey (E13). · *Read:* `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` §H-E\\n\\n**FQ-35 · Is the three-loop harness its own repository — and public?**\\nIt is the only unit in NIMOI that already states its own extraction boundary, has been extracted three times and ran for a month outside the parent with nothing depending on it inwards. Onboarding still promises a shared harness that does not exist, and one vendor SDK document is 76% of the bundle's bytes and is cited by nothing.\\n*Default:* **its own subproject, private**, with the SDK document left in place. · *Touches:* three-loop harness (E25), next-generation design (E08), nimoi-autosurvey (E13). · *Read:* `efforts/E25_three_loop_harness.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-36 · Do the personal areas — the job search, `applications/`, and `ignore/` — become one private subproject; and is onboarding's silence about them deliberate compartmentalisation?**\\nOnboarding has never named either folder in ten versions; if that is deliberate, it is already the public/private line you drew once by hand, and the re-org should simply formalise it.\\n*Default:* **yes — one private subproject, never published; the silence is read as deliberate.** · *Touches:* job search (E24), doctrine (E01). · *Read:* `efforts/E24_job_search_portfolio.md` §9\\n\\n---\\n\\n## D · Repairs to the record\\n\\n*NIMOI ranks a defect that corrupts the record above one that causes a failure. 122 are on file; these are the ones that need your ruling rather than an edit.*\\n\\n**FQ-37 · Which failure-record scheme wins — the warm-referenced one with no entry point, or the one with an entry point and a single record?**\\nBoth are dormant; \\\"the institution's primary product is its failures\\\" cannot be filed anywhere until one of them is the place.\\n*Default:* **the scheme with the entry point wins; the other is frozen and pointed at.** · *Touches:* failure records (E02), findings (E03), doctrine (E01). · *Read:* `efforts/E02_failure_records.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-38 · Are run-record deviations, the out-of-tree harness memory store, and defects found in institution-general tools part of the institution's memory — and should they be promoted into it?**\\nRoughly 770 such entries sit outside the memory system against four filed failure records and nine findings. \\\"Yes\\\" means the memory physically lives in the measurement records and in a per-machine cache outside both repositories, and the re-org must carry both. \\\"No\\\" means the institution is choosing to keep them out, which should be written down. Four effort files ask this from four sides.\\n*Default:* **no promotion; the map records that the institution's memory is de facto in the run records and the harness store, and says so.** · *Touches:* failure records (E02), findings (E03), EMI suites (E19), harness (E25), harvest (E10), detection (E14). · *Read:* `efforts/E02_failure_records.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-39 · Should the deleted general finding be restored (keeping its original creation date), and should the exposure that actually fired on 09-10 be written back into the 08-26 mistakes record, which still calls it unresolved?**\\nBoth are cases where the record says something the tree contradicts — the defect class NIMOI cares most about — and both are cheap and reversible.\\n*Default:* **neither** — both left as they are, with the discrepancy noted in the map. · *Touches:* findings (E03), failure records (E02), clone corpus (E15), gold harvest (E16). · *Read:* `relationships/record_defects.md`\\n\\n**FQ-40 · The five stale entry-point documents (including onboarding, which omits whole built subsystems): correct them, or freeze them with a correction banner?**\\nAny of them could become a new subproject's landing page, and each currently describes a project that no longer exists. NIMOI's own doctrine argues for a banner over a silent fix.\\n*Default:* **banner, not rewrite** — each gets a dated \\\"this is stale, see the map\\\" note when it moves. · *Touches:* doctrine (E01), procedure library (E04), legacy package (E12), step surveys (E17), nimoi-autosurvey (E13). · *Read:* `relationships/record_defects.md` §Fix-or-freeze\\n\\n**FQ-41 · Before the harness and the chart toolchain are cut loose, may the map declare which duplicate is canonical in three cases?**\\nFour copies of the harness bundle carry three different claims about which is authoritative; two different files are both named `build_emi_growth_v1.0.py`; and one measurement card was moved with no record across ten files that still cite it. Each sits exactly on a carve-out boundary.\\n*Default:* **the map declares the in-place original canonical in each case and records the others as copies**, changing nothing on disk. · *Touches:* harness (E25), chart toolchain (E26), legacy package (E12), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `relationships/record_defects.md` §Fix-or-freeze\\n\\n**FQ-42 · Three debts nobody has discharged — pay them or write them off? (a) the gold-harvest verification pass, named twice and done nowhere, whose grades the design work leans on; (b) the ranking that was adjudicated under the v4 definition while the paper reports that funnel and defines the paradigm by v5; (c) the outside critique of the virtue register, unanswered since 09-04.**\\nEach is an acknowledged hole in a document that something downstream treats as sound.\\n*Default:* **written off** — each marked \\\"owed, not done\\\" where it is cited. · *Touches:* gold harvest (E16), detection (E14), paradigm theory (E18), paper (E21), outreach (E22), doctrine (E01). · *Read:* `relationships/record_defects.md`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## E · Small things\\n\\n**FQ-43 · Five facts only you know, a phrase each:** what ended the overnight harness run at 12:05:56 on 08-29 (kill, sleep, closed terminal)? Where does the \\\"task-tracker\\\" harness it cites as its design precedent live? What happened to the clone that vanished from the corpus with no record? Was the first EMI index file edited on 09-02? And of the two parallel 09-11 model-governance sessions, which one is authoritative?\\nEach is a small hole that no amount of reading the tree can fill, and each currently forces a \\\"not knowable\\\" line in an effort file.\\n*Default:* **each recorded as permanently unknown.** · *Touches:* harness (E25), institution scan (E11), clone corpus (E15), paradigm theory (E18), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `waves/wave_02/digest_efforts_s9.md`\\n\\n**FQ-44 · Does anything outside these trees still exist that the map should know about — the pre-08-21 project home, and the chat transcripts holding two procedures' lost first versions?**\\nBoth would be primary records of work whose only surviving trace here is a citation; if they are gone, the map can stop saying \\\"recoverable\\\".\\n*Default:* **assumed gone; nothing is searched for outside the mapped trees.** · *Touches:* campaign (E06), procedure library (E04). · *Read:* `efforts/E06_procedure_acquisition_campaign.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-45 · Retention and orphans, a word each:** of 30 chart renderings across three corpora, which are records of a claim and which are debris? Do the visualization data set and the two \\\"special\\\" studies keep a purpose? And do three homeless documents (two in `references/`, one in `standards/`) belong to any effort at all?\\nThese are the files that a re-org will otherwise file by accident, into whichever folder they happen to sit in.\\n*Default:* **everything kept, nothing deleted**; orphans filed under the directory they sit in, marked homeless. · *Touches:* chart toolchain (E26), paper (E21), step surveys (E17), job search (E24), story (E09), design (E08). · *Read:* `efforts/E26_emi_chart_export_toolchain.md` §9\\n\\n---\\n\\n## F · Added at the end of Wave 03 (2026-09-20, by the orchestrator, from the merged subproject scheme)\\n\\n*These came out of `relationships/subprojects.md` §10 and the publication-blockers inventory after the 45 above were written. The first one gates most of group C.*\\n\\n**FQ-46 · Are the GitHub remotes of `nimoi` and `nimoi-autosurvey` private?**\\nNothing on disk records it. Every publication grade in the map assumes they are — and FQ-19 (commit the untracked work) and FQ-17 (push autosurvey) send more material to them.\\n*Default:* **assumed private; nothing new is pushed on the map's advice until you confirm.** · *Touches:* all. · *Read:* `relationships/publication_blockers.md`, `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` H70\\n\\n**FQ-47 · Three things already public that you may want to act on before any re-org — leave, fix, or withdraw?** (a) the public survey repository's ledgers contain about twenty email-address strings, most apparently belonging to authors of the surveyed projects; (b) `nimoi_samples` is public, unsanitised and unlicensed (FQ-27); (c) `nlt-ledger` was scrubbed in a later commit but never rewritten, so its first content commit still shows the pre-scrub text.\\n*Default:* **the map records the facts and changes nothing.** · *Touches:* EMI suites (E19), paper (E21), job portfolio (E24), ledger (E07). · *Read:* `relationships/publication_blockers.md` (\\\"already public\\\"), `directories/siblings.md`\\n\\n**FQ-48 · What are the `refs/codex/…` snapshots — record, backup, or debris?**\\n`nimoi/.git` holds 12 of them (the two public siblings hold 9 more): full working-tree snapshots written by Codex sessions. Locally they are the *only second copy* of the untracked design work, the comparison study and the contact folders; under a mirror push they would publish all of it.\\n*Default:* **kept, never mirror-pushed, and copied with `.git` in any backup.** · *Touches:* all. · *Read:* `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` H38, H76\\n\\n**FQ-49 · Which unit is the rehearsal — the first thing to be given its own git?**\\nCandidates the two proposals named: the three-loop harness (cleanest boundary, but it would be a *copy-out*, and which of its copies is the head is unclear), `nlt_ledger/` (an island, already has a public twin), `story/` (one tool dependency).\\n*Default:* **none chosen; the map lists criteria only.** · *Touches:* harness (E25), ledger (E07), story (E09). · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-50 · The three early-survey archives (`harvest/`, `hail_mary_2/`, `legacy_survey_material/`) — their own repositories, or left with the parent?**\\nThey are private and already committed either way. The case for separating them is that they hold 2,630 fetched third-party documents — 633 of them other projects' agent-instruction files — in the place every session starts. The case against: they still reach into the parent's procedures and findings.\\n*Default:* **left with the parent in the first stage.** · *Touches:* E10, E11, E12, E16. · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` §3a, §10\\n\\n**FQ-51 · When `nimoi-autosurvey` is pulled in: whole, or split into its record (≈150 MB) and its re-fetchable stores (≈3.7 GB)? And are sessions working inside an adopted repository onboarded into NIMOI, or does it keep its own entry contract?**\\nIt has its own standards, its own agent instructions, and its own out-of-repository memory store, which moving it will detach.\\n*Default:* **whole, moved not re-cloned, keeping its own entry contract, with a pointer in the parent's registry.** · *Touches:* autosurvey (E13), detection (E14), harness (E25). · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` §5 (G06), `efforts/E13_nimoi_autosurvey.md`\\n\\n**FQ-52 · May `candidate_analysis/contacts/` (tables about named third parties) be moved out before `candidate_analysis/` gets its first commit as its own repository?**\\nOnce it is in a new repository's history it is there for good; today it sits in `nimoi`'s.\\n*Default:* **yes — moved to the paper/outreach side first, with a receipt** (and see FQ-33 on whether it is retained at all). · *Touches:* outreach (E22), EMI study (G08). · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` §5 (G08)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Already answered — nothing needed from you\\n\\n**By your directives** (`method/founder_directives.md` D4–D6, 2026-09-19):\\n- *May the map read the four sibling directories?* → D4.1: yes, read-only. Done; it answered four of the questions below.\\n- *What is the re-org actually for?* → D4.2: `nimoi/` becomes a parent of gitignored subprojects, each with its own git, some public and some private. This reframed roughly a dozen \\\"where should this live?\\\" questions into the per-subproject questions in group C.\\n- *Keep 24 efforts, or split the harness out of the scan and the chart toolchain out of the paper?* → D4.3: split both (now E25 and E26), and add a grouping level between the two spines and the efforts. Applied.\\n\\n**By the map's own work since the questions were written:**\\n- *What is in the public ledger repository?* → the MIT-licensed public extraction of the ledger server, 8 commits, in sync; nothing in `nimoi/` names it. No elder-agency material is in it (its elder documents are in an ignored folder).\\n- *What is in the public survey repository?* → the published post, its evidence pack, a CC BY 4.0 licence, a Discussions form and two outside replies; 39 of its 44 files are byte-identical to files in `nimoi/`.\\n- *Was the paper ever posted with the growth chart?* → yes: that chart has been Figure 1 of the public README since 09-04, byte-identical to the private copy, and is recorded nowhere inside `nimoi/`.\\n- *Does the public Discussions board hold the missing half of the outreach effort?* → partly: the exchange-venue charter was published as the Discussions category form on 09-06, five minutes after it was drafted, and two counterparty replies live there.\\n- *Was a second job candidate ever pursued?* → yes: `applications/` holds a second target brief and résumés through v2.5, to 08-24.\\n- *Were four measurement runs missing their register lines?* → the claim rested on a refuted date range; the run receipts account for all of them.\\n- *Were four survey reports left unflagged as partial?* → refuted: there are seven, and all seven flag themselves.\\n\\n## Questions the map could answer itself with more work — not for you\\n\\nRecorded here so nobody re-asks them of the founder: where the root tools should live (a tools census exists); whether the chart toolchain groups with the suites or with the paper (the two blind subproject proposals will recommend); whether the two doctrine primers can leave `origins/` without breaking links (a link check); whether the story's four procedure entries need stubs if it moves (re-org design); whether the design work mentions the story (one search); the crosswalk between the two convergence schemes; the migration table from the proposed ledger family to the six things already called a ledger; whether the trigger-authority record must move with the five process versions that cite it; whether the duplicate harness copy in autosurvey is deletable; which effort owns the 08-26 mistakes record; whether the protocol document should be listed as a job-search location; which of the two parallel governance sessions was run on which vendor's model; and the rule that a move must carry the corrective receipts rather than the four wrong ones.\"\n}"}],"is_error":null}],"uuid":"938fce1c-1c42-4078-8502-c6b367423b55","parent_tool_use_id":null,"tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n \"start_line\": 1,\n \"end_line\": 272,\n \"total_lines\": 272,\n \"next_offset\": null,\n \"line_truncated\": false,\n \"sha256\": \"72ddabea99b2e1de1fb4c7c95e46399e827ae0eaca4ea06debd49108d501e2d1\",\n \"text\": \"# FOUNDER_QUESTIONS — 52 decisions only you can make\\n\\n*This is every question the map cannot answer for itself, merged from ~110 raised across the 26 effort files and three mapping waves. Written 2026-09-19 (Wave 03).*\\n**How to answer:** a word or a line each — \\\"paused\\\", \\\"abandoned\\\", \\\"yes\\\", \\\"later\\\", \\\"your call\\\" are all complete answers. Write them anywhere; nothing here asks you to do work at the keyboard.\\n**If you skip one, the stated default stands** and the map will be written that way. No default deletes anything, publishes anything, or runs anything, so skipping is always safe.\\n**If you answer only six,** make them **FQ-46 (are the `nimoi` and autosurvey GitHub remotes private? — it gates the rest)**, FQ-17 (push autosurvey), FQ-19 (what to commit), FQ-27 / FQ-47 (what is already public), FQ-01 (is the measurement loop over), FQ-25 (who owns the shared libraries). *(FQ-46–FQ-52 were added by the orchestrator on 2026-09-20, after the subproject scheme was merged; FQ-24, FQ-26 and FQ-30 were corrected the same day — each says how.)*\\nGroups: **A** what is finished vs paused · **B** protect before moving · **C** subprojects and what may be public · **D** repairs to the record · **E** small things · **F** seven added after the subproject scheme. The last two sections need nothing from you.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## A · State calls — finished, paused, or abandoned?\\n\\n*Every one of these decides whether a pile of files is a live working set (must stay reachable and keep its tools) or a closed record (can be frozen, moved and forgotten).*\\n\\n**FQ-01 · Is the five-hourly scanning loop over — and if it resumes, does it take the 23 unscanned clones or the 99 shortlisted repositories it cannot see?**\\nIt stopped 09-13 with no stop note, four days before its own expiry; it decides whether the 3,300-file measurement directory is a growing working set or a closed record.\\n*Default:* **closed as of 09-13; queue not resumed** (nothing deleted). · *Touches:* EMI index and suites (E19), clone corpus (E15), detection ranking (E14). · *Read:* `efforts/E19_emi_index_measurement_suites.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-02 · Is the instrument finished — is Suite 4.2 wanted, and is a v6 of the EMI index definition owed?**\\nNine Suite 4.2 proposals sit unowned; v5's canon is seven clauses you wrote, so only you can open a v6 — and the rubric is already public, so a v6 changes a published document.\\n*Default:* **no Suite 4.2, no v6; v5 and Suite 4.1 are the final instrument.** · *Touches:* EMI suites (E19), paradigm theory (E18). · *Read:* `efforts/E18_paradigm_theory.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-03 · Which survey draft is current, v5 or v6 — and do the 09-16 review's 11 recommended edits get applied, or are the drafts frozen at 09-08?**\\nTwo unreconciled drafts; a re-org that takes \\\"v6\\\" as latest by filename would quietly discard a live alternative. (Note: what is *published* is neither — it is the v2/v3 line, frozen 09-04.)\\n*Default:* **both frozen at 09-08, v6 marked \\\"latest file, not adjudicated\\\"; edits not applied.** · *Touches:* survey paper (E21), chart toolchain (E26). · *Read:* `efforts/E21_emi_paper_charts.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-04 · Did the outreach posts go out — to whom and when — and is peer contact still a live line of work?**\\nThree replies prove contact happened but nothing records sending; until it is settled the map must label this effort's state as unknown, and it is the effort most entangled with personal data.\\n*Default:* **contact happened via the public repository's Discussions only; the line is closed as of 09-06.** · *Touches:* outreach (E22), survey paper (E21). · *Read:* `efforts/E22_outreach_peer_contact.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-05 · Is the NLT ledger server parked or abandoned?**\\nIt was switched off in a deliberate, separately dated act on 08-29; it works, it is wired, its credential is still provisioned, and a public extraction of it exists — it is the cleanest single-subproject candidate in the estate.\\n*Default:* **parked, not abandoned** — kept whole, off, with its credential revoked (FQ-20). · *Touches:* NLT ledger (E07). · *Read:* `efforts/E07_nlt_ledger.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-06 · Is the procedure library's stage 2 to be deployed, rolled back, or declared a finished testbed experiment?**\\nThe library is stalled mid-deployment and its generator would now fail if run; everything about where `procedures/` goes hangs on this.\\n*Default:* **finished testbed experiment** — stage 1 frozen as the record, stage 2 not pursued. · *Touches:* procedure library (E04), the campaign that built it (E06). · *Read:* `efforts/E04_procedure_library_governance.md` §5\\n\\n**FQ-07 · Is the procedure-acquisition campaign to be closed formally now (and under process v0.14 or v1.0), or left open to its 2026-11-21 deadline — and who holds its 16 open liens?**\\n27,000 files, mostly unversioned, cannot be filed as \\\"record\\\" or \\\"working set\\\" until the campaign is open or shut.\\n*Default:* **left open on paper, treated as dormant**; liens unassigned; closes under v0.14 if closed. · *Touches:* campaign (E06), ETA process (E05), procedure library (E04). · *Read:* `efforts/E06_procedure_acquisition_campaign.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-08 · Is ETA still the institution's process for acquiring capability, given that three major builds bypassed it?**\\nIf yes, it is doctrine and belongs with the institution core; if no, it is a completed artifact and can be filed as history.\\n*Default:* **still the declared process, never re-used** — filed as doctrine, marked unexercised. · *Touches:* ETA process (E05), campaign (E06). · *Read:* `efforts/E05_eta_process.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-09 · Is the institution/ARPI scanning line retired for good, and should its open survey tickets be finished or retired?**\\nIts analysis method was superseded, but the mission is resumable by design and leaving partial reports unflagged in the record is the kind of defect NIMOI ranks above a failure.\\n*Default:* **retired; open tickets retired with a note, not finished.** · *Touches:* institution/ARPI scan (E11), step surveys (E17), paradigm theory (E18). · *Read:* `efforts/E11_institution_arpi_scan_hm2_harness.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-10 · Is the papers-harvest line finished — no third window — and is the ~4.7 GB of arXiv material across the two repositories archival?**\\nIt is the largest reclaimable disk in the estate, and \\\"archival\\\" vs \\\"parked\\\" decides whether the download tooling and its state files must keep working.\\n*Default:* **finished; both corpora archival, kept, not re-fetched, tooling frozen.** · *Touches:* papers harvest (E10), nimoi-autosurvey (E13). · *Read:* `efforts/E10_papers_harvest.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-11 · Is the next-generation design line live, superseded, or simply never read?**\\nIts two branches were written the same day and never reconciled; one of them is the only per-domain mechanism catalogue NIMOI has, and filing it as \\\"superseded\\\" would be a guess.\\n*Default:* **dormant, both branches kept as live alternatives; neither superseded.** · *Touches:* next-generation design (E08), comparison study (E20). · *Read:* `efforts/E08_nextgen_design.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-12 · Did `nimoi-autosurvey` owe a final synthesis stage, or was that synthesis executed inside `nimoi` under a different regime?**\\nThis decides whether the survey line is one effort spanning two repositories — i.e. whether they must become one subproject or can be split cleanly.\\n*Default:* **the synthesis happened in `nimoi`; autosurvey's last stage is not owed.** · *Touches:* nimoi-autosurvey (E13), paradigm theory (E18), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `efforts/E13_nimoi_autosurvey.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-13 · Is the ai-2026 story finished, paused, or abandoned?**\\nIt is a self-contained candidate for its own private subproject; the answer also settles which of two conflicting \\\"first run\\\" claims in its record is right.\\n*Default:* **paused, kept whole, nothing pruned.** · *Touches:* the story (E09), procedure library (E04, which indexes four of its procedures). · *Read:* `efforts/E09_story_ai2026.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-14 · Is the general-findings corpus abandoned, or has promoting findings into it simply never been anyone's job?**\\nNine findings against roughly 770 deviation entries elsewhere: if the corpus is the memory, the memory is nearly empty, and a re-org that files it as \\\"the memory\\\" files the smaller part.\\n*Default:* **not abandoned, unstaffed** — kept open, no promotion backlog assumed. · *Touches:* general findings (E03), failure records (E02), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `efforts/E03_general_findings.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-15 · Is the job-search line live or closed?**\\nIt did not stop on 08-23 as the map said: `applications/` runs to 08-24 with a second employer and résumés to v2.5 — and it is the least-protected work in the estate (FQ-18).\\n*Default:* **closed as of 08-24; kept private and backed up, not developed.** · *Touches:* job search and portfolio (E24). · *Read:* `directories/siblings.md` §`applications/`\\n\\n**FQ-16 · Three small state calls, a word each: does the portable \\\"survey craft\\\" package still have a job? Is a second edition of the 49-feature comparison wanted over the now-34 scored systems? And the one measured repository with a ledger but no card (`jarvis`) — finish it, stop-card it, or document it as incomplete?**\\nEach is a single stuck deliverable that otherwise gets filed as \\\"complete\\\" by default and quietly disappears.\\n*Default:* **no job / no second edition / documented as incomplete.** · *Touches:* legacy package (E12), comparison study (E20), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `efforts/E12_legacy_survey_package.md` §9\\n\\n---\\n\\n## B · Protect first — before anything moves\\n\\n*A gitignored subproject gets no protection from the parent's git. These are the things that exist on one disk today.*\\n\\n**FQ-17 · May `nimoi-autosurvey`'s 54 unpushed commits be pushed now?**\\nThe entire 15,072-repository survey record exists on one disk; any split or move risks it, and it is a one-command fix. Verified still 54 ahead today.\\n*Default:* **push blocked; the map will say loudly that this is unresolved.** · *Touches:* nimoi-autosurvey (E13) and everything downstream of the survey. · *Read:* `relationships/git_state.md`\\n\\n**FQ-18 · May `applications/` (290 MB, 2,236 files, no git, no remote, no backup) be backed up before anything else happens?**\\nIt is the only record of a second job target and a PDF toolchain that exists nowhere else; it is the single least-protected thing found anywhere in the estate.\\n*Default:* **back it up** (copy only; no repository created, nothing published). · *Touches:* job search (E24). · *Read:* `directories/siblings.md` §`applications/`\\n\\n**FQ-19 · Which untracked work gets committed before the re-org — all of it, or a named subset?**\\nUntracked today: the whole next-generation design, the comparison study, outreach, the AI-organizations study, most of the paper and chart toolchain, 47% of the EMI record including all 63 per-run tools, and the only record of nine clone deletions. Moving untracked files loses their history silently.\\n*Default:* **commit all of it, in one labelled commit per effort, before any move.** · *Touches:* E08, E19, E20, E21, E22, E23, E26, E15. · *Read:* `relationships/git_state.md`\\n\\n**FQ-20 · Is the `harness-prod` credential (and its two token files) to be revoked, or carried?**\\nThe same secrets now exist in two places on disk — including inside a repository you push — and they authorise six write prefixes for a harness that was never built. Only `.gitignore` keeps them off GitHub.\\n*Default:* **carried, unrevoked, and both copies flagged as a blocker on any public move.** · *Touches:* NLT ledger (E07). · *Read:* `directories/siblings.md` §Re-org cautions\\n\\n**FQ-21 · Should the campaign's sandbox, its runs and results, and `build/` come under version control?**\\nAbout 1,830 irreplaceable files are excluded by an ignore rule written before most of them existed; a subproject boundary would make that permanent.\\n*Default:* **left ignored, and listed as at-risk in the map.** · *Touches:* campaign (E06), procedure library (E04). · *Read:* `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` §H-A\\n\\n**FQ-22 · Should a `folder → origin → revision` manifest of the cloned-repository corpus be written before anything moves?**\\nThe corpus is the cleanest thing to excise from the tree, but without a manifest it cannot be re-created and the measurement records' pins cannot be checked; clone folder names also steer the scanner's pick order, so they are not free to rename.\\n*Default:* **write the manifest first** (a read-only listing; nothing is cloned, fetched or executed). · *Touches:* clone corpus (E15), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `directories/candidate_repos.md`\\n\\n**FQ-23 · The fetched-README stores — four in `harvest/` and autosurvey's 15,072 samples — freeze them, drop them, or accept that they drift?**\\nThey are the evidence base under thousands of verdicts, they are a 2026-08/09 snapshot, and the largest set is gitignored and drifting; re-fetching would invalidate every score.\\n*Default:* **frozen where they are, never re-fetched; the autosurvey set flagged as unprotected.** · *Touches:* institution scan (E11), nimoi-autosurvey (E13), gold harvest (E16). · *Read:* `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` §H-E\\n\\n**FQ-24 · Confirm the mechanics: each subproject is made from the working tree — in place, or by *moving* it, never by re-cloning — with git's text conversion switched *off* wherever checksum-bound records live, and gets its own remote?**\\nAbout 3,800 tracked files are CRLF on disk but LF inside git (machine-wide `core.autocrlf=true`, no `.gitattributes`), and NIMOI's checksums bind the bytes *on disk* — the 75 frozen review files, the EMI cards, 11 of the comparison study's 69 pinned sources. A fresh clone rewrites those bytes and breaks every such checksum. And a gitignored subproject with no remote has no backup at all.\\n*Default:* **yes to all three**; the map assumes every subproject needs a remote you will have to create. · *Touches:* all. · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` §8, `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` §H-A\\n*(Corrected 09-20 by the orchestrator: this question first said to copy the public ledger repository's `.gitattributes`. That file normalises text to LF — right for a repository with no byte-bound hashes, wrong here. Found by `w03_merge_subprojects`, re-checked.)*\\n\\n---\\n\\n## C · Subprojects and what may be public\\n\\n*The re-org's own design questions. The map can lay out options for every one of these; it cannot choose.*\\n\\n**FQ-25 · Where do the shared libraries go — the procedure library, `context/`, `from_chat/`, `references/` and the root tools — when each subproject gets its own git?**\\nThey belong to no one effort (the procedure library alone is shared by six, one root tool by twelve areas), so every boundary in the scheme depends on this one answer. Options: a parent-level shared library; duplicate frozen copies; or one owning subproject that the others point at.\\n*Default:* **they stay in the parent as a shared library, and subprojects reference them by pointer, not by path.** · *Touches:* E01, E04, E05, E06, E09, E10, E24 and every tool user. · *Read:* `relationships/root_tools.md`\\n\\n**FQ-26 · Does doctrine — `origins/`, onboarding, and the virtue register — live in the parent, or in an \\\"institution\\\" subproject of its own; and does the virtue register travel with doctrine or with the measurement suites that write to it?**\\nThe register is the only file both halves of NIMOI touch, 15 machine records embed its path, and 55% of it is uncommitted. *(Corrected 09-20: \\\"16\\\" → 15; and the map has since found that **no tracked file tells the scanning loop to write there** — the instruction lives in the scheduled-task prompt, outside both repositories — so moving the register breaks little mechanically, but no file can be edited to tell the loop where it went.)*\\n*Default:* **doctrine stays in the parent; the register stays with doctrine and the suites write to it across the boundary.** · *Touches:* doctrine (E01), failure records (E02), findings (E03), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `efforts/E01_constitution_onboarding_virtues.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-27 · The public `nimoi_samples` repository was published verbatim with no licence — sanitise it, licence it, or withdraw it?**\\nIt is world-readable today and carries your full name, NIMOI's name (212 times), the elder agency's name inside a copy of onboarding, an absolute local path, and a review protocol addressed to an AI reviewer — and with no licence file, no reuse is granted either. It is also the counter-example that the sanitisation standard has to be written against.\\n*Default:* **left exactly as it is**, and recorded in the map as an unresolved live exposure. · *Touches:* job search (E24), ETA process (E05), doctrine (E01). · *Read:* `directories/siblings.md` §`nimoi_samples/`\\n\\n**FQ-28 · Does the seven-project modular seed in your own design work govern this re-organisation, or is the re-org independent of it?**\\nIt is the only existing internal proposal for how NIMOI should be divided; if it governs, the sub-grouping must be checked against it rather than drawn fresh.\\n*Default:* **independent** — the seed is read as input and precedent, not as the specification. · *Touches:* next-generation design (E08). · *Read:* `efforts/E08_nextgen_design.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-29 · For each of the three public repositories, which side is authoritative — the public copy or the private original?**\\nAll three have diverged both ways: the public ledger holds four documents that exist nowhere privately; the public portfolio is a *later* edition than the private one; and the public survey's 0.3→0.4 editorial pass was never brought back, while the private drafts moved on to v4–v6. Two known blemishes ride on the same answer: the published figure plots 16 of 37 cards, and one published ledger file leaks an internal clone path.\\n*Default:* **private is authoritative everywhere; public-only material is pulled back into the map as \\\"public-only, unmerged\\\"; nothing republished, nothing corrected.** · *Touches:* NLT ledger (E07), EMI suites (E19), paper (E21), charts (E26), job search (E24). · *Read:* `directories/siblings.md`\\n\\n**FQ-30 · Do the untrusted cloned repositories stay inside the working tree?**\\nYou opened this yourself in the 08-26 mistakes record and nothing has closed it; the exposure has since fired once, and the re-org is the natural moment to move them out. It is also the cheapest large excision available.\\n*Default:* **they stay where they are for now — a gitignored quarantine at the parent level, with a manifest (FQ-22) and a marker file — and moving them out is a later, separate step.** The scanner's target picker and the ARPI pipeline both find the clones from the parent root, and the picker's memory of what has been scanned depends on it; moving the clones means re-pointing both first. · *Touches:* clone corpus (E15), failure records (E02), EMI suites (E19), gold harvest (E16). · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` (the quarantine rows), `directories/candidate_repos.md`\\n*(Corrected 09-20 by the orchestrator: the first default here was \\\"they move out of the tree\\\", which contradicted both subproject proposals and the merged scheme. The question is unchanged and still yours — \\\"move them out now\\\" remains a complete answer.)*\\n\\n**FQ-31 · One procedure regime for the whole family, or a federation in which each subproject keeps its own?**\\nThree regimes already operate side by side and only one is registered anywhere; the measurement suites have effectively seceded, and the size ceilings the library imposes are not applied to them or to autosurvey's products. This is the deepest design question in the map.\\n*Default:* **federation, stated openly** — each subproject declares its own regime; the library governs only the parent. · *Touches:* procedure library (E04), EMI suites (E19), gold harvest (E16), nimoi-autosurvey (E13). · *Read:* `relationships/themes.md` §T10\\n\\n**FQ-32 · Does the re-org honour `nimoi-autosurvey`'s own rebaseline clause, waive it in writing, or exempt that repository from the re-org?**\\nBy the repository's written standard, moving an operational product requires an exact sentence from you first; ignoring it would be the one rule-break the estate documents in advance.\\n*Default:* **the repository is exempt from the re-org for now** — pulled in as a subproject unchanged, no rebaseline triggered. · *Touches:* nimoi-autosurvey (E13), three-loop harness (E25). · *Read:* `efforts/E13_nimoi_autosurvey.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-33 · Is the third-party contacts folder to be retained at all?**\\nIt is tracked and committed and holds outside people's names, employers and professional assessments gathered from public profiles, plus one drafted message; retention is a decision only you can take, and it decides whether the whole outreach line can ever be public.\\n*Default:* **retained, private, and marked as a hard publication blocker.** · *Touches:* outreach (E22), detection ranking (E14). · *Read:* `efforts/E22_outreach_peer_contact.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-34 · Was committing fetched third-party content intended — and may any of it be redistributed in a public subproject?**\\n2,630 fetched documents are tracked, plus a 10.9 MB page committed against its own README's caveat, another collective's 56-file handbook, and extracted paper texts. 41 of them contain text addressed to a model reader. Republishing them is a licence question, not a tidiness question.\\n*Default:* **kept, never republished**; any subproject containing them is private until each source's terms are checked. · *Touches:* papers harvest (E10), institution scan (E11), detection (E14), AI-organizations study (E23), nimoi-autosurvey (E13). · *Read:* `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` §H-E\\n\\n**FQ-35 · Is the three-loop harness its own repository — and public?**\\nIt is the only unit in NIMOI that already states its own extraction boundary, has been extracted three times and ran for a month outside the parent with nothing depending on it inwards. Onboarding still promises a shared harness that does not exist, and one vendor SDK document is 76% of the bundle's bytes and is cited by nothing.\\n*Default:* **its own subproject, private**, with the SDK document left in place. · *Touches:* three-loop harness (E25), next-generation design (E08), nimoi-autosurvey (E13). · *Read:* `efforts/E25_three_loop_harness.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-36 · Do the personal areas — the job search, `applications/`, and `ignore/` — become one private subproject; and is onboarding's silence about them deliberate compartmentalisation?**\\nOnboarding has never named either folder in ten versions; if that is deliberate, it is already the public/private line you drew once by hand, and the re-org should simply formalise it.\\n*Default:* **yes — one private subproject, never published; the silence is read as deliberate.** · *Touches:* job search (E24), doctrine (E01). · *Read:* `efforts/E24_job_search_portfolio.md` §9\\n\\n---\\n\\n## D · Repairs to the record\\n\\n*NIMOI ranks a defect that corrupts the record above one that causes a failure. 122 are on file; these are the ones that need your ruling rather than an edit.*\\n\\n**FQ-37 · Which failure-record scheme wins — the warm-referenced one with no entry point, or the one with an entry point and a single record?**\\nBoth are dormant; \\\"the institution's primary product is its failures\\\" cannot be filed anywhere until one of them is the place.\\n*Default:* **the scheme with the entry point wins; the other is frozen and pointed at.** · *Touches:* failure records (E02), findings (E03), doctrine (E01). · *Read:* `efforts/E02_failure_records.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-38 · Are run-record deviations, the out-of-tree harness memory store, and defects found in institution-general tools part of the institution's memory — and should they be promoted into it?**\\nRoughly 770 such entries sit outside the memory system against four filed failure records and nine findings. \\\"Yes\\\" means the memory physically lives in the measurement records and in a per-machine cache outside both repositories, and the re-org must carry both. \\\"No\\\" means the institution is choosing to keep them out, which should be written down. Four effort files ask this from four sides.\\n*Default:* **no promotion; the map records that the institution's memory is de facto in the run records and the harness store, and says so.** · *Touches:* failure records (E02), findings (E03), EMI suites (E19), harness (E25), harvest (E10), detection (E14). · *Read:* `efforts/E02_failure_records.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-39 · Should the deleted general finding be restored (keeping its original creation date), and should the exposure that actually fired on 09-10 be written back into the 08-26 mistakes record, which still calls it unresolved?**\\nBoth are cases where the record says something the tree contradicts — the defect class NIMOI cares most about — and both are cheap and reversible.\\n*Default:* **neither** — both left as they are, with the discrepancy noted in the map. · *Touches:* findings (E03), failure records (E02), clone corpus (E15), gold harvest (E16). · *Read:* `relationships/record_defects.md`\\n\\n**FQ-40 · The five stale entry-point documents (including onboarding, which omits whole built subsystems): correct them, or freeze them with a correction banner?**\\nAny of them could become a new subproject's landing page, and each currently describes a project that no longer exists. NIMOI's own doctrine argues for a banner over a silent fix.\\n*Default:* **banner, not rewrite** — each gets a dated \\\"this is stale, see the map\\\" note when it moves. · *Touches:* doctrine (E01), procedure library (E04), legacy package (E12), step surveys (E17), nimoi-autosurvey (E13). · *Read:* `relationships/record_defects.md` §Fix-or-freeze\\n\\n**FQ-41 · Before the harness and the chart toolchain are cut loose, may the map declare which duplicate is canonical in three cases?**\\nFour copies of the harness bundle carry three different claims about which is authoritative; two different files are both named `build_emi_growth_v1.0.py`; and one measurement card was moved with no record across ten files that still cite it. Each sits exactly on a carve-out boundary.\\n*Default:* **the map declares the in-place original canonical in each case and records the others as copies**, changing nothing on disk. · *Touches:* harness (E25), chart toolchain (E26), legacy package (E12), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `relationships/record_defects.md` §Fix-or-freeze\\n\\n**FQ-42 · Three debts nobody has discharged — pay them or write them off? (a) the gold-harvest verification pass, named twice and done nowhere, whose grades the design work leans on; (b) the ranking that was adjudicated under the v4 definition while the paper reports that funnel and defines the paradigm by v5; (c) the outside critique of the virtue register, unanswered since 09-04.**\\nEach is an acknowledged hole in a document that something downstream treats as sound.\\n*Default:* **written off** — each marked \\\"owed, not done\\\" where it is cited. · *Touches:* gold harvest (E16), detection (E14), paradigm theory (E18), paper (E21), outreach (E22), doctrine (E01). · *Read:* `relationships/record_defects.md`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## E · Small things\\n\\n**FQ-43 · Five facts only you know, a phrase each:** what ended the overnight harness run at 12:05:56 on 08-29 (kill, sleep, closed terminal)? Where does the \\\"task-tracker\\\" harness it cites as its design precedent live? What happened to the clone that vanished from the corpus with no record? Was the first EMI index file edited on 09-02? And of the two parallel 09-11 model-governance sessions, which one is authoritative?\\nEach is a small hole that no amount of reading the tree can fill, and each currently forces a \\\"not knowable\\\" line in an effort file.\\n*Default:* **each recorded as permanently unknown.** · *Touches:* harness (E25), institution scan (E11), clone corpus (E15), paradigm theory (E18), EMI suites (E19). · *Read:* `waves/wave_02/digest_efforts_s9.md`\\n\\n**FQ-44 · Does anything outside these trees still exist that the map should know about — the pre-08-21 project home, and the chat transcripts holding two procedures' lost first versions?**\\nBoth would be primary records of work whose only surviving trace here is a citation; if they are gone, the map can stop saying \\\"recoverable\\\".\\n*Default:* **assumed gone; nothing is searched for outside the mapped trees.** · *Touches:* campaign (E06), procedure library (E04). · *Read:* `efforts/E06_procedure_acquisition_campaign.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-45 · Retention and orphans, a word each:** of 30 chart renderings across three corpora, which are records of a claim and which are debris? Do the visualization data set and the two \\\"special\\\" studies keep a purpose? And do three homeless documents (two in `references/`, one in `standards/`) belong to any effort at all?\\nThese are the files that a re-org will otherwise file by accident, into whichever folder they happen to sit in.\\n*Default:* **everything kept, nothing deleted**; orphans filed under the directory they sit in, marked homeless. · *Touches:* chart toolchain (E26), paper (E21), step surveys (E17), job search (E24), story (E09), design (E08). · *Read:* `efforts/E26_emi_chart_export_toolchain.md` §9\\n\\n---\\n\\n## F · Added at the end of Wave 03 (2026-09-20, by the orchestrator, from the merged subproject scheme)\\n\\n*These came out of `relationships/subprojects.md` §10 and the publication-blockers inventory after the 45 above were written. The first one gates most of group C.*\\n\\n**FQ-46 · Are the GitHub remotes of `nimoi` and `nimoi-autosurvey` private?**\\nNothing on disk records it. Every publication grade in the map assumes they are — and FQ-19 (commit the untracked work) and FQ-17 (push autosurvey) send more material to them.\\n*Default:* **assumed private; nothing new is pushed on the map's advice until you confirm.** · *Touches:* all. · *Read:* `relationships/publication_blockers.md`, `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` H70\\n\\n**FQ-47 · Three things already public that you may want to act on before any re-org — leave, fix, or withdraw?** (a) the public survey repository's ledgers contain about twenty email-address strings, most apparently belonging to authors of the surveyed projects; (b) `nimoi_samples` is public, unsanitised and unlicensed (FQ-27); (c) `nlt-ledger` was scrubbed in a later commit but never rewritten, so its first content commit still shows the pre-scrub text.\\n*Default:* **the map records the facts and changes nothing.** · *Touches:* EMI suites (E19), paper (E21), job portfolio (E24), ledger (E07). · *Read:* `relationships/publication_blockers.md` (\\\"already public\\\"), `directories/siblings.md`\\n\\n**FQ-48 · What are the `refs/codex/…` snapshots — record, backup, or debris?**\\n`nimoi/.git` holds 12 of them (the two public siblings hold 9 more): full working-tree snapshots written by Codex sessions. Locally they are the *only second copy* of the untracked design work, the comparison study and the contact folders; under a mirror push they would publish all of it.\\n*Default:* **kept, never mirror-pushed, and copied with `.git` in any backup.** · *Touches:* all. · *Read:* `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` H38, H76\\n\\n**FQ-49 · Which unit is the rehearsal — the first thing to be given its own git?**\\nCandidates the two proposals named: the three-loop harness (cleanest boundary, but it would be a *copy-out*, and which of its copies is the head is unclear), `nlt_ledger/` (an island, already has a public twin), `story/` (one tool dependency).\\n*Default:* **none chosen; the map lists criteria only.** · *Touches:* harness (E25), ledger (E07), story (E09). · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-50 · The three early-survey archives (`harvest/`, `hail_mary_2/`, `legacy_survey_material/`) — their own repositories, or left with the parent?**\\nThey are private and already committed either way. The case for separating them is that they hold 2,630 fetched third-party documents — 633 of them other projects' agent-instruction files — in the place every session starts. The case against: they still reach into the parent's procedures and findings.\\n*Default:* **left with the parent in the first stage.** · *Touches:* E10, E11, E12, E16. · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` §3a, §10\\n\\n**FQ-51 · When `nimoi-autosurvey` is pulled in: whole, or split into its record (≈150 MB) and its re-fetchable stores (≈3.7 GB)? And are sessions working inside an adopted repository onboarded into NIMOI, or does it keep its own entry contract?**\\nIt has its own standards, its own agent instructions, and its own out-of-repository memory store, which moving it will detach.\\n*Default:* **whole, moved not re-cloned, keeping its own entry contract, with a pointer in the parent's registry.** · *Touches:* autosurvey (E13), detection (E14), harness (E25). · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` §5 (G06), `efforts/E13_nimoi_autosurvey.md`\\n\\n**FQ-52 · May `candidate_analysis/contacts/` (tables about named third parties) be moved out before `candidate_analysis/` gets its first commit as its own repository?**\\nOnce it is in a new repository's history it is there for good; today it sits in `nimoi`'s.\\n*Default:* **yes — moved to the paper/outreach side first, with a receipt** (and see FQ-33 on whether it is retained at all). · *Touches:* outreach (E22), EMI study (G08). · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` §5 (G08)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Already answered — nothing needed from you\\n\\n**By your directives** (`method/founder_directives.md` D4–D6, 2026-09-19):\\n- *May the map read the four sibling directories?* → D4.1: yes, read-only. Done; it answered four of the questions below.\\n- *What is the re-org actually for?* → D4.2: `nimoi/` becomes a parent of gitignored subprojects, each with its own git, some public and some private. This reframed roughly a dozen \\\"where should this live?\\\" questions into the per-subproject questions in group C.\\n- *Keep 24 efforts, or split the harness out of the scan and the chart toolchain out of the paper?* → D4.3: split both (now E25 and E26), and add a grouping level between the two spines and the efforts. Applied.\\n\\n**By the map's own work since the questions were written:**\\n- *What is in the public ledger repository?* → the MIT-licensed public extraction of the ledger server, 8 commits, in sync; nothing in `nimoi/` names it. No elder-agency material is in it (its elder documents are in an ignored folder).\\n- *What is in the public survey repository?* → the published post, its evidence pack, a CC BY 4.0 licence, a Discussions form and two outside replies; 39 of its 44 files are byte-identical to files in `nimoi/`.\\n- *Was the paper ever posted with the growth chart?* → yes: that chart has been Figure 1 of the public README since 09-04, byte-identical to the private copy, and is recorded nowhere inside `nimoi/`.\\n- *Does the public Discussions board hold the missing half of the outreach effort?* → partly: the exchange-venue charter was published as the Discussions category form on 09-06, five minutes after it was drafted, and two counterparty replies live there.\\n- *Was a second job candidate ever pursued?* → yes: `applications/` holds a second target brief and résumés through v2.5, to 08-24.\\n- *Were four measurement runs missing their register lines?* → the claim rested on a refuted date range; the run receipts account for all of them.\\n- *Were four survey reports left unflagged as partial?* → refuted: there are seven, and all seven flag themselves.\\n\\n## Questions the map could answer itself with more work — not for you\\n\\nRecorded here so nobody re-asks them of the founder: where the root tools should live (a tools census exists); whether the chart toolchain groups with the suites or with the paper (the two blind subproject proposals will recommend); whether the two doctrine primers can leave `origins/` without breaking links (a link check); whether the story's four procedure entries need stubs if it moves (re-org design); whether the design work mentions the story (one search); the crosswalk between the two convergence schemes; the migration table from the proposed ledger family to the six things already called a ledger; whether the trigger-authority record must move with the five process versions that cite it; whether the duplicate harness copy in autosurvey is deletable; which effort owns the 08-26 mistakes record; whether the protocol document should be listed as a job-search location; which of the two parallel governance sessions was run on which vendor's model; and the rule that a move must carry the corrective receipts rather than the four wrong ones.\"\n}"}],"origin":null}}}
