{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:19:59.195Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/000435","body":{"kind":"codex_rpc","agent":"owner.2","turn":1,"direction":"from_codex","rpc":"rawResponseItem/completed","rpc_id":null,"message":{"method":"rawResponseItem/completed","params":{"threadId":"01a0ee2d-9fad-7f31-a203-ab008d6683f2","turnId":"01a0ee2d-a1db-7190-8b90-ba922ad2767b","item":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0ee2e-2eda-7211-a7dc-4912b95f5365","call_id":"call_qPnYNq9m9J7JgcOOxrq36dd1","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## /nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E01_constitution_onboarding_virtues.md (282)"},{"type":"input_text","text":"1: # E01 · Constitution, onboarding & virtue register\n5: ## 1. What it is\n22: ## 2. Where it lives\n53: ## 3. How it works\n100: ## 4. Timeline\n123: ## 5. State and unfinished business\n139: ## 6. Relationships\n152: ## 7. Re-org notes\n205: ## 8. Record-integrity defects found\n236: ## 9. Open questions\n259: ## 10. Verification ledger"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## /nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E02_failure_records.md (250)"},{"type":"input_text","text":"1: # E02 · Failure records\n6: ## 1. What it is\n24: ## 2. Where it lives\n36: ### Where failures are actually recorded (the R29 thread, followed)\n53: ## 3. How it works\n95: ## 4. Timeline\n115: ## 5. State and unfinished business\n129: ## 6. Relationships\n141: ## 7. Re-org notes\n186: ## 8. Record-integrity defects found\n210: ## 9. Open questions\n231: ## 10. Verification ledger"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## /nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E03_general_findings.md (300)"},{"type":"input_text","text":"1: # E03 · General-findings corpus\n17: ## 1. What it is\n35: ## 2. Where it lives\n62: ## 3. How it works\n102: ## 4. Timeline\n120: ## 5. State and unfinished business\n133: ### What is accumulating where the corpus does not look\n168: ## 6. Relationships\n180: ## 7. Re-org notes\n221: ## 8. Record-integrity defects found\n258: ## 9. Open questions\n278: ## 10. Verification ledger"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## /nimoi_mapping_project/relationships/subprojects.md (457)"},{"type":"input_text","text":"1: # Subprojects — sub-groups `G01`–`G09`, and how each could be realised on disk\n16: ## 1 · The criterion, and the two levels\n49: ## 2 · The sub-groups (allocated by the merge directive §2 — A's nine, two placements from B: M3, M4)\n70: ## 3 · Realisation\n72: ### 3a · Stage 1 — zero-move (A; M2). Each row reads \"if this location is kept as, or made, the stated pattern, then it holds …\"\n116: ### 3b · Stage 2 — optional gatherings, one sub-group at a time, each \"moved with receipt\", each passing §1's four tests\n131: ## 4 · Visibility (M9) — every work subproject is private; \"public\" means a publication subproject\n155: ## 5 · What crosses each boundary (both proposals' (c), merged and de-duplicated)\n160: ### G01 · Charter & memory — in Stage 1 the parent, so these are the crossings between the parent and everything else\n172: ### G02 · Method engineering — library half in the parent commons; `campaigns/` a P1 subproject\n184: ### G03 · Platform — `nlt_ledger/` P1 · E08 parent-resident · E25 a resident of `hail_mary_2/` and of `nimoi-autosurvey/`\n198: ### G04 · Story — `story/` P1\n208: ### G05 · Personal — `job/` P1; `applications/` and `nimoi_samples/` adopted. Inbound citations: none (E24 §7f)\n218: ### G06 · Field survey — `nimoi-autosurvey/` adopted; `harvest/`, `hail_mary_2/`, `legacy_survey_material/` P1 (or P0); E14 housed in `candidate_analysis/`\n234: ### G07 · Corpus first reads — co-housed (E17 in `candidate_analysis/`, E16 in `harvest/candidate_gold/`)\n247: ### G08 · EMI study — `candidate_analysis/` P1 + the parent-level quarantine; E26 a resident of `paper/`\n265: ### G09 · Paper & outreach — `paper/` P1; `emi-survey/` its (and G08's) publication subproject\n277: ## 6 · The shared libraries (M7, M8)\n306: ## 7 · What stays in the parent (M11 — the union of both)\n326: ## 8 · Git and history (M10)\n355: ## 9 · Sequence — constraints, not a schedule (M12)\n379: ## 10 · Open choices for the founder (M13) — de-duplicated against `../FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md`\n401: ## 11 · Against NIMOI's own seven-project seed (M14)\n424: ## 12 · What came from where"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## /nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md (272)"},{"type":"input_text","text":"1: # FOUNDER_QUESTIONS — 52 decisions only you can make\n11: ## A · State calls — finished, paused, or abandoned?\n81: ## B · Protect first — before anything moves\n120: ## C · Subprojects and what may be public\n175: ## D · Repairs to the record\n205: ## E · Small things\n221: ## F · Added at the end of Wave 03 (2026-09-20, by the orchestrator, from the merged subproject scheme)\n254: ## Already answered — nothing needed from you\n270: ## Questions the map could answer itself with more work — not for you"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0ee2d-a1db-7190-8b90-ba922ad2767b","create_time":1790702399.194242}}},"emittedAtMs":1790702399194}}}
