{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:22:29.081Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/000755","tag":"agent.owner.1.1"}
{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:22:29.087Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/000756","body":{"kind":"message","agent":"owner.1.1","turn":1,"direction":"to_agent","message":{"_type":"UserMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolResultBlock","tool_use_id":"toolu_01S1okHuU6AMfdH3DxvqeLo8","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/MAP.md\",\n \"start_line\": 1,\n \"end_line\": 131,\n \"total_lines\": 131,\n \"next_offset\": null,\n \"line_truncated\": false,\n \"sha256\": \"4f3bc738b71be6f4aa713f9c0c7124eeb8f4f8055921e1227beeb93cc99fa96e\",\n \"text\": \"# MAP — the NIMOI map report\\n\\n*ROOT 1 of 2. The other root is `CONTINUE.md` (state of the mapping effort itself).\\n**Last updated: 2026-09-20, after Wave 03.** Three waves: by location (14 agents) → by effort, with\\nverification (10 agents; 303 claims verified, 90 refuted or sharpened) → audit, siblings and the\\nre-org target (12 agents). A blind adversarial reader then tried to break 104 of the map's claims:\\n**84 held, 6 were refuted, 11 were imprecise** — all since corrected; the errors were in words like\\n*never / only / tracked*, not in counts. Refuted claims are annotated in place, never silently\\noverwritten. **This is a catalogue of what exists and where — not evidence that any of it works, and\\nit decides nothing.** Before acting on any git-state claim, read it from git per file.*\\n\\n## What NIMOI is\\n\\nNIMOI (\\\"Necessity Is Mother Of Invention\\\", named 2026-08-10) is the Hudgins family's persistent,\\nmulti-model AI \\\"general agency\\\": an institution defined as its artifacts, worked by disposable Claude\\nand GPT sessions. Its declared primary purpose is to evolve methods for stabilising a persistent,\\nself-modifying AI institution by analysing its own real failures; everything else it does is\\ndeliberately unscoped *load*. In six weeks (2026-08-09 → 09-16) it produced ~50,000 files in `nimoi/`,\\n~91,000 in the sibling `nimoi-autosurvey/`, three small **public** repositories and one private\\napplications folder. What it is *about*, in twelve themes: `relationships/themes.md`.\\n\\n**Its shape is a chronology with one change of regime.** First the institution's own machinery\\n(08-09 → 08-28): a fiction project as first workload, a self-upgrade campaign and the process that ran\\nit, a procedure library, a ledger inherited from an elder agency, a job portfolio built from all of it.\\nThen looking outward (from 08-20): a papers harvest and GitHub scans, a sibling repository that\\nmachine-checked 15,072 repositories, a corpus of cloned systems, a named paradigm (**EMI**), a\\nmeasurement index with five generations of scanning suites, a comparison study, a paper, outreach — and\\nthe findings turned back on NIMOI as a design. The early outward work still fed the institution's\\nprocedures and findings; **after about 08-30 it runs on its own regimes and feeds nothing back** except\\nlines in the virtue register. No outside contact has ever changed NIMOI's doctrine.\\n\\n## Start here — by task\\n\\n| If you want to … | Open |\\n|---|---|\\n| know what must be protected **before anything moves**, and what disk could be reclaimed | `relationships/protection_and_volume.md` |\\n| see the proposed **sub-groups and subprojects** (the re-org target), what crosses each boundary, and the order constraints | `relationships/subprojects.md` |\\n| know **what may be public**, what blocks the rest, and **what is already public** | `relationships/publication_blockers.md` · `directories/siblings.md` |\\n| answer the questions only the founder can answer (52, each with a default) | `FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md` |\\n| find one effort: state, every location, re-org notes (§7), open questions | `efforts/INDEX.md` → `efforts/E##_*.md` |\\n| find out **what is in a directory** and which efforts share it | `directories/INDEX.md` |\\n| see what breaks if something moves (85 hazards) | `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` |\\n| see how efforts feed, copy and supersede one another (103 relationships); where an effort is smeared | `relationships/effort_graph.md` · `relationships/spaghetti.md` |\\n| find stale or wrong documents inside NIMOI (122 record defects) | `relationships/record_defects.md` |\\n| know which tool reads or writes what, and which are hard-wired | `relationships/tools_census.md` · `relationships/root_tools.md` |\\n| know what `candidate_repos/` is without opening it | `directories/candidate_repos.md` |\\n| continue the mapping, or check how it was made | `CONTINUE.md` |\\n\\n## The 26 efforts, in nine sub-groups\\n\\nFull table — state, dates, home, export potential, file: `efforts/INDEX.md`.\\n\\n| Sub-group | Efforts | In a line |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **G01 Charter & memory** | E01 constitution, onboarding, virtue register · E02 failure records · E03 general findings | doctrine frozen 08-26; the register still written to (55% uncommitted); failure memory dormant while ~770 deviations pile up elsewhere |\\n| **G02 Method engineering** | E04 procedure library & governance · E05 assimilation (ETA) process · E06 procedure-acquisition campaign | one cluster in eight places; stalled at deployment stage 1; 27K files, ≈1,780 irreplaceable ones outside git |\\n| **G03 Platform** | E07 NLT ledger · E08 next-generation design · E25 three-loop harness | ledger shelved (its public twin `nlt-ledger` has diverged); design untracked; harness lives on as a port in autosurvey |\\n| **G04 Story** | E09 ai-2026 scenario & governed-revision method | dormant since 08-17; the cleanest self-contained unit |\\n| **G05 Personal** | E24 job search & portfolio | `job/` dormant; continued in `applications/` (no git, no backup); portfolio public, unsanitised, unlicensed |\\n| **G06 Field survey** | E10 papers harvest · E11 institution/ARPI scan · E12 survey-craft package · E13 `nimoi-autosurvey` · E14 detection & ranking | one effort in five instalments across two repositories; autosurvey 54 commits unpushed; ≈5.7 GB re-fetchable |\\n| **G07 Corpus first reads** | E16 gold harvest · E17 step-1/2 surveys | completed / superseded; by NIMOI's own rule the later suites may not read them |\\n| **G08 EMI study** | E15 candidate corpus · E18 paradigm theory · E19 EMI index & suites · E20 comparison study · E26 chart & export toolchain | the live centre: loop stopped 09-13, 23 clones + 99 shortlisted repositories to go; 47% untracked |\\n| **G09 Paper & outreach** | E21 survey paper · E22 outreach & peer contact · E23 AI-organizations study | drafts v5/v6 unreconciled; what is *published* is the v3 line; replies on record, sending not |\\n\\n**The proposed scheme, in five lines** (`relationships/subprojects.md` — a proposal; it decides\\nnothing): a sub-group is *membership*, a repository is *housing*, and they need not coincide. **Stage 1\\nmoves no files**: existing top-level directories get their own git in place and the parent ignores\\nthem; the parent *is* the charter plus the shared libraries, a registry of subprojects, the map, and a\\ngitignored quarantine for the clones. Every working subproject is private; **\\\"public\\\" means a separate\\nexport repository** — which is what the three existing public siblings already are. Siblings are\\nadopted by moving the directory, never by re-cloning. Gatherings and cuts come later, one at a time,\\neach \\\"moved with receipt\\\". Two blind proposals on different models converged on this.\\n\\n## Ten things to know before re-organising\\n\\n1. **Back up, push and decide what to commit — first.** Back up both repositories *with* `.git` and\\n   ignored files. `nimoi-autosurvey` is 54 commits ahead of its remote. `applications/` and this map\\n   have no git at all. `nimoi` holds 151 MB of untracked real work (47% of the measurement record, the\\n   comparison study, the design line, most of `paper/`) and ≈1,780 irreplaceable ignored campaign\\n   files, `build/`, the ARPI run log, 679 harvest judgement files, the ledger's run evidence.\\n   → `relationships/protection_and_volume.md`\\n2. **Make new repositories from the working tree, with text conversion off; never re-clone, never\\n   filter history.** ~3,800 tracked files are CRLF on disk and LF in git, and NIMOI's checksums bind\\n   the bytes on disk. Do **not** copy `nlt-ledger`'s `.gitattributes` — it normalises to LF.\\n   `.git` also holds 12 Codex working-tree snapshots (incl. contact folders): keep them in backups,\\n   never mirror-push. → `reorg_hazards.md` H41, H74, H82, H38\\n3. **Neither `git ls-files` nor the filesystem is a safe list of \\\"the project\\\".** One omits ~2,000\\n   real files; the other includes ~40,000 ignored fixtures and downloads, ~7,000 of them verbatim,\\n   unlabelled copies of live or former project files. → `spaghetti.md` S10\\n4. **Most duplication is deliberate evidence** — portfolio freezes with hash claims, a declared mirror,\\n   mutation-test *bundles* (keep whole), a mandated harness fork, five parallel ledger implementations.\\n   Do not dedupe by name or hash. → `reorg_hazards.md` H-C\\n5. **Tools are hard-wired to where they sit.** Root tools compute paths from their own location; three\\n   read campaign files and the campaign reads `procedures/` back; all 63 per-run tools and the target\\n   picker are untracked; the comparison study holds ≈6,950 absolute links; chart builders import\\n   predecessors by path; the scanner finds the clones from the parent root (never strip a clone's\\n   `.git`). → `reorg_hazards.md` H-B, `tools_census.md`\\n6. **Three clusters are smeared, and directory names describe the first thing put there.** E04–E06 in\\n   eight places; the survey in five instalments across two repositories whose seam neither declares;\\n   paper-side work under `metrics/` and `origins/`. `candidate_analysis/` holds 8 efforts, `origins/` 5,\\n   `paper/` 4, `harvest/` 3, `hail_mary_2/` 3; the root is an unindexed bin of 11 tools and 11 scratch\\n   files. → `spaghetti.md`, `directories/INDEX.md`\\n7. **Words are overloaded** — *ledger* ×7, *harness* ×7, *procedure* ×4, *reference* ×5, *contacts* ×3,\\n   *findings* ×4 — and NIMOI's own entry points are stale: onboarding names 7 of 23 directories and\\n   omits whole built subsystems; five indexes misstate their own directory. → `naming_collisions.md`,\\n   `record_defects.md`\\n8. **Untrusted text is not confined to `candidate_repos/`.** 2,630 fetched third-party documents are\\n   git-tracked — **633 of them other projects' `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md`** — plus detection READMEs, a\\n   10.9 MB HTML, `paper/readmes/`, an external handbook. The one recorded exposure (M-6) fired on 09-10.\\n   → `reorg_hazards.md` H-E\\n9. **The institution's stated product — its failures — is not where its memory looks.** ~770 deviation\\n   and memory entries sit in run records, a campaign sandbox log, a campaign ledger and two harness\\n   memory stores *outside the repositories*, against four filed failure records and nine findings.\\n   → `efforts/E02_failure_records.md`\\n10. **Some of NIMOI is already public, and nothing inside `nimoi/` says so.** Three public repositories\\n    carry the ledger, the portfolio, and the survey with its cards, ledgers, chart, candidate list and\\n    forum; all three have diverged from their private originals in both directions. One is unsanitised\\n    and unlicensed; one was scrubbed only at its tip; one's ledgers carry third parties' email strings.\\n    **Whether the `nimoi` remote itself is public is recorded nowhere** — every publication grade in\\n    this map assumes it is private (FQ-46). → `directories/siblings.md`, `publication_blockers.md`\\n\\n## Go deeper\\n\\n| Level | What | Where |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| L1 | the 26 efforts (slim; paragraphs in `INDEX_detailed.md`) | `efforts/INDEX.md` |\\n| L1 | every directory of all six trees | `directories/INDEX.md` |\\n| L1 | relationships R01–R103 · tangles S01–S12 · hazards H01–H85 · sub-groups G01–G09 · themes T01–T12 · git state · timeline · coupling matrix · name collisions | `relationships/INDEX.md` |\\n| L1 | the founder's instructions, verbatim (D1–D6) | `method/founder_directives.md` |\\n| L2 | one file per effort, each ending in a verification ledger | `efforts/E##_*.md` |\\n| L3 | how the map was made: plans, agent reports, change logs, syntheses; tool outputs | `CONTINUE.md` → `waves/`, `evidence/` |\"\n}"}],"is_error":null}],"uuid":"509781b8-e072-4ade-9096-44e195af791d","parent_tool_use_id":null,"tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/MAP.md\",\n \"start_line\": 1,\n \"end_line\": 131,\n \"total_lines\": 131,\n \"next_offset\": null,\n \"line_truncated\": false,\n \"sha256\": \"4f3bc738b71be6f4aa713f9c0c7124eeb8f4f8055921e1227beeb93cc99fa96e\",\n \"text\": \"# MAP — the NIMOI map report\\n\\n*ROOT 1 of 2. The other root is `CONTINUE.md` (state of the mapping effort itself).\\n**Last updated: 2026-09-20, after Wave 03.** Three waves: by location (14 agents) → by effort, with\\nverification (10 agents; 303 claims verified, 90 refuted or sharpened) → audit, siblings and the\\nre-org target (12 agents). A blind adversarial reader then tried to break 104 of the map's claims:\\n**84 held, 6 were refuted, 11 were imprecise** — all since corrected; the errors were in words like\\n*never / only / tracked*, not in counts. Refuted claims are annotated in place, never silently\\noverwritten. **This is a catalogue of what exists and where — not evidence that any of it works, and\\nit decides nothing.** Before acting on any git-state claim, read it from git per file.*\\n\\n## What NIMOI is\\n\\nNIMOI (\\\"Necessity Is Mother Of Invention\\\", named 2026-08-10) is the Hudgins family's persistent,\\nmulti-model AI \\\"general agency\\\": an institution defined as its artifacts, worked by disposable Claude\\nand GPT sessions. Its declared primary purpose is to evolve methods for stabilising a persistent,\\nself-modifying AI institution by analysing its own real failures; everything else it does is\\ndeliberately unscoped *load*. In six weeks (2026-08-09 → 09-16) it produced ~50,000 files in `nimoi/`,\\n~91,000 in the sibling `nimoi-autosurvey/`, three small **public** repositories and one private\\napplications folder. What it is *about*, in twelve themes: `relationships/themes.md`.\\n\\n**Its shape is a chronology with one change of regime.** First the institution's own machinery\\n(08-09 → 08-28): a fiction project as first workload, a self-upgrade campaign and the process that ran\\nit, a procedure library, a ledger inherited from an elder agency, a job portfolio built from all of it.\\nThen looking outward (from 08-20): a papers harvest and GitHub scans, a sibling repository that\\nmachine-checked 15,072 repositories, a corpus of cloned systems, a named paradigm (**EMI**), a\\nmeasurement index with five generations of scanning suites, a comparison study, a paper, outreach — and\\nthe findings turned back on NIMOI as a design. The early outward work still fed the institution's\\nprocedures and findings; **after about 08-30 it runs on its own regimes and feeds nothing back** except\\nlines in the virtue register. No outside contact has ever changed NIMOI's doctrine.\\n\\n## Start here — by task\\n\\n| If you want to … | Open |\\n|---|---|\\n| know what must be protected **before anything moves**, and what disk could be reclaimed | `relationships/protection_and_volume.md` |\\n| see the proposed **sub-groups and subprojects** (the re-org target), what crosses each boundary, and the order constraints | `relationships/subprojects.md` |\\n| know **what may be public**, what blocks the rest, and **what is already public** | `relationships/publication_blockers.md` · `directories/siblings.md` |\\n| answer the questions only the founder can answer (52, each with a default) | `FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md` |\\n| find one effort: state, every location, re-org notes (§7), open questions | `efforts/INDEX.md` → `efforts/E##_*.md` |\\n| find out **what is in a directory** and which efforts share it | `directories/INDEX.md` |\\n| see what breaks if something moves (85 hazards) | `relationships/reorg_hazards.md` |\\n| see how efforts feed, copy and supersede one another (103 relationships); where an effort is smeared | `relationships/effort_graph.md` · `relationships/spaghetti.md` |\\n| find stale or wrong documents inside NIMOI (122 record defects) | `relationships/record_defects.md` |\\n| know which tool reads or writes what, and which are hard-wired | `relationships/tools_census.md` · `relationships/root_tools.md` |\\n| know what `candidate_repos/` is without opening it | `directories/candidate_repos.md` |\\n| continue the mapping, or check how it was made | `CONTINUE.md` |\\n\\n## The 26 efforts, in nine sub-groups\\n\\nFull table — state, dates, home, export potential, file: `efforts/INDEX.md`.\\n\\n| Sub-group | Efforts | In a line |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **G01 Charter & memory** | E01 constitution, onboarding, virtue register · E02 failure records · E03 general findings | doctrine frozen 08-26; the register still written to (55% uncommitted); failure memory dormant while ~770 deviations pile up elsewhere |\\n| **G02 Method engineering** | E04 procedure library & governance · E05 assimilation (ETA) process · E06 procedure-acquisition campaign | one cluster in eight places; stalled at deployment stage 1; 27K files, ≈1,780 irreplaceable ones outside git |\\n| **G03 Platform** | E07 NLT ledger · E08 next-generation design · E25 three-loop harness | ledger shelved (its public twin `nlt-ledger` has diverged); design untracked; harness lives on as a port in autosurvey |\\n| **G04 Story** | E09 ai-2026 scenario & governed-revision method | dormant since 08-17; the cleanest self-contained unit |\\n| **G05 Personal** | E24 job search & portfolio | `job/` dormant; continued in `applications/` (no git, no backup); portfolio public, unsanitised, unlicensed |\\n| **G06 Field survey** | E10 papers harvest · E11 institution/ARPI scan · E12 survey-craft package · E13 `nimoi-autosurvey` · E14 detection & ranking | one effort in five instalments across two repositories; autosurvey 54 commits unpushed; ≈5.7 GB re-fetchable |\\n| **G07 Corpus first reads** | E16 gold harvest · E17 step-1/2 surveys | completed / superseded; by NIMOI's own rule the later suites may not read them |\\n| **G08 EMI study** | E15 candidate corpus · E18 paradigm theory · E19 EMI index & suites · E20 comparison study · E26 chart & export toolchain | the live centre: loop stopped 09-13, 23 clones + 99 shortlisted repositories to go; 47% untracked |\\n| **G09 Paper & outreach** | E21 survey paper · E22 outreach & peer contact · E23 AI-organizations study | drafts v5/v6 unreconciled; what is *published* is the v3 line; replies on record, sending not |\\n\\n**The proposed scheme, in five lines** (`relationships/subprojects.md` — a proposal; it decides\\nnothing): a sub-group is *membership*, a repository is *housing*, and they need not coincide. **Stage 1\\nmoves no files**: existing top-level directories get their own git in place and the parent ignores\\nthem; the parent *is* the charter plus the shared libraries, a registry of subprojects, the map, and a\\ngitignored quarantine for the clones. Every working subproject is private; **\\\"public\\\" means a separate\\nexport repository** — which is what the three existing public siblings already are. Siblings are\\nadopted by moving the directory, never by re-cloning. Gatherings and cuts come later, one at a time,\\neach \\\"moved with receipt\\\". Two blind proposals on different models converged on this.\\n\\n## Ten things to know before re-organising\\n\\n1. **Back up, push and decide what to commit — first.** Back up both repositories *with* `.git` and\\n   ignored files. `nimoi-autosurvey` is 54 commits ahead of its remote. `applications/` and this map\\n   have no git at all. `nimoi` holds 151 MB of untracked real work (47% of the measurement record, the\\n   comparison study, the design line, most of `paper/`) and ≈1,780 irreplaceable ignored campaign\\n   files, `build/`, the ARPI run log, 679 harvest judgement files, the ledger's run evidence.\\n   → `relationships/protection_and_volume.md`\\n2. **Make new repositories from the working tree, with text conversion off; never re-clone, never\\n   filter history.** ~3,800 tracked files are CRLF on disk and LF in git, and NIMOI's checksums bind\\n   the bytes on disk. Do **not** copy `nlt-ledger`'s `.gitattributes` — it normalises to LF.\\n   `.git` also holds 12 Codex working-tree snapshots (incl. contact folders): keep them in backups,\\n   never mirror-push. → `reorg_hazards.md` H41, H74, H82, H38\\n3. **Neither `git ls-files` nor the filesystem is a safe list of \\\"the project\\\".** One omits ~2,000\\n   real files; the other includes ~40,000 ignored fixtures and downloads, ~7,000 of them verbatim,\\n   unlabelled copies of live or former project files. → `spaghetti.md` S10\\n4. **Most duplication is deliberate evidence** — portfolio freezes with hash claims, a declared mirror,\\n   mutation-test *bundles* (keep whole), a mandated harness fork, five parallel ledger implementations.\\n   Do not dedupe by name or hash. → `reorg_hazards.md` H-C\\n5. **Tools are hard-wired to where they sit.** Root tools compute paths from their own location; three\\n   read campaign files and the campaign reads `procedures/` back; all 63 per-run tools and the target\\n   picker are untracked; the comparison study holds ≈6,950 absolute links; chart builders import\\n   predecessors by path; the scanner finds the clones from the parent root (never strip a clone's\\n   `.git`). → `reorg_hazards.md` H-B, `tools_census.md`\\n6. **Three clusters are smeared, and directory names describe the first thing put there.** E04–E06 in\\n   eight places; the survey in five instalments across two repositories whose seam neither declares;\\n   paper-side work under `metrics/` and `origins/`. `candidate_analysis/` holds 8 efforts, `origins/` 5,\\n   `paper/` 4, `harvest/` 3, `hail_mary_2/` 3; the root is an unindexed bin of 11 tools and 11 scratch\\n   files. → `spaghetti.md`, `directories/INDEX.md`\\n7. **Words are overloaded** — *ledger* ×7, *harness* ×7, *procedure* ×4, *reference* ×5, *contacts* ×3,\\n   *findings* ×4 — and NIMOI's own entry points are stale: onboarding names 7 of 23 directories and\\n   omits whole built subsystems; five indexes misstate their own directory. → `naming_collisions.md`,\\n   `record_defects.md`\\n8. **Untrusted text is not confined to `candidate_repos/`.** 2,630 fetched third-party documents are\\n   git-tracked — **633 of them other projects' `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md`** — plus detection READMEs, a\\n   10.9 MB HTML, `paper/readmes/`, an external handbook. The one recorded exposure (M-6) fired on 09-10.\\n   → `reorg_hazards.md` H-E\\n9. **The institution's stated product — its failures — is not where its memory looks.** ~770 deviation\\n   and memory entries sit in run records, a campaign sandbox log, a campaign ledger and two harness\\n   memory stores *outside the repositories*, against four filed failure records and nine findings.\\n   → `efforts/E02_failure_records.md`\\n10. **Some of NIMOI is already public, and nothing inside `nimoi/` says so.** Three public repositories\\n    carry the ledger, the portfolio, and the survey with its cards, ledgers, chart, candidate list and\\n    forum; all three have diverged from their private originals in both directions. One is unsanitised\\n    and unlicensed; one was scrubbed only at its tip; one's ledgers carry third parties' email strings.\\n    **Whether the `nimoi` remote itself is public is recorded nowhere** — every publication grade in\\n    this map assumes it is private (FQ-46). → `directories/siblings.md`, `publication_blockers.md`\\n\\n## Go deeper\\n\\n| Level | What | Where |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| L1 | the 26 efforts (slim; paragraphs in `INDEX_detailed.md`) | `efforts/INDEX.md` |\\n| L1 | every directory of all six trees | `directories/INDEX.md` |\\n| L1 | relationships R01–R103 · tangles S01–S12 · hazards H01–H85 · sub-groups G01–G09 · themes T01–T12 · git state · timeline · coupling matrix · name collisions | `relationships/INDEX.md` |\\n| L1 | the founder's instructions, verbatim (D1–D6) | `method/founder_directives.md` |\\n| L2 | one file per effort, each ending in a verification ledger | `efforts/E##_*.md` |\\n| L3 | how the map was made: plans, agent reports, change logs, syntheses; tool outputs | `CONTINUE.md` → `waves/`, `evidence/` |\"\n}"}],"origin":null}}}
