{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:23:12.493Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/000854","body":{"kind":"message","agent":"owner.1.1","turn":1,"direction":"to_agent","message":{"_type":"UserMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolResultBlock","tool_use_id":"toolu_01EuxKB2TfuYgk596PUwgCGq","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n \"pattern\": \"FQ-31|FQ-37|FQ-38|FQ-14|FQ-26|FQ-42c|FQ-06|FQ-08|FQ-17|FQ-18|FQ-19|FQ-27|FQ-46|FQ-47|FQ-49|FQ-50|FQ-51|FQ-52|FQ-25\",\n \"glob\": null,\n \"matches\": [\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 6,\n   \"text\": \"**If you answer only six,** make them **FQ-46 (are the `nimoi` and autosurvey GitHub remotes private? — it gates the rest)**, FQ-17 (push autosurvey), FQ-19 (what to commit), FQ-27 / FQ-47 (what is already public), FQ-01 (is the measurement loop over), FQ-25 (who owns the shared libraries). *(FQ-46–\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 35,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-06 · Is the procedure library's stage 2 to be deployed, rolled back, or declared a finished testbed experiment?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 43,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-08 · Is ETA still the institution's process for acquiring capability, given that three major builds bypassed it?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 67,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-14 · Is the general-findings corpus abandoned, or has promoting findings into it simply never been anyone's job?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 72,\n   \"text\": \"It did not stop on 08-23 as the map said: `applications/` runs to 08-24 with a second employer and résumés to v2.5 — and it is the least-protected work in the estate (FQ-18).\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 85,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-17 · May `nimoi-autosurvey`'s 54 unpushed commits be pushed now?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 89,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-18 · May `applications/` (290 MB, 2,236 files, no git, no remote, no backup) be backed up before anything else happens?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 93,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-19 · Which untracked work gets committed before the re-org — all of it, or a named subset?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 124,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-25 · Where do the shared libraries go — the procedure library, `context/`, `from_chat/`, `references/` and the root tools — when each subproject gets its own git?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 128,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-26 · Does doctrine — `origins/`, onboarding, and the virtue register — live in the parent, or in an \\\"institution\\\" subproject of its own; and does the virtue register travel with doctrine or with the measurement suites that write to it?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 132,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-27 · The public `nimoi_samples` repository was published verbatim with no licence — sanitise it, licence it, or withdraw it?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 149,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-31 · One procedure regime for the whole family, or a federation in which each subproject keeps its own?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 179,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-37 · Which failure-record scheme wins — the warm-referenced one with no entry point, or the one with an entry point and a single record?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 183,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-38 · Are run-record deviations, the out-of-tree harness memory store, and defects found in institution-general tools part of the institution's memory — and should they be promoted into it?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 225,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-46 · Are the GitHub remotes of `nimoi` and `nimoi-autosurvey` private?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 226,\n   \"text\": \"Nothing on disk records it. Every publication grade in the map assumes they are — and FQ-19 (commit the untracked work) and FQ-17 (push autosurvey) send more material to them.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 229,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-47 · Three things already public that you may want to act on before any re-org — leave, fix, or withdraw?** (a) the public survey repository's ledgers contain about twenty email-address strings, most apparently belonging to authors of the surveyed projects; (b) `nimoi_samples` is public, unsani\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 236,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-49 · Which unit is the rehearsal — the first thing to be given its own git?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 240,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-50 · The three early-survey archives (`harvest/`, `hail_mary_2/`, `legacy_survey_material/`) — their own repositories, or left with the parent?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 244,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-51 · When `nimoi-autosurvey` is pulled in: whole, or split into its record (≈150 MB) and its re-fetchable stores (≈3.7 GB)? And are sessions working inside an adopted repository onboarded into NIMOI, or does it keep its own entry contract?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 248,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-52 · May `candidate_analysis/contacts/` (tables about named third parties) be moved out before `candidate_analysis/` gets its first commit as its own repository?**\"\n  }\n ],\n \"files_searched\": 1,\n \"files_walked\": 1,\n \"pruned\": [],\n \"truncated\": false\n}"}],"is_error":null}],"uuid":"1b1a4338-c83e-49fa-b6ad-a61aac76f969","parent_tool_use_id":null,"tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n \"pattern\": \"FQ-31|FQ-37|FQ-38|FQ-14|FQ-26|FQ-42c|FQ-06|FQ-08|FQ-17|FQ-18|FQ-19|FQ-27|FQ-46|FQ-47|FQ-49|FQ-50|FQ-51|FQ-52|FQ-25\",\n \"glob\": null,\n \"matches\": [\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 6,\n   \"text\": \"**If you answer only six,** make them **FQ-46 (are the `nimoi` and autosurvey GitHub remotes private? — it gates the rest)**, FQ-17 (push autosurvey), FQ-19 (what to commit), FQ-27 / FQ-47 (what is already public), FQ-01 (is the measurement loop over), FQ-25 (who owns the shared libraries). *(FQ-46–\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 35,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-06 · Is the procedure library's stage 2 to be deployed, rolled back, or declared a finished testbed experiment?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 43,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-08 · Is ETA still the institution's process for acquiring capability, given that three major builds bypassed it?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 67,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-14 · Is the general-findings corpus abandoned, or has promoting findings into it simply never been anyone's job?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 72,\n   \"text\": \"It did not stop on 08-23 as the map said: `applications/` runs to 08-24 with a second employer and résumés to v2.5 — and it is the least-protected work in the estate (FQ-18).\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 85,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-17 · May `nimoi-autosurvey`'s 54 unpushed commits be pushed now?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 89,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-18 · May `applications/` (290 MB, 2,236 files, no git, no remote, no backup) be backed up before anything else happens?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 93,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-19 · Which untracked work gets committed before the re-org — all of it, or a named subset?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 124,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-25 · Where do the shared libraries go — the procedure library, `context/`, `from_chat/`, `references/` and the root tools — when each subproject gets its own git?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 128,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-26 · Does doctrine — `origins/`, onboarding, and the virtue register — live in the parent, or in an \\\"institution\\\" subproject of its own; and does the virtue register travel with doctrine or with the measurement suites that write to it?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 132,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-27 · The public `nimoi_samples` repository was published verbatim with no licence — sanitise it, licence it, or withdraw it?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 149,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-31 · One procedure regime for the whole family, or a federation in which each subproject keeps its own?**\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n   \"line\": 179,\n   \"text\": \"**FQ-37 · Which failure-record scheme wins — the warm-referenced