{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:23:39.150Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/000884","tag":"agent.owner.1.1"}
{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:23:39.154Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/000885","body":{"kind":"message","agent":"owner.1.1","turn":1,"direction":"to_agent","message":{"_type":"UserMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolResultBlock","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DYNHh2f1W2w4nuxjCdMqRd","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n \"start_line\": 140,\n \"end_line\": 159,\n \"total_lines\": 272,\n \"next_offset\": 160,\n \"line_truncated\": false,\n \"sha256\": \"72ddabea99b2e1de1fb4c7c95e46399e827ae0eaca4ea06debd49108d501e2d1\",\n \"text\": \"**FQ-29 · For each of the three public repositories, which side is authoritative — the public copy or the private original?**\\nAll three have diverged both ways: the public ledger holds four documents that exist nowhere privately; the public portfolio is a *later* edition than the private one; and the public survey's 0.3→0.4 editorial pass was never brought back, while the private drafts moved on to v4–v6. Two known blemishes ride on the same answer: the published figure plots 16 of 37 cards, and one published ledger file leaks an internal clone path.\\n*Default:* **private is authoritative everywhere; public-only material is pulled back into the map as \\\"public-only, unmerged\\\"; nothing republished, nothing corrected.** · *Touches:* NLT ledger (E07), EMI suites (E19), paper (E21), charts (E26), job search (E24). · *Read:* `directories/siblings.md`\\n\\n**FQ-30 · Do the untrusted cloned repositories stay inside the working tree?**\\nYou opened this yourself in the 08-26 mistakes record and nothing has closed it; the exposure has since fired once, and the re-org is the natural moment to move them out. It is also the cheapest large excision available.\\n*Default:* **they stay where they are for now — a gitignored quarantine at the parent level, with a manifest (FQ-22) and a marker file — and moving them out is a later, separate step.** The scanner's target picker and the ARPI pipeline both find the clones from the parent root, and the picker's memory of what has been scanned depends on it; moving the clones means re-pointing both first. · *Touches:* clone corpus (E15), failure records (E02), EMI suites (E19), gold harvest (E16). · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` (the quarantine rows), `directories/candidate_repos.md`\\n*(Corrected 09-20 by the orchestrator: the first default here was \\\"they move out of the tree\\\", which contradicted both subproject proposals and the merged scheme. The question is unchanged and still yours — \\\"move them out now\\\" remains a complete answer.)*\\n\\n**FQ-31 · One procedure regime for the whole family, or a federation in which each subproject keeps its own?**\\nThree regimes already operate side by side and only one is registered anywhere; the measurement suites have effectively seceded, and the size ceilings the library imposes are not applied to them or to autosurvey's products. This is the deepest design question in the map.\\n*Default:* **federation, stated openly** — each subproject declares its own regime; the library governs only the parent. · *Touches:* procedure library (E04), EMI suites (E19), gold harvest (E16), nimoi-autosurvey (E13). · *Read:* `relationships/themes.md` §T10\\n\\n**FQ-32 · Does the re-org honour `nimoi-autosurvey`'s own rebaseline clause, waive it in writing, or exempt that repository from the re-org?**\\nBy the repository's written standard, moving an operational product requires an exact sentence from you first; ignoring it would be the one rule-break the estate documents in advance.\\n*Default:* **the repository is exempt from the re-org for now** — pulled in as a subproject unchanged, no rebaseline triggered. · *Touches:* nimoi-autosurvey (E13), three-loop harness (E25). · *Read:* `efforts/E13_nimoi_autosurvey.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-33 · Is the third-party contacts folder to be retained at all?**\\nIt is tracked and committed and holds outside people's names, employers and professional assessments gathered from public profiles, plus one drafted message; retention is a decision only you can take, and it decides whether the whole outreach line can ever be public.\\n*Default:* **retained, private, and marked as a hard publication blocker.** · *Touches:* outreach (E22), detection ranking (E14). · *Read:* `efforts/E22_outreach_peer_contact.md` §9\"\n}"}],"is_error":null}],"uuid":"0cdae848-e51d-4ca3-bd98-183b414dd4ea","parent_tool_use_id":null,"tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n \"path\": \"/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md\",\n \"start_line\": 140,\n \"end_line\": 159,\n \"total_lines\": 272,\n \"next_offset\": 160,\n \"line_truncated\": false,\n \"sha256\": \"72ddabea99b2e1de1fb4c7c95e46399e827ae0eaca4ea06debd49108d501e2d1\",\n \"text\": \"**FQ-29 · For each of the three public repositories, which side is authoritative — the public copy or the private original?**\\nAll three have diverged both ways: the public ledger holds four documents that exist nowhere privately; the public portfolio is a *later* edition than the private one; and the public survey's 0.3→0.4 editorial pass was never brought back, while the private drafts moved on to v4–v6. Two known blemishes ride on the same answer: the published figure plots 16 of 37 cards, and one published ledger file leaks an internal clone path.\\n*Default:* **private is authoritative everywhere; public-only material is pulled back into the map as \\\"public-only, unmerged\\\"; nothing republished, nothing corrected.** · *Touches:* NLT ledger (E07), EMI suites (E19), paper (E21), charts (E26), job search (E24). · *Read:* `directories/siblings.md`\\n\\n**FQ-30 · Do the untrusted cloned repositories stay inside the working tree?**\\nYou opened this yourself in the 08-26 mistakes record and nothing has closed it; the exposure has since fired once, and the re-org is the natural moment to move them out. It is also the cheapest large excision available.\\n*Default:* **they stay where they are for now — a gitignored quarantine at the parent level, with a manifest (FQ-22) and a marker file — and moving them out is a later, separate step.** The scanner's target picker and the ARPI pipeline both find the clones from the parent root, and the picker's memory of what has been scanned depends on it; moving the clones means re-pointing both first. · *Touches:* clone corpus (E15), failure records (E02), EMI suites (E19), gold harvest (E16). · *Read:* `relationships/subprojects.md` (the quarantine rows), `directories/candidate_repos.md`\\n*(Corrected 09-20 by the orchestrator: the first default here was \\\"they move out of the tree\\\", which contradicted both subproject proposals and the merged scheme. The question is unchanged and still yours — \\\"move them out now\\\" remains a complete answer.)*\\n\\n**FQ-31 · One procedure regime for the whole family, or a federation in which each subproject keeps its own?**\\nThree regimes already operate side by side and only one is registered anywhere; the measurement suites have effectively seceded, and the size ceilings the library imposes are not applied to them or to autosurvey's products. This is the deepest design question in the map.\\n*Default:* **federation, stated openly** — each subproject declares its own regime; the library governs only the parent. · *Touches:* procedure library (E04), EMI suites (E19), gold harvest (E16), nimoi-autosurvey (E13). · *Read:* `relationships/themes.md` §T10\\n\\n**FQ-32 · Does the re-org honour `nimoi-autosurvey`'s own rebaseline clause, waive it in writing, or exempt that repository from the re-org?**\\nBy the repository's written standard, moving an operational product requires an exact sentence from you first; ignoring it would be the one rule-break the estate documents in advance.\\n*Default:* **the repository is exempt from the re-org for now** — pulled in as a subproject unchanged, no rebaseline triggered. · *Touches:* nimoi-autosurvey (E13), three-loop harness (E25). · *Read:* `efforts/E13_nimoi_autosurvey.md` §9\\n\\n**FQ-33 · Is the third-party contacts folder to be retained at all?**\\nIt is tracked and committed and holds outside people's names, employers and professional assessments gathered from public profiles, plus one drafted message; retention is a decision only you can take, and it decides whether the whole outreach line can ever be public.\\n*Default:* **retained, private, and marked as a hard publication blocker.** · *Touches:* outreach (E22), detection ranking (E14). · *Read:* `efforts/E22_outreach_peer_contact.md` §9\"\n}"}],"origin":null}}}
