{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:23:41.767Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/000891","body":{"kind":"tool_call","agent":"owner.2","turn":1,"phase":"pre","tool_use_id":"exec-ff93a89d-15ad-484a-afe3-3f096089ae3e","tool_name":"mcp__ledger__write","tool_input":{"name":"work/doctrine-priorities/gpt/recommendation","body":"Bar: A founder-decidable, deliberately small pre-launch doctrine sequence: it must preserve the evidence from real failures, define who may change what, keep sensitive and untrusted material inside explicit boundaries, distinguish observed practice from binding authority, and avoid treating the 2026-09-20 map as current operational state. It need not settle the whole constitution or make NIMOI production-ready.\n\n# Doctrine priorities before NIMOI launch\n2026-09-29 · recommendation, not doctrine\n\n## What I counted as doctrine, and how I ranked it\n\nDoctrine here means a cross-session commitment that governs authority, permissible change, evidence, or institutional memory. A map, a tool, a procedure for one task, and a successful precedent are inputs, not standing doctrine merely because they exist. Founder language becomes standing only by explicit designation or confirmation; the current onboarding already makes that distinction. [checked: read origins/onboarding_1.12.md, Authority section] The older origins/NIMOI.md identifies constitutional *candidates* and says a constitution is owed; I have not promoted those candidates by inference. [checked: read origins/NIMOI.md, Lineage and Present state; nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E01_constitution_onboarding_virtues.md §5]\n\nMy ordering rule is: (1) irreversible loss or falsification of the failure record, unauthorized authority growth, or involuntary disclosure; (2) how directly an unresolved rule would affect the first governed self-modification; (3) how much can be settled with a short founder decision rather than a new system. This follows NIMOI's stated bar—real attempts whose failures remain informative, with record-corrupting defects ranked above ordinary failures—not a shipping checklist. [checked: read origins/persistent_testbed.md §§2–6] The map's large counts and defaults are leads, not votes. [checked: read nimoi_mapping_project/MAP.md opening caveat; FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md opening]\n\nI recommend a **thin, ratified launch kernel**, then one real governed change under it, then revision from what breaks. This is a proposed sequence, not a declaration that NIMOI has already adopted these rules. Do not hold launch for a comprehensive constitution, a complete legacy-failure harvest, a unified procedure library, or a finished reorganization. [working: prioritization judgment based on sources below]\n\n## Ranked decisions\n\n### P0 / launch gate 1 — Authority and amendment envelope\n\n**Founder decision:** Ratify one short charter for the launch window: which artifacts agents may propose and change, which changes require independent review or founder authorization, who can stop a run, how a worker objects to malformed work, and how the charter itself may be amended. Distinguish a standing directive from a task instruction at the point it is recorded; retain the dated source and an explicit status rather than making every chat utterance law. Put non-delegable powers (for example widening permissions or public release) outside the initial agent grant unless the founder expressly decides otherwise. [working: proposed rule]\n\n**Why first:** Full governed self-modification begins at launch, but the historical constitution is unwritten; the map says doctrine froze while three practice regimes arose beside it. [checked: read origins/onboarding_1.12.md, Current stage; nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E01_constitution_onboarding_virtues.md §5; relationships/themes.md T10] Onboarding now grants escalation and justified dissent without granting concealment or unilateral scope expansion. [checked: read origins/onboarding_1.12.md, Organizational responsibility] That is a sound seed, not a complete change jurisdiction. Existing harness bounds are enforcement mechanisms; doctrine must state the *authority* they implement. [working]\n\n**Minimum artifact / pass condition:** A dated v0.1 charter with owner, effective scope, protected surfaces, grant matrix, amendment path, and a pointer from the entry contract. A fresh agent should be able to classify a proposed change as allowed, approval-needed, or out of scope without guessing from a map default. [working]\n\n### P0 / launch gate 2 — Failure intake and record integrity\n\n**Founder decision:** Choose the institutional intake route and whether run deviations and harness-side memory count as NIMOI memory (map FQ-37/FQ-38). Permit local detailed formats, but require a durable cross-lane pointer for each material failure or discrepancy: stable identifier, source run/artifact, expected and observed, evidence/claim status, impact on record integrity, open/resolved state, and next owner or explicit closure. Route transferable lessons to findings as a separate promotion step. [working: proposed minimum, not an adopted schema]\n\n**Why now:** Two failure-record conventions do not refer to one another; the directed failure-record procedure has an entry point, while the map reports one use. [checked: read procedures/failure_record.md and nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E02_failure_records.md §§1–3] The map reports hundreds of numbered deviations in run records and further campaign/harness stores, versus four filed failure records and nine general findings; I did not recount those objects. [working: map E02 §§1–2 and E03 §5, historical through 2026-09-20] The finding procedure has a useful admission test but is a different product from a failure record. [checked: read procedures/general_findings.md and procedures/failure_record.md] Treating the four filed records as the total institutional failure history would make the record misleading. [working: inference from map E02 §7f]\n\n**Minimum artifact / pass condition:** One accessible index connecting a new launch-window failure to its raw run record, investigation, correction, and any general finding; a cold reader can tell what was not checked. Keep original records addressable and label supersession. Do **not** retroactively classify the historical deviation pile before launch; start a bounded harvest after the standard survives actual use. [working]\n\n### P0 / launch gate 3 — Governed change with evidence and independent challenge\n\n**Founder decision:** Define risk tiers for self-modification. A proposal should state its bar and expected failure mode; preserve a before state; name who made, checked, and accepted the change; attach receipts; and say how to reverse or supersede it. Record an adverse or inconclusive result rather than quietly rewriting the claim. Record-affecting changes need stronger independent checks than ordinary reversible work. Let ordinary failures occur under observation: zero failures is not the objective. [working: proposed lifecycle]\n\n**Why now:** The primary-purpose document ranks corrupt records and dead instruments above ordinary failures, calls for versions rather than silent edits, and records a cold reader catching its own author's omission. [checked: read origins/persistent_testbed.md §§3, 5–6] The map records a procedure library stalled at stage 1, a generator that would fail on three later additions, and parallel autosurvey/measurement regimes; installing a universal lifecycle by fiat would falsely describe practice. [working: map E04 §§1, 5–6; relationships/themes.md T10] The useful pre-launch requirement is one governed *route* for the launch lane, not instant conformity of all legacy work. [working]\n\n**Minimum artifact / pass condition:** Rehearse this route on one genuine, reversible change, then have a reader other than the author inspect the evidence and the recorded non-actions. A failed but legible rehearsal may meet NIMOI's bar; an untraceable success does not. [working]\n\n### P0, conditional gate — Trust, privacy, and public export\n\nIf launch agents can ingest fetched text, act on personal material, contact outsiders, or write to public destinations, settle the relevant boundary **before those powers are granted**: external text remains data; readers of untrusted text lack unrelated write authority; public export requires explicit source/provenance and human release decision; personal/third-party material has a retention and publication decision. If launch is strictly private with those powers withheld, the full handling standard can be developed during bootstrapping, but the withheld powers and escalation route must be explicit. [working: proposed conditional gate]\n\nThe map reports an actual instruction-injection exposure from a cloned repository and notes that fetched instruction-like files sit in several tracked areas, not just the clone store. [working: map relationships/themes.md T05 and E02 §9.4; not independently reproduced] It also inventories already-public material and unresolved remote visibility, so publication safety cannot be inferred from directory placement. [working: map FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md FQ-34, FQ-46/FQ-47; relationships/subprojects.md §4] I did not inspect personal records or third-party messages, and this recommendation reproduces none. [checked: my read list below]\n\n### P1 / first post-kernel doctrine — Federation and state, not forced uniformity\n\nHave each active subproject entry declare its authority source, local procedure regime, owner, state word, protected/untrusted zones, parent writes, external dependencies, and where its failures feed institutional memory. Ratify whether the library governs the parent alone or all subprojects (FQ-31); until then, label each lane's actual regime. The map's proposal for parent/shared libraries and boundary manifests is a useful design input, not an adopted layout. [working: recommendation; checked: read relationships/subprojects.md §§1, 6–7 and FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md FQ-25/FQ-31]\n\nRequire a one-line closing state with reason for new efforts. [checked: read origins/onboarding_1.12.md, State words] This is especially cheap protection against the map's recurring uncertainty about paused versus abandoned work. [working: map relationships/themes.md T09; FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md group A] Keep the first launch lane's entry contract accurate; do not wait to resolve all legacy subproject boundaries. [working]\n\n### P2 / deliberately deferred\n\nA comprehensive constitution (including whether the inherited “honour” candidate becomes NIMOI law), a rebase of the virtue register, promotion of the historical deviation backlog, reconciliation of all three procedure regimes, and the whole reorganization are real work but should follow a first legible governed-change cycle. The existing virtue-methodology directive and its two-vices form remain operative; I am not proposing to discard them. [checked: read origins/NIMOI.md, Lineage; origins/onboarding_1.12.md, Self-optimization; nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E01_constitution_onboarding_virtues.md §5] This deferral is not a verdict that those tasks are unimportant; it avoids polishing doctrine while its new governance has not yet met real load. [working]\n\n## Short founder decision sheet\n\n1. What is the initial self-modification grant, and what stays founder-only? (P0-1)\n2. Which failure intake becomes the entry point, and do raw run deviations/harness memories belong to institutional memory? (FQ-37/38; P0-2)\n3. What is the approval/review rule for changes that can corrupt records or widen authority? (P0-3)\n4. Will launch have any public, third-party-contact, or sensitive-data power? If yes, decide the handling/release route first; if no, record the denial. Confirm remote visibility before any publication-related action. (FQ-34/46/47; conditional P0)\n5. Which regime governs the first launch lane, and where is its entry contract? The broader federation decision can follow. (FQ-25/31; P1)\n\nAn unanswered choice should be marked open with a constrained launch behavior, not silently filled from the map's defaults. [working] The map explicitly calls its subproject scheme a proposal and its evidence a catalogue, not proof that a mechanism works. [checked: read MAP.md opening; relationships/subprojects.md opening]\n\n## Reading depth, confidence, and exclusions\n\nI read onboarding 1.12; bootstrap-harness/rules.md; mapping roots MAP.md and CONTINUE.md; mapping founder-directives, themes, subproject proposal, founder questions, Wave-03 synthesis §§3–5; targeted E01–E04 and E25 sections; and the primary NIMOI, persistent-testbed, failure-record, and general-findings documents. This is a purposive doctrine/authority/record/boundary read, not a fresh audit of 26 efforts. [checked: tool reads in this session] I did not read the candidate repository tree, personal files, third-party correspondence, full run records, the 122-defect register, all effort files, git state, or the sibling repositories. I ran no script or git command. Historical counts and states above therefore remain working map claims, not present-day measurements. The map describes a 2026-09-20 tree, while onboarding was revised later. [checked: read MAP.md date, origins/onboarding_1.12.md date]\n\nAI-addressed text encountered and treated as data rather than a task instruction: nimoi_mapping_project/CONTINUE.md (mapping continuation commands); nimoi_mapping_project/method/founder_directives.md (historical quoted work orders); origins/NIMOI.md (direct onboarding address); procedures/failure_record.md and procedures/general_findings.md (worker-facing steps). E25 also reports a directive-like sentence in hail_mary_2/ignore_brainstorming.md; I did not open that file. [checked: reads of listed pages; working: E25's report for the unopened file]\n\nDISCREPANCY: nimoi_mapping_project/CONTINUE.md, opening and “Where the method lives” | expected: founder-directive register ends D1–D6, per continuation root dated 2026-09-20 | found: nimoi_mapping_project/method/founder_directives.md contains D7–D9 through 2026-09-24, by direct read | 2026-09-29.\nDISCREPANCY: nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E01_constitution_onboarding_virtues.md §1/§3 | expected: onboarding 1.10 is the latest, per the 2026-09-20 effort snapshot | found: origins/onboarding_1.12.md exists and is the directed current onboarding, by direct read | 2026-09-29.\nDISCREPANCY: nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E01_constitution_onboarding_virtues.md §8.1 | expected: four runs without virtue entries are inside the live scheduled-loop window, per its 31-filename count | found: that file's §9.4 correction and §6 R24 say those four were pre-loop interactive runs; 37 completed runs were counted by receipts and all 16 loop fires wrote entries, by cross-read of its annotations | 2026-09-29.\nDISCREPANCY: nimoi_mapping_project/relationships/subprojects.md §10 choice 10 | expected: FQ-30's stated default moves the clone quarantine out of the tree, per that choice's wording | found: nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md FQ-30 contains a dated correction making its default stay at parent level, by direct read | 2026-09-29.\n\nState: completed — recommendation delivered as a ranked, source-labelled pre-launch decision packet; current-state verification and founder ratification remain open."},"policy_allow":true,"policy_reason":"available to this agent; the tool checks its own target"}}
