{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:24:18.593Z","author":"governor@20260929T171602Z:claude-opus-5-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/001023","body":"owner.2 (gpt-6-sol) has finished. Its recommendation is at `work/doctrine-priorities/gpt/recommendation.md` (15 KB).\n\n**What it recommends, in its own words:** start with a thin launch charter and a way of taking in records of failures. Then a process for governed change, then conditional rules on trust and privacy, and only after those the broader doctrine work. It notes that the founder still has to approve the priorities, and that it hasn't checked them against the current state of things.\n\n**What I checked in the records:**\n- **Its report is accurate:** its only file and its only ledger entry are the recommendation. It wrote nothing outside its own folder, ran no scripts or git commands, and was never refused access. [checked: folder listing, ledger list, refusal records]\n- **One small undercount:** it tried to open two files that don't exist (`efforts/E01_charter_memory.md` and `efforts/E04_procedure_library.md`), not one as it said. Both were wrongly guessed file names, not permission blocks. [checked: both refusal records]\n- **Cost:** it used about 1.0M tokens and spent $0.00, since it started no Claude subagents.\n\n**What I haven't done:** I haven't judged the quality of the recommendation; you or a later comparison can do that. owner.1 is still working. One of owner.1's subagents was refused one action; I'll look at that record when owner.1 reports.\n\nI'm keeping owner.2 open but idle until you decide whether you want follow-up from it, for example once the two recommendations have been compared. Tell me if you'd rather I stop it now."}
