{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:27:00.768Z","author":"harness:claude-anthropic-harness/task-7-project","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/001140","body":{"kind":"message","agent":"owner.1.1","turn":1,"direction":"from_agent","message":{"_type":"AssistantMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolUseBlock","id":"toolu_01Kqyu3ocKEuJx6STftBF83a","name":"mcp__ledger__write","input":{"name":"work/doctrine-priorities/claude/review/cold-read-1","labels":["cold-read"],"body":{"summary":"Cold read of work/doctrine-priorities/claude/recommendation (rev 20260929T171602Z:2472) by owner.1.1. Most [checked:] and [working: map ...] labels verified true against the named sources. Found 5 concrete defects (2 unsupported/wrong checked-labels, 1 wrong source-attribution on a working-label, 1 imprecise citation range, 1 internal contradiction) and 2 items I could not check because they sit outside my fs.read / ledger.read bounds.","defects":[{"n":1,"sentence":"\"It is the most-cited lesson in NIMOI's doctrine [checked: read persistent_testbed.md §6].\" (P3)","source_says":"persistent_testbed.md §6 presents the 'state the bar' lesson once, as the origin story of the file itself ('the general lesson, and it applies well beyond that campaign'). It contains no citation count and makes no comparative claim about other doctrine lessons. Nothing else in my reachable sources (onboarding_1.12.md, themes.md, MAP.md) establishes citation frequency across doctrine.","severity":"unsupported — the checked-label claims a verification the cited section does not perform. 'Most-cited' would need a count across doctrine documents, which was not done."},{"n":2,"sentence":"\"The 09-23 statement already exists verbatim and binds all agents [checked: read onboarding_1.12.md]\" (P7)","source_says":"onboarding_1.12.md quotes the founder verbatim: 'All NIMOI agents, including subagents, outside of bounded harness tests less than 100 turns, must have mechanism and license to raise issues if their task seems impossible or otherwise malformed.' The statement itself carves out bounded harness tests under 100 turns from the mandatory-license clause (their supervisors, not the participants, retain the escalation duty).","severity":"imprecise — fails the 'sentence contains all/every/only/none/never/zero' check. 'Binds all agents' overstates a statement that explicitly excepts one class of agent."},{"n":3,"sentence":"\"The map calls this 'the deepest design question' [working: map themes T10]\" (P4)","source_says":"The phrase 'This is the deepest design question in the map' is in FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md, at FQ-31 (line 150), not in relationships/themes.md. I read themes.md T10 in full; that exact phrase does not occur there (T10 does say 'this is the theme a re-org is most likely to either repair or cement', a different claim).","severity":"wrong — the working-label cites the wrong file as the source of a direct quote."},{"n":4,"sentence":"\"...its dominant writer was a scheduled loop whose instruction lived outside both repositories... 55% of it is uncommitted [working: map E01 §3, §5, §8]\" (P6)","source_says":"E01_constitution_onboarding_virtues.md: the 'instruction lived in the scheduled-task prompt, outside both repositories' fact is in §7d ('Hard-wired paths'), not §3/§5/§8. The 55%-uncommitted figure is stated in the effort's header line and in §10's verification ledger ('55.4% by bytes'), not in §3, §5 or §8. (V-1's 32 entries and the two starved axes, also in this same bullet list, ARE in §3 and §5 respectively, so the citation is partly right.)","severity":"imprecise — the facts themselves are true, but two of the bullets under this citation range are not found in the cited sections."},{"n":5,"sentence":"P7: \"The 09-23 statement already exists verbatim and binds all agents\" vs. P1: \"The founder confirms which existing directives are standing: at least the 08-17 virtue directive, the 08-23 testbed statement, the 09-23 organizational-responsibility statement, and the 09-24 claims and discrepancy conventions.\"","source_says":"Onboarding 1.12's own rule ('Authority' section): 'a directive is standing only when the founder says so, or confirms it when asked; everything else is a task instruction.' Nothing in onboarding_1.12.md records the founder confirming the 09-23 statement as standing.","severity":"imprecise / internal contradiction — the draft's own P1 treats the 09-23 statement's standing-vs-task-instruction status as an open question needing founder confirmation, then P7 asserts it 'already... binds all agents' as settled. This is check #4/#5 territory: a founder statement's authority is being read two different ways in the same document."}],"could_not_check":[{"item":"Discrepancy-2: \"[checked: fs list /bootstrap-harness]\" — 'the directory holds 6 (claude-openai-harness and gpt-openai-harness are not listed)'","why":"My fs.read scope is /bootstrap-harness/rules.md only, not a directory listing of /bootstrap-harness (attempting mcp__fs__list on /bootstrap-harness was refused: 'outside this agent's fs.read'). I confirmed rules.md's Swimlanes section lists exactly 4 directories (gpt-codex-harness, gpt-anthropic-harness, claude-codex-harness, claude-anthropic-harness) — the '4 listed' half of the claim is correct. I could not confirm or refute that 6 actually exist on disk.","note":"Worth flagging to the founder regardless: rules.md's own naming rule defines only two second-path-elements, 'anthropic' and 'codex' — no 'openai'. The two allegedly-missing directories ('claude-openai-harness', 'gpt-openai-harness') don't fit the architecture taxonomy rules.md itself defines. If they exist, that's itself worth a discrepancy note; if they don't, the draft's discrepancy is wrong. Either way this needs someone with /bootstrap-harness list access."},{"item":"P3: \"The founder's 2026-09-29 rule says the governor sets rules and not the bar, and the task owner sets its own bar. The harness refuses Bar: lines in assignments (per my assignment). The governor has already recorded this as a discrepancy (per my assignment; I did not read that record).\"","why":"This rests on gov/assignments/doctrine-priorities-claude and a governor discrepancy record, neither under my ledger.read scope (work/doctrine-priorities/claude only). I confirmed by mcp__ledger__list that no such record exists under my readable prefix. Could not verify the quoted rule or the claimed conflict independently — the drafter (owner.1) is the only one who read the assignment directly, and says so."}],"checked_and_confirmed_correct":["P1: 8-hour override-clause window (onboarding 1.04→1.05) — matches E01 §4 timeline exactly.","P1: 23-minute failure-record pointer (1.09→1.10), 'orphaned at birth' — matches E01 §4 and E02 §3 verbatim.","P1/P2/P4/P5/P6/P7: all [checked: read onboarding_1.12.md] labels re-read against onboarding_1.12.md and found accurate, except defect #2 above.","P2: '~770 deviation and memory entries... four filed failure records and nine findings' — matches MAP.md item 9 verbatim.","P2: two failure-record schemes 'never mention each other' — matches E02 §3 ('The two schemes do not know about each other... ✔').","P2: Claude-only memory store unreachable by GPT — matches E02 R43 verbatim.","P4: 'three unconnected procedure regimes... cites the library once in 3,294 files' — matches themes.md T10 verbatim.","P4/P5: rules.md 'No agent may modify this file under any conditions' and notebook.md 'conventions, not rules' — both verbatim quotes confirmed.","P5: 'human owns git in this phase' — confirmed in both onboarding_1.12.md and rules.md.","P6: V-1 has 32 entries; two axes (insistence, correction-response) fed nothing since 08-23 — matches E01 §3.","P6: virtues.md is 42,496 bytes — confirmed live via fs.list of /origins (2026-09-29) AND matches E01's historical record of the same figure; a genuinely well-checked claim.","P8: 'constitution owed and unwritten', virtue_methodology.md self-labelled PRECURSOR — matches E01 §5 and virtue_methodology.md's own header verbatim.","Discrepancy-1 (CONTINUE.md/MAP.md still say D1–D6 while founder_directives.md holds D7–D9) — fully confirmed by reading all three files.","Discrepancy-3 (notebook.md 'Current state (2026-09-24)' heading over two 2026-09-25-dated bullets with test counts of nine and seven) — fully confirmed.","No personal or third-party data is quoted anywhere in the draft (FQ-27/FQ-47 email-string exposures are referenced by ID only, not quoted).","No sentence with never/every/only/none/zero/all was found false except defect #2; others (e.g. 'no autonomous publication is possible today', 'the human owns git') check out against rules.md and onboarding."],"what_i_read":["/origins/onboarding_1.12.md (full, required before any other tool)","/origins/persistent_testbed.md (full)","/origins/virtue_methodology.md (full)","/origins listing (for virtues.md's current byte size)","/bootstrap-ledger/notebook.md (full)","/bootstrap-harness/rules.md (full)","/nimoi_mapping_project/MAP.md (full)","/nimoi_mapping_project/CONTINUE.md (full)","/nimoi_mapping_project/relationships/themes.md (full)","/nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E01_constitution_onboarding_virtues.md (full)","/nimoi_mapping_project/efforts/E02_failure_records.md (full)","/nimoi_mapping_project/method/founder_directives.md (full, D1–D9)","/nimoi_mapping_project/FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md (targeted: FQ-06,08,14,17,18,19,25,26,27,29,30,31,32,33,37,38,41,42,43,46,47,49,50,51,52)"],"what_i_did_not_reach":["/bootstrap-harness directory listing (only rules.md is in my fs.read scope) — could not verify Discrepancy-2's swimlane-directory count.","gov/assignments/doctrine-priorities-claude and any governor discrepancy record about the bar — outside my ledger.read scope (work/doctrine-priorities/claude only); confirmed via mcp__ledger__list that nothing else exists under that prefix.","E03–E26 effort files (the drafter also says it relied on map summaries for these; I did not independently re-check them).","relationships/record_defects.md, publication_blockers.md, subprojects.md, reorg_hazards.md, effort_graph.md — not needed for the labels I was checking, not read.","/candidate_repos — correctly never entered, per instructions.","Any git state — no exec scope; not attempted."]}}}],"model":"claude-sonnet-5","parent_tool_use_id":null,"error":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13450,"cache_read_input_tokens":100297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13450},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"message_id":"msg_011CfY81x1FdrZL9vJjXjNoQ","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"15494310-fed3-484b-a052-b3904801fe1a","uuid":"22318079-2e5b-4112-a9c5-e4c95c723659"}}}
