{"ts":"2026-09-29T17:27:17.181Z","author":"owner.1.1@20260929T171602Z:claude-sonnet-5@claude-anthropic-harness","name":"log/20260929T171602Z/001147","body":"## Result\n\nCold read written to `work/doctrine-priorities/claude/review/cold-read-1` (rev `20260929T171602Z:4593`).\n\n**Defects found (5), each tied to a quoted sentence + source:**\n\n1. **Unsupported** — P3's \"It is the most-cited lesson in NIMOI's doctrine `[checked: read persistent_testbed.md §6]`.\" §6 tells the origin story of \"state the bar\" once; it establishes no citation count across doctrine. The checked-label claims a verification that wasn't done.\n2. **Imprecise** — P7's \"The 09-23 statement already exists verbatim and binds all agents `[checked: ...]`.\" The founder's verbatim quote itself carves out \"bounded harness tests less than 100 turns\" — it doesn't bind literally all agents.\n3. **Wrong (source misattributed)** — P4's `[working: map themes T10]` for the quote \"the deepest design question.\" That exact phrase is in `FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md` (FQ-31), not in `themes.md`, which I read in full.\n4. **Imprecise** — P6's `[working: map E01 §3, §5, §8]` for \"dominant writer was a scheduled loop... outside both repositories\" and \"55% uncommitted.\" Those two facts are in E01 §7d and §10 respectively, not §3/§5/§8 (other bullets in the same list are correctly in §3/§5).\n5. **Internal contradiction** — P1 lists the 09-23 organizational-responsibility statement as needing founder confirmation to become \"standing,\" per onboarding's own standing-vs-task-instruction rule; P7 then asserts it \"already... binds all agents\" as settled. The draft treats the same statement's authority two different ways.\n\n**Could not check** (bounds narrower than the draft's sources, as expected): the actual `/bootstrap-harness` directory listing (only `rules.md` is in my `fs.read`, so I couldn't confirm Discrepancy-2's \"holds 6\" claim — I did confirm rules.md lists exactly 4, and flagged that the two allegedly-missing dirs use an \"openai\" naming pattern rules.md's own taxonomy never defines); and `gov/assignments/doctrine-priorities-claude` plus any governor discrepancy record cited in P3, which sit outside my `ledger.read` scope (`work/doctrine-priorities/claude` only) — confirmed via `ledger.list` that nothing else exists there.\n\n**Confirmed correct** (extensive): all record-integrity figures (770 deviations/4 records/9 findings, two schemes never mentioning each other, Claude-only memory store, 3,294-file citation, virtues.md's 42,496 bytes both live and historical, V-1's 32 entries, the two starved axes, the 8-hour override clause, the 23-minute pointer, both CONTINUE.md/rules.md/notebook.md discrepancies, no personal data quoted). No misquotes of founder words found elsewhere.\n\n## Observations on harness/tools\n\n- **Onboarding-first gate worked as described**: only `mcp__fs__read` on the onboarding file was available until I'd read it fully; no other tool was offered or attempted before that.\n- **Bounds enforcement was exact and correctly narrower than the draft's own sources**, as the task predicted: `mcp__fs__list` on `/bootstrap-harness` was refused with a precise message (\"outside this agent's fs.read (/origins /nimoi_mapping_project /bootstrap-ledger/notebook.md /bootstrap-harness/rules.md)\") — the single-file carve-out for `rules.md` is real and distinct from the directory.\n- **`ledger.read` scope was tight and correctly prevented me from reaching the governor's assignment/discrepancy record** the draft leans on in P3; `mcp__ledger__list` on my one allowed prefix confirmed nothing else was reachable there — useful for reporting \"could not check\" precisely rather than guessing.\n- **No malformed or surprising tool behavior**; `mcp__fs__read`'s line-offset/next_offset pagination and sha256 worked cleanly on every file, including the larger effort files (E01/E02, 250–280 lines). `mcp__fs__search` correctly reported pruned/searched counts and found exact-phrase matches efficiently (used to catch defect #3).\n- I have no `fs.exec` or subagent tools in this harness instance (consistent with bounds: no `fs.exec` line, and depth-2 subagents can't spawn further); I did not attempt either, per instructions."}
